10.1126_science.1127333.md,Third Party Punishment Game (3PPG) – all populations with 3PPG,"Single standardized 3PPG protocol described, run in each population except Dolgan/Nganasan; no internal treatment variants mentioned.",0.8,Stake size fixed at 1 day’s local wage; Player 1 allocation to Player 2 (0–100% of stake); Player 3 strategy-method choice to punish or not for each possible allocation.,"3PPG description specifies stake level, Player 1’s allocation decision, and Player 3’s punishment decisions across all possible offers.",0.9,True,Behavioral experiment with human adults across multiple societies.,1,True,"Controlled, incentivized game with specified rules and random matching.",1,False,"Described as field experiments in natural community settings, not lab sessions.",0.95,False,All data come from human play; no numerical simulations reported.,1,False,"Study reports empirical regressions, not an analytical game-theoretic derivation as the primary result.",1,3,"3PPG defined with Player 1, passive Player 2, and punishing third party (Player 3).",1,1,Described as a one-shot anonymous game with no repeat interaction.,1,1,Player 1 chooses how much of the stake to give; example uses 10% but no indication of all-or-nothing restriction.,0.7,0,Entire stake initially held by Player 1 to allocate; 0 proportion is initially in a shared/public account.,0.6,N/A,Not a linear public goods or contribution game; MPCR not defined.,1,0,Interactions are anonymous and protocols restrict talking about the game; no communication channel introduced.,0.9,0,Paper does not report participants seeing others’ earnings or punishment histories; only own triad outcomes.,0.7,0,Game described as anonymous; Player 1 does not know identity of the punisher in a socially meaningful way.,0.9,0,No costly reward mechanism; only punishment by Player 3.,1,1,Game is explicitly one-shot; participants know there will be a single decision.,0.8,1,Player 3 can pay 10% of the stake to impose a 30% stake deduction on Player 1.,1,0.1,Text: Player 3 ‘decide whether to pay 10% of the stake (20% of his or her allocation) to punish player 1’. Cost per punishment act is 10% of the stake.,1,0.3,Paying 10% of stake causes a 30% stake deduction to Player 1; hence 0.3 stake reduction per punishment act.,1,0,Design only allows costly punishment; no option to pay to increase others’ payoffs.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in this game.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in this game.,1,1,Stake standardization: ‘two players are allotted a sum of real money (the stake) … stake of each game to 1 day’s wage’; recorded as 1 stake unit.,0.9,N/R,"Not a public good; Player 1’s allocation is a transfer, not a contribution rate in a social dilemma sense; no normalized rate reported.",1,N/R,"Paper discusses mean offers qualitatively and in figures, but does not give a single numeric amount per condition.",0.2,N/R,No explicit efficiency (total payoff / maximum possible) is reported for the 3PPG.,0.2,N/R,Only illustrative payoff examples are given; no aggregate group payoff figures per population.,0.2,"Multiple (same set of field sites as UG, except Dolgan/Nganasan did not play 3PPG)",Text notes: ‘The Dolgan/Nganasan did not play the 3PPG’; otherwise same populations; specific countries listed in Table 1.,0.9,Adults (exact age range N/R),Same sampling frame of adults; no additional age detail for 3PPG.,0.8,Mixed (both sexes; exact proportions N/R),Sex used as a predictor in regressions analyzing MAO-3PP; implies inclusion of both genders.,0.8,Varied; includes students (Emory) and nonstudents with differing education levels,Same heterogeneous populations as UG; education included in regressions but details N/R.,0.7,Field experiment,3PPG conducted as part of the same round of ‘field experiments’ as UG and DG.,0.95,"Third-party punishment game: Stake = 1 day’s wage; Player 1 decides how much of the stake to give to Player 2 (who is passive). Player 3 receives half the stake and, before knowing the actual offer, specifies for each possible offer whether to pay 10% of the stake to punish Player 1, imposing a 30% stake deduction on Player 1. One-shot anonymous triad.",Directly summarized from description of the 3PPG in the paper.,1
