itions.,0.5,N/R,Discussion mentions average group payoff qualitatively but no explicit ratio of realized payoff to maximum possible is reported.,0.4,N/R,No explicit numerical group payoff values for this parameterization; only comparative statements that Shunner yields higher group payoff than Defector.,0.4,N/A,No human participants; evolutionary simulation only.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely theoretical/evolutionary model with no empirical subjects.,1,"Two-stage interaction per generation: (1) one-shot collective action in groups of size n where contributors pay cost C to create benefit B for each of the n−1 others; (2) repeated mutual aid (indirect reciprocity) game with continuation probability w, where in each period one individual per group is needy and others may help at cost c conferring benefit b, reputations track standing and are shared perfectly; three heritable strategies (Defector, Cooperator, Shunner) determine contributions and helping rules; implementation errors with probability e prevent intended help; evolutionary dynamics follow payoffs over both stages with reproduction proportional to payoff.",Summarizes the described structure of the collective action and mutual aid games and strategy definitions associated with this parameterization.,1
