,0.6,N/R,"Panel reports threshold p* for strategy dominance, not contributions.",0.5,N/R,No quantitative contributions provided.,0.5,N/R,"Discussion notes that when condition (1) is satisfied and B>C, Shunner has a larger basin of attraction, implying higher group payoff, but no explicit efficiency values plotted.",0.4,N/R,"Group payoff is compared qualitatively, not numerically.",0.4,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Theoretical analysis.,1,"Same two-stage collective action plus mutual aid game. Figure 3a examines, for various assortment levels r and mutual aid lengths 1/(1−w), the threshold initial frequency p* above which Shunners increase when competing solely with Defectors. Shunner cannot coexist with Defector in stable polymorphism. Parameter values: b=2, c=1, C=1, B=10, n=30, e=0.01.",Condenses description associated with Fig. 3a.,1
