10.1126_science.1177418.md,PN – punishment only targeted interaction,"Described as 'first treatment (""PN"", 10 groups) subjects can punish or do nothing'.",1,Targeted interaction option: punishment or non-action after public goods stage,PN differs from other treatments by offering only punishment as targeted action.,1,True,Human participants in lab study.,1,True,Randomly assigned groups and treatments in controlled setting.,1,True,Conducted at Harvard Business School computer lab.,1,False,No simulation model described.,1,False,No analytical derivations central to design.,1,4,Subjects 'interacted ... in groups of four' across all treatments.,1,50,"Figures show 'over 50 rounds of play' for PN, RN, RNP.",0.9,1,Same public goods structure as control; contribution between 0 and 20 MUs.,0.9,0,Endowment given privately each round; no automatic public allocation.,0.9,0.4,Same PG technology: contributions multiplied by 1.6 and split among 4.,1,0,No mention of communication; standard design implies no chat.,0.8,1,"To target punishment, subjects must observe each group member's contribution/outcome; not numerically specified.",0.6,1,"Paper emphasizes 'truly repeated games, where player identities persist from round to round' and non-anonymous targeted interactions; implies punishees know who punished them.",0.8,N/A,No reward option in PN treatment.,1,0,Subjects 'are not told the total number of rounds' in the experiment.,1,1,In PN 'subjects can punish or do nothing' after each PG round.,1,N/R,Cost per unit of punishment not specified in main text.,0,N/R,Magnitude of loss to target per punishment unit not specified in main text.,0,0,Treatment allows only punishment or non-action.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Same PG structure: 20 MUs per round.,1,N/R,Only qualitative statements and figures; no numeric averages reported.,0,N/R,Mean contributions per round shown graphically; no explicit numbers.,0,N/R,"Percentage of maximum payoff plotted, but not s