10.1038_nature01474.md,"Experiment 1 – Incentive condition, no fine chosen","First experiment’s incentive condition subset where investors chose not to impose the fine; corresponds to 'Incentive condition, no fine chosen' in Table 1.",1,Sanction availability and choice: fine option available but investor voluntarily refrains from imposing a 4 MU fine; Game: trust game with sanction option; investor chooses no fine.,"Independent variable is investor’s use of sanction given availability; here, investors select the 'no deduction' option.",1,True,Human participants in incentivized decision-making.,1,True,Controlled manipulation of fine choice; random anonymous pairings.,1,True,"On-site, controlled environment using booths at the university.",0.9,False,No non-human simulation.,1,False,No purely analytical component.,1,2,Investor–trustee dyads.,1,1,One-shot game.,1,1,Continuous choice of transfer and back-transfer within allowed ranges.,1,0,Endowment starts entirely in investor’s private account.,1,N/R,Not a standard public goods MPCR case; no MPCR reported.,0,0,"No communication described; anonymous, form-based decisions.",0.9,0,No data on others’ earnings or sanctions shown; only matched partner’s decisions.,0.9,0,Anonymity preserved; no identities linked to hypothetical sanctions.,0.9,0,"No explicit reward mechanism, and player identities are anonymous.",0.9,0,One-shot; no interface or rounds information mentioned.,0.9,1,"Institution allows a deduction of 4 MUs, even though here the investor chooses not to use it.",1,0,"If used, the deduction would only reduce trustee’s payoff; cost to investor is 0. In this subset, punishment is not implemented but technology is the same.",1,4,"Sanction technology, if chosen, deducts 4 MUs from trustee’s payoff for insufficient back-transfer.",0.7,0,No separate reward technology exists; only standard back-transfer.,1,N/A,No explicit reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No explicit reward mechanism.,1,10,Both roles receive 10 MUs; same across all conditions.,1,0.87,Average investment is 8.7 MUs out of 10 MUs (Table 1): 8.7 / 10 = 0.87.,1,8.7,"Table 1 'Investment' for 'Incentive condition, no fine chosen' reports 8.7 MUs.",1,N/R,No aggregate efficiency measure toward maximum possible payoffs reported for this subset.,0.2,N/R,"Table 1 reports average payoffs per role (investor 13.8, trustee 23.5), but not labeled as group payoff; sum could be computed but is not an explicit DV.",0.6,Germany,Same Bonn student subject pool.,1,N/R,No ages reported.,0.2,N/R,No gender information provided.,0,University students (various disciplines),Recruited in university lunch room from student population.,1,On site,Physical experiment at University of Bonn lunch room.,1,"Same trust game with potential fine as in incentive condition overall: investor selects transfer and desired back-transfer and a fine option, but in this subset the investor chooses 'no deduction'. Trustee knows that no fine will be imposed regardless of actual back-transfer chosen.",Describes the subset where investors voluntarily waive the sanction despite its availability.,1
