10.1017_s0140525x11002202.md,No discrete experiments with human participants (review/theoretical paper),"The paper is a theoretical and review article; it summarizes many other authors' experiments but does not report any new, original experimental, simulation, or observational study with its own methods or results.",1,N/A,No original experiments or conditions are introduced; only prior literature is reviewed.,1,False,The authors conduct no new empirical study with human participants; they only discuss others' empirical work and develop a theoretical account.,1,False,"No experimental design, procedures, or original data collection are described.",1,False,There is no lab or field experiment conducted by the authors.,1,False,"Although the text mentions that other authors use numerical simulations, this article itself does not present any new simulation model or results.",1,True,"The core contribution is a formal/theoretical account of morality evolution by partner choice, integrating prior analytical and simulation work; no new data are collected.",1,0,No original game or experiment is run; player counts only appear when summarizing external studies.,1,0,No iterative game is implemented by the authors; rounds are only described in cited work.,1,0,Not applicable because no new game is implemented; coding as 0 by convention and treating as not applicable elsewhere.,0.5,N/A,No human subjects or baseline endowments in an original task.,1,N/R,No MPCR is defined for any original public goods game; specific MPCRs in cited papers are not systematically reported.,1,N/A,No experimental interaction among participants is implemented.,1,N/A,No experimental interface is used.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism is implemented within a new experiment.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in an original design.,1,N/A,"No rounds or horizon are presented to participants, because there are no participants.",1,0,"The article discusses punishment conceptually and in others' experiments, but does not implement any punishment option itself.",1,N/A,"No original punishment mechanism, so no cost parameter.",1,N/A,No original mapping from punishment points to losses is defined.,1,0,The paper does not introduce a reward mechanism in a new experiment.,1,N/A,No original reward option is present.,1,N/A,No original mapping from reward points to gains.,1,0,"No new dictator, ultimatum, trust, or public-goods games are run by the authors; endowments are only mentioned when describing previous studies.",1,N/A,No dependent variables are measured in this article.,1,N/A,The paper does not collect behavioral data on contributions.,1,N/R,"No experimental outcomes are computed, so efficiency is not defined.",1,N/A,No groups of participants are formed and no payoffs are realized.,1,N/A,No human participants are recruited for an original study.,1,N/A,No sample is described beyond references to other authors' experiments.,1,N/A,No demographic composition for a new study is provided.,1,N/A,No original participant pool is defined.,1,No human,"The contribution is purely theoretical/analytical and literature review; there is no empirical environment (online, lab, field) for a new study.",1,"This article is a theoretical and integrative review about the evolution of fairness via partner choice, using existing evidence from dictator, ultimatum, trust, and public goods games, hunter-gatherer ethnography, and formal models; it does not introduce new game structures or conditions.","Summary based on the abstract, section 2 (formal/evolutionary argument), and section 3 (review of prior economic games).",1
