10.1111_j.1465-7295.2007.00051.x.md,"Sanction & Reward – Sequence II (Rounds 11–20), neutral framing","Additional ‘RSN’ sanction&reward sessions (RSN1–RSN6) using neutral language instead of ‘sanction/reward’, as per footnote 30.",0.9,Institution: VCM with Stage 2 allowing both increasing and decreasing others’ earnings (functionally rewards and sanctions); 10-round Sequence II; neutral framing (no ‘sanction/reward’ labels).,Footnote 30: ‘two additional sessions... of our sanction&reward treatment’ with wording changed to ‘decrease or increase others’ earnings’.,0.9,True,Experimental sessions with human subjects.,1,True,Controlled manipulation of framing while holding institution constant.,1,True,Same lab facility and procedures.,1,False,"Data from people, not agents.",1,False,No analytical model only.,1,4,Two additional sessions with three 4-person groups each (RSN1–RSN6).,1,10,Neutral-language sessions are modifications of sanction&reward treatment with 10-round Sequence II.,0.9,1,Token allocations remain flexible 0–6.,1,0,Same VCM structure.,1,0.8333,Payoff technology unchanged.,1,0,No mention of allowing communication; follows original protocol.,1,1,History and feedback features unchanged; only wording modified.,0.9,0,"Mechanism identical to sanction&reward: subjects only see total decreases received, not who imposed them.",0.9,0,Same anonymity for increases in earnings.,0.9,1,Subjects were informed of the full experimental protocol; adaptation likely preserved this feature.,0.9,1,Functional ability to decrease others’ earnings acts as sanctions.,1,1,Each decrease-token costs the chooser one token (10 cents) in private payoff.,1,1,Each decrease-token reduces another’s earnings by 10 cents.,1,1,Functional ability to increase others’ earnings acts as rewards.,1,1,Each increase-token costs one token in private account.,1,1,Each increase-token adds 10 cents to recipient.,1,6,Six tokens Stage 1 as in all treatments.,1,N/R,"Appendix B lists RSN groups, but ‘Sequence I