.,1,N/A,,0,0,Not applicable; no specific experiment from this paper is being coded.,1,0,"Within this article, no new game with a punishment stage is actually run; punishment is discussed only conceptually and via reviews.",1,N/A,No concrete parameterization of punishment per experimental condition is given by the author.,1,N/A,No new punishment technology (mapping from cost to fine) is specified for an original study.,1,0,The article does not implement or parameterize any reward mechanisms; it only cites others’ work.,1,N/A,No original reward scheme is part of a concrete experiment here.,1,N/A,No new reward technology is described for a coded condition.,1,0,"While examples like '10 dollars in the Ultimatum Game' are mentioned, they are illustrative of prior work and not part of a specific new experiment with full design details.",1,N/R,No numeric contribution rates for any particular experimental condition are reported with enough context to be coded.,1,N/R,"The paper reports only very high-level patterns (e.g., increased cooperation) from other studies; no specific means or distributions are given.",1,N/R,"Although the author discusses whether punishment improves aggregate payoffs in various studies, precise efficiency values for a single specified condition are not reported.",1,N/R,"No detailed payoff statistics (means, variances) for a particular new experiment are presented.",1,N/R,No original sample is recruited; external studies span multiple countries but no one dataset is fully specified.,1,N/R,The article does not report age ranges or distributions for any sample.,1,N/R,No gender composition is provided.,1,N/R,"The author only notes in passing that much work uses university undergraduates or small-scale societies, but provides no detailed educational breakdown.",1,No human,No new human-subject experiment is conducted; the paper is a theoretical and review article.,1,N/R,"While many game structures (Prisoner’s Dilemma, Ultimatum Game, public goods with punishment) are discussed at a high level, no single condition has all its parameters sufficiently reported to treat it as a coded experiment.",1
