ersity undergraduates in Germany.,1,N/R,Age not provided.,0.4,N/R,No mention of gender.,0.1,Undergraduate university students,Participants were undergraduates.,1,On site,Conducted with students present in a lab setting at Hamburg University.,1,"Same structure as other climate public goods conditions: climate game alternates with indirect reciprocity game; in nonanonymous rounds, contributions are recorded under stable pseudonyms that also display prior indirect reciprocity and nonanonymous climate decisions, allowing reputations to form.",Summarized from Methods and Results sections on reputational information.,1
