10.1126_science.1183532.md,NCP-only periods (neither communication nor punishment),"Condition in which neither communication nor costly punishment is allowed (NCP), as described when groups experience three consecutive NCP periods.",0.9,"Institutional condition: no communication, no punishment (NCP); order varies across treatments but condition itself has neither communication nor punishment.",Independent variable is the presence/absence of communication and costly punishment. This row isolates periods with NCP.,0.9,True,Human participants in laboratory experiments are explicitly described (165 persons in 33 groups).,1,True,The study manipulates communication and punishment conditions in a controlled lab setting.,1,True,Conducted in an experimental laboratory (Interdisciplinary Experimental Laboratory at Indiana University).,1,False,"Although a computer-simulated resource is used, human subjects make decisions; not a pure simulation study.",1,False,No formal analytical model is the primary method; focus is on experiments.,1,5,Each experiment has a group of five participants harvesting from the resource.,1,3,Each condition block consists of three consecutive 4‑min periods; here considering the three NCP periods when that condition applies.,0.9,1,Participants move in real time and can collect individual tokens repeatedly; contribution/harvest is not an all-or-nothing binary choice.,0.9,0,There is no initial contribution to a public fund; all tokens are on the resource grid and must be actively harvested to become private payoffs.,0.8,N/R,"This is a spatial renewable resource harvesting game, not a linear public goods game; no MPCR is defined or derivable as a single value.",0.2,0,NCP is defined as 'neither communication nor costly punishment is allowed'.,1,0,Paper does not report feedback of others’ earnings or punishment summaries; only describes visual avatars and tokens.,0.3,0,"No punishment option exists in NCP periods, so no punisher identity is displayed.",1,0,N