10.1073_pnas.1421402112.md,N/A – purely theoretical/review paper (no distinct experimental or simulation conditions),"The article is a conceptual and theoretical review on major evolutionary transitions; it summarizes prior empirical and theoretical work but does not introduce new experiments, simulations, or observational datasets with defined conditions.",1,N/A,"No new experiment, simulation, or observational condition is implemented; variables are discussed conceptually (e.g., relatedness, sanctions) but not manipulated in a reported study.",1,False,The paper does not collect or analyze new data with human or nonhuman subjects; it is a synthesis of existing literature and theory.,1,False,No controlled experimental design with treatments and controls is reported; only prior studies are cited.,1,False,There is no lab or field experiment conducted by the authors; all empirical work mentioned is from other sources.,1,False,No new numerical or computer simulations are presented; theoretical points are made verbally and via conceptual figures.,1,True,"The article develops and discusses formal evolutionary concepts (e.g., Hamilton’s rule, inclusive fitness, group-formation conditions) but without explicit new mathematical derivations; still, the core contribution is analytical/theoretical rather than empirical.",0.8,0,No game-theoretic or experimental interaction with defined players is implemented; set to 0 as not applicable.,1,0,No repeated-game or round-based design is reported.,1,0,No contribution game with discrete vs. continuous choices is implemented; defaulted to 0 and treated as not applicable.,1,N/A,No endowment or contribution structure involving human or artificial players is described.,1,N/R,"No public-goods or linear contribution game is specified, so a marginal per capita return cannot be defined.",1,0,No communication treatment or chat option is part of an experimental design; not applicable.,1,0,No experimental feedback or summary screens are involved.,