10.1111_j.1467-9442.2006.00444.x.md,"MildEnd – endogenous, mild law accepted by majority vote",Endogenous second-stage condition where mild law is accepted by referendum; label defined in design section.,1,Sanction regime and enactment: mild law (s = 4) endogenously chosen via majority vote; this row covers contribution decisions in groups where the referendum outcome is to enact mild law (MildEnd).,Independent variables are sanction level (4) and outcome of endogenous voting (law accepted).,1,True,Human subjects vote and then choose contributions under the resulting legal regime.,1,True,Laboratory experiment with two-stage game and strategy method.,1,True,Conducted in lecture hall sessions at University of St. Gallen.,1,False,No simulation; behavior from human participants.,1,False,"This row pertains to experimental results, not purely analytical model.",1,3,Group size n=3 in all treatments.,1,1,Subjects play the underlying contribution game only once; strategy method used to elicit contingent plans but still one-shot.,1,1,"Contributions can vary between 0 and 20 points, not restricted to all-or-nothing.",1,0,Endowment starts fully in private account and is then allocated.,1,0.5,Same linear public good parameters: marginal return from public good a=0.5.,0.7,0,No communication or face-to-face discussion reported; only anonymous voting and decisions.,1,0,Subjects not informed about referendum or contribution outcomes before end of experiment; no summaries during play.,0.9,0,Sanctions are automatic monetary deductions; participants remain anonymous; no identification of punishers or punished.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism implemented.,1,1,One-shot nature and game structure known to subjects.,1,1,Law prescribes full contribution and sanctions free-riding with s=4 in mild law conditions.,1,1,Sanction is implemented as direct deduction; each sanction point reduces payoff one-for-one.,0.6,1,One point of sanction causes one point decrease in payoff.,0.6,0,There are no positive