10.1073_pnas.0808450106.md,"Simulation – Voluntary public goods with loners, C, D, and L","Fig. 2C and text describe voluntary public goods game with loners (L) without punishment; strategies C, D, L.",1,"Game type: voluntary public goods; Strategy set: {C, D, L}; Mutation rate μ varied","Condition characterized by optional participation via loners, no punishment, μ varied.",1,False,Modeling study; references behavioral experiments but does not run them here.,1,False,No direct experimentation with human subjects reported.,1,False,No lab described.,1,True,They state that symbols in Fig. 2 come from individual-based simulations for this game as well.,1,True,"They analyze this case using Markov chains for small μ and Fokker-Planck for large μ, especially the small-μ stationary distribution (50% L, 25% C, 25% D).",1,5,Same N=5 parameter set used for all Fig. 2 simulations.,1,1,Evolutionary process with repeated group formation; one interaction per update.,0.3,1,"Players either participate as cooperator (pay c), defect (pay 0), or abstain as loner; no partial contributions discussed.",0.7,N/A,No explicit endowment or UI for human decision; pure strategy model.,1,0.6,"Same public goods parameters: N=5, r=3.",1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No UI.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,0,This scenario is ‘voluntary public goods games without punishment’.,1,N/A,No punishment.,1,N/A,No punishment.,1,0,No reward option in model.,1,N/A,No reward.,1,N/A,No reward.,1,N/R,Only cost c=1 and loner payoff σ=1 specified; endowment not explicitly given.,0.2,N/R,"They present stationary fractions of C, D, L but not an explicit normalized contribution rate; could be inferred but not reported.",0.5,N/R,No numeric average contribution amounts reported.,0.2,N/R,Discussion of payoffs is qualitative; no normalized efficiency values are shown.,0.2,N/R,No numeric group payoff statistics provided.,0.2,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participa