 not reported separately from raw point contributions.,0,8.3,Reported: “In the condition without punishment… laboratory (8.30).” This is average contribution per person per period.,1,N/R,No explicit ratio of actual to maximum group payoff reported for this specific condition and sample.,0,N/R,Only individual contributions reported; earnings by condition and sample not broken out.,0,USA,Lab sessions conducted at Harvard and Yale in the USA; participants are students there.,0.9,Mean 25.2 years (s.d. 7.45),Reported for laboratory sample as a whole.,1,42.3% female,Reported for laboratory sample as a whole.,1,University students (Harvard and Yale subject pools),Recruited via university recruitment system SONA at Harvard and Yale.,0.9,On site,Physical lab sessions at Harvard and Yale with in-person attendance using browsers.,1,"Repeated 10-period linear public goods game, fixed groups of 4, MPCR 0.4, feedback: own and others’ contributions; partner matching, two-part within-subject design, this is first part without punishment. Lab exchange rate $0.02 per point plus $10 show-up fee.",Synthesized from design description in Sections 2.1–2.4.,1
