£3 per round.,1,0.88,Overall high-identification condition had 88% contributors; assumed homogeneous across provision/feedback as the paper reports no interactions (χ² for provision point < 1).,0.6,2.64,Binary decision: contribute £3 or £0; expected amount = 0.88 × 3 = 2.64 in high-identification conditions.,0.6,N/R,No payoffs or efficiency ratios reported by condition.,1,N/R,No group earnings reported at condition level.,1,United Kingdom,Participants are Southampton University undergraduates in the south of England.,0.95,18-22,Reported age range for Study 1 participants.,1,"Approximately 62 female, 33 male, 1 not reported across all conditions",Study 1 sample description; distribution across cells not given.,0.7,Undergraduate psychology students,Explicitly described as undergraduate psychology students from Southampton University.,1,On site,Participants attended the laboratory and sat in individual cubicles.,1,"Step-level public good with group bonus £30 (i.e., £5 per person) if minimum 2 of 6 contribute; otherwise only contributors lose £3 and no bonus is paid. Decisions were one-shot per round; leader types were chosen but never implemented in actual payoff structure.",Summarized from Study 1 task description and leader-choice procedure.,1
