10.1037_0022-3514.76.4.587.md,"Study 2 – High identification, instrumental leader",Study 2 has 2 (identification) × 2 (leader type); this row is high-ID with instrumental leader.,1,Group identification = high; Leader type = instrumental (punishes lowest contributor 220 pence each round); Sessions factor = before vs. after leader introduction,Directly from Study 2 design and leader manipulation.,1,True,Human participants contributing money in repeated public goods task.,1,True,"Random assignment to identification and leader-type conditions, with controlled feedback.",1,True,Participants invited to university laboratory in groups of six.,1,False,No artificial agents or numeric simulation.,1,False,Not a formal analytical model test.,1,6,Six participants per experimental session.,1,8,Eight contribution sessions in total.,1,1,"Contributions are continuous: any amount between 0 and 300 pence, not all-or-nothing.",1,0,"At the beginning of each session, each member receives an endowment of £3, fully private.",1,1.6667,"Group bonus £30 if group contributes at least £12 total. If exactly £12 is invested, total group surplus over contributions is £30 − £12 = £18; per capita return per £1 contributed is £30/£12 = 2.5. MPCR = 2.5 / 6 ≈ 0.4167. However, for each individual, marginal group benefit per £1 is £30/£12 = 2.5 and their own share is 2.5/6 ≈ 0.4167. Summation over group yields 2.5. To stay consistent with definition multiplier/group size, multiplier here is 2.5, so MPCR = 2.5/6 ≈ 0.4167.",0.5,0,No communication channel among participants; only one-way leader/examiner messages.,1,0,Participants receive only group total success/failure information and that least contributor was punished; no full earnings or contribution profiles shared.,0.7,0,Message indicates ‘the least contributing group member’ is punished but does not reveal who; identities stay anonymous.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism; leader only promises to distribute bonus equally when earned.,1,1,Participants are informed there will be eight contribution sessions.,1,1,Instrumental leader imposes a fine of 220 pence on least-contributing member each session.,1,0,"Leader is an external assistant; no indication that punisher pays a cost from their own payoff, so cost per punishment coin from punisher’s perspective is effectively zero.",0.6,220,Punishment is a fixed fine of 220 pence to the lowest contributor per session; treat that as punishment magnitude.,1,0,"No explicit positive rewards per contribution; only possibility of group bonus, not discretionary rewards.",1,N/A,No reward option.,1,N/A,No reward option.,1,3,Each group member receives £3 (300 pence) each of the 8 sessions.,1,0.7551,"Average contribution in high-identification groups overall is 215.58 pence out of 300 pence. Normalized rate = 215.58 / 300 ≈ 0.7186 across both leader types. Specifically for high-ID + instrumental leader, overall mean across sessions is about (209.77 + 226.54)/2 ≈ 218.16, giving 218.16/300 ≈ 0.727, but the paper reports only per-block means; using with-leader sessions: 226.54/300 ≈ 0.755.",0.5,226.54,"For high-identification groups with instrumental leader in sessions with leader, mean contribution is 226.54 pence.",1,N/R,No explicit efficiency (payoff / max payoff) reported or derivable by condition because actual provision and fines per session not given.,0.7,N/R,Group-level earnings not reported by condition.,1,United Kingdom,Participants are Southampton University students in England.,0.95,18-25,Study 2 age range.,1,"59 female, 34 male across all Study 2 conditions",Overall sample composition; not broken down by condition.,0.7,Undergraduate students,Described as undergraduate Southampton University students (no major specified).,1,On site,Participants attended the laboratory in groups of six.,1,"Linear public goods game with per-session endowment 300 pence. Group earns £30 bonus if total contributions reach at least 1200 pence (i.e., £12). Eight sessions; first 4 without leader, second 4 with instrumental leader who observes individual contributions, always reports group failure to obtain bonus, and fines the least contributor 220 pence each session.",Summarized from Study 2 task and leader description.,1
