10.1016_j.plrev.2016.08.015.md,ES-set probabilistic strategy simulations (Fig. 5b – 3-gene encoding),"Fig. 5b explicitly labeled as '3-genes encoding', showing average trajectories of probabilistic strategies towards an ES-set for a=1,b=0.2.",1,"Encoding scheme of probabilities (3-gene implementation where mutation in one locus renormalizes all three probabilities p,q,r); game parameters a=1, b=0.2; mutation type local ±5%.",Text distinguishes 3-gene vs 2-gene encodings while holding payoff parameters fixed.,1,False,Digital agents only.,1,False,"Simulation study of evolutionary trajectories, not empirical experiment with humans.",1,False,No physical lab with subjects.,1,True,Described as agent-based methods exploring ES-set dynamics.,1,False,Analytical ES-set theory exists but this condition is numerical implementation with genetic encoding.,1,1024,"Stated: 'obtained from populations with 1,024 agents'.",1,3000,"Runs described as 'evolving... for 3,000 generations'.",1,1,"Agents choose between discrete pure moves C,D,M probabilistically; not a continuous investment game.",0.7,N/A,No contribution or endowment.,1,N/A,Not a public goods game.,1,N/A,No human communication; genetic encoding only.,1,N/A,No UI.,1,N/A,No punishment action.,1,N/A,No reward action.,1,N/A,No human interface.,1,0,Only payoffs are defined by three-strategy snowdrift-derived matrix; no separate punishment decision.,1,N/A,No punishment option.,1,N/A,No punishment option.,1,0,No separate reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No tokens endowed.,1,N/A,Not a contributions game.,1,N/A,Not a contributions game.,1,N/R,Only trajectories in strategy simplex relative to deterministic ES-set are discussed.,0.2,N/R,Group payoffs are not reported numerically.,0.2,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Agent-based genetic algorithm with digital agents.,1,"Three-strategy game with C, D, and M where M replicates payoffs of the mixed ESS of the underlying snowdrift game (a=1,b=0.2). Strategies are probabilistic over C,D,M with three genetic loci (3-gene encoding). Mutation is local (±5%) with renormalization. Populations of 1024 agents evolved for 3000 generations; trajectories converge to the deterministic ES-set but paths depend on encoding.","Combines game, encoding, mutation, and qualitative outcome from the description.",1
