10.1016_j.plrev.2016.08.015.md,"Memory-one Prisoner's Dilemma evolutionary simulations – donation game, GCd quasistrategy (Fig. 6a)","Fig. 6a: 'Average LOD that begins with a population of ZD_R strategies ... donation game payoff matrix (2,-1,3,0)'; result is GCd quasistrategy.",1,"Initial resident strategy ZD_R with probability vector (1.0,0.35,0.75,0.1); payoff matrix donation game (R,S,T,P)=(2,-1,3,0); mutation rate 1% per locus; population size N=1024; well-mixed Moran/WF-style updating.",These parameters are explicitly given as defining the condition.,1,False,Purely agent-based evolutionary simulations.,1,False,No empirical data collection; simulation-based test of theoretical robustness.,1,False,No lab with human subjects.,1,True,Described as agent-based simulations evolving memory-one strategies.,1,False,Mathematical predictions are contrasted to these numerical results.,1,1024,"Fig. 6 caption: 'All runs use N=1,024'.",1,2000000,Fig. 6 caption: 'We show only the first 100K of 2×10^6 generations.',1,1,"Each round, agents choose C or D; binary choice mapped as standard non-all-or-nothing contribution to a public good is not applicable; here it's PD actions.",0.6,N/A,No endowed tokens; binary PD actions only.,1,N/A,Not a PG game.,1,N/A,"Strategies condition on past moves via memory-one, not explicit communication.",1,N/A,No human interface.,1,N/A,No punishment action variable; PD payoffs only.,1,N/A,No separate reward option.,1,N/A,No display.,1,0,Payoffs follow donation game PD; no extra punishment decision.,1,N/A,No punishment feature.,1,N/A,No punishment feature.,1,0,No explicit costly reward; only base PD payoffs.,1,N/A,No reward feature.,1,N/A,No reward feature.,1,N/A,No tokens.,1,N/A,"Game is PD, not public goods; they track probabilities p1..p4 not normalized contributions.",1,N/A,No numeric contributions.,1,N/R,"They track evolution of probability vector, not average payoff divided by maximum.",0.3,N/R,Group payoff statistics not given; only relative stability of strategies and quasistrategies.,0.3,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Computational evolutionary game.,1,"Iterated Prisoner’s Dilemma using donation game payoffs (2,-1,3,0). Strategies are memory-one with probabilities (p1..p4) plus first-move probability p0; initial population monomorphic ZD_R (1.0,0.35,0.75,0.1). Population of 1024 agents evolves for 2M generations at per-locus mutation 1%. Analysis of lines of descent shows ZD_R is unstable in WSSM regime and is replaced by a cooperative quasistrategy 'GCd' with mean probabilities approximately (1.0,0.36,0.42,0.64).","Captures payoff matrix, strategy parameterization, and main qualitative outcome.",1
