at when DS is most abundant initially, DN tends to win for small β, DA for large β, and additional simulations show CP winning when β>10. Self-inconsistent strategies like DS punish their own type, which undermines their success on the lattice; hence DS never ultimately dominates despite initial majority.",Summarized from Figure 3C caption and surrounding text explaining outcomes when DS is initially most abundant.,1
