10.1257_aer.100.1.420.md,"4:4P – Team vs Team, 20 rounds, with intra-team punishment",Treatment '4:4P' has two four-person teams with within-team punishment opportunities over 20 rounds.,1,"Contest party composition and punishment: team of 4 vs team of 4 (4:4P), intra-team punishment enabled, 20-round horizon",Key variations are team size (4 vs 4) and presence of punishment.,1,True,Lab experiment with human participants.,1,True,Controlled randomized treatment in laboratory.,1,True,Conducted at University of Nottingham lab using PCs.,1,False,"Human experiment, no computational model here.",1,False,This row is empirical treatment.,1,8,Two teams of four; eight participants per contest group.,1,20,4:4P listed among four 20-round treatments.,1,1,Contest token choice 0–1000 per player as integer.,1,0,Participants start each round with 1000 private points used to buy tokens.,1,N/R,Not a linear public-goods environment.,1,0,Instructions prohibit any communication beyond computer interface.,1,1,"Team members see each teammate’s contest tokens and know total team and rival tokens; after punishment, they see received punishment.",1,1,Participants assign deduction tokens to each of the other own team members individually; they must know which teammate punished them to compute 'received punishment from team colleagues'.,0.7,0,Group-level win/loss is shown but identities of rival team members remain anonymous.,0.8,1,20-round horizon explicitly stated; likely indicated on screen as in instructions.,0.6,1,4:4P adds possibility of punishment between own team members.,1,1,Each deduction token assigned costs punisher one point.,1,3,Each deduction token received reduces recipient’s point balance by three points (ignoring capped excess).,1,1,Lottery determines which team wins 1000-point prize for each member.,1,0,"Prize is funded by experimenter, not by players.",1,1000,"Winning team members each receive 1,000 points.",1,1000,"At beginning of each round each participant receives endowment of 1,000 points.",1,N/R,"Paper provides per-team contest expenditures and punishment levels, but not normalized contribution rates.",0.4,1530,"In last five rounds of 4:4P, direct contest expenditures per team are 1,530 points on average.",0.9,N/R,They report rent dissipation and material losses as multiples of equilibrium; direct efficiency ratio (payoff/max payoff) not separately stated.,0.4,N/R,No explicit per-group payoff for 4:4P presented.,0.2,United Kingdom,Same Nottingham lab as other treatments.,0.9,University undergraduates; exact ages N/R,Unified undergraduate subject pool; ages not detailed.,0.7,N/R,No gender statistics reported.,1,Undergraduate students,Subjects recruited from undergraduate pool.,1,On site,Same lab environment described in procedures.,1,"Same 4:4 contest as without punishment, but with an additional punishment stage each round. After lottery, each participant may assign up to 500 'deduction tokens' to each of the three teammates. Each assigned token costs punisher 1 point and reduces recipient’s payoff by 3 points (subject to lower bound of zero for round earnings). Punishment and conflict expenditures are borne individually but affect team morale and effective payoffs.",Summarizes extra punishment stage and parameters unique to 4:4P.,1
