ach participant decided whether to contribute an endowment of C$5.00.,1,N/R,Only proportion cooperating (65%) is given; no normalized mean across all subjects reported.,0.6,N/R,"Reported only as proportion cooperating, not mean amount (binary contribute/keep).",0.6,N/R,No aggregate payoff relative to maximum fully cooperative payoff reported.,0,N/R,Group earnings not tabulated in results.,0,Canada,"Participants were first-year students at McMaster University, Hamilton, Ontario, Canada.",0.95,N/R,Described only as 1st-year students; no age statistics given.,0.4,N/R,Gender composition not reported.,0,1st-year university students,Explicitly stated that participants were 1st-year students at McMaster University.,1,On site,Conducted on computers with partitions in a university setting.,1,"One-shot 4-player public goods game with binary contribution (C$5 or 0), MPCR 0.5; then two unanticipated sanction stages with punishment only. Stage 1: participants got three C$1 endowments (one per other player) to punish any of three others (3:1 impact). Stage 2: exogenous pattern where one cooperator punished defector with ~C$0.80–1.00 and other cooperator and defector did not punish; participants then received C$1 per other player to punish again.",Summarized procedural description of Study 1 punishment condition.,1
