f NO-players receiving NO are described, not overall help rates.",0.2,N/R,No aggregate help counts provided.,0.1,N/R,No payoff efficiency metrics reported.,0.1,N/R,No payoff statistics reported.,0.1,Germany,Author’s institution is in Germany and many cited experiments are from German universities; paper later thanks students from German universities as participants.,0.6,N/R,Only described as students; no age data.,0.3,N/R,No gender information.,0.1,University students,Described as students in typical university lab experiments.,0.9,On site,Standard laboratory economic experiment; no indication of online implementation.,0.9,Indirect reciprocity helping game with 6 subjects + 1 instructed NO-player per group. NO-player always refuses to help. 16 rounds. Treatments vary information: much vs little information about others’ previous decisions. Behaviour of donors towards donors of NO-player used to infer reputation updating rule (scoring vs standing).,Summarizes key procedural elements mentioned in section 4 and Figure 2 description.,0.95
