10.1016_j.jtbi.2008.09.015.md,"Simulation – robustness parameter sweeps (β, α, d=e, b, τ, μ, w)",Set of simulations varying payoff and evolutionary parameters to test robustness of preference for D over P in response to defection (Figure 6).,1,"One parameter varied at a time among β, α, d=e, b, τ, μ, w; baseline b=3, c=1, d=e=1, α=1, β=4, τ=0.8, μ=0.1; w=1 except when w is varied",Authors specify a baseline parameter set and then vary each parameter individually (Figure 6A–G).,1,False,No human subjects; it is a computational evolutionary model.,1,False,"Parameter sweeps in simulations, not empirical experiments.",1,False,No physical laboratory or human participants.,1,True,Described explicitly as simulations with parameters varied.,1,False,These results come from simulations rather than analytic expressions.,1,2,Interactions are pairwise games between two agents.,0.9,0,"Primarily w=1 (infinite repetition); when w<1, expected number of rounds finite but not specified; encoded as 0 for indefinite/variable.",0.7,0,"Only discrete PD actions C, D, P exist.",0.6,N/A,No endowment-based contributions; direct PD payoffs.,1,N/R,Not a public-goods framework; MPCR not defined.,1,N/A,No agent communication modeled.,1,0,"Selection uses payoffs, but no explicit feedback summaries described.",0.8,N/A,Agents lack identities in the model.,1,N/A,No reward stage.,1,0,Rounds are not explicitly represented to agents.,1,1,Punishment action P is present in all these simulations.,1,1,"Baseline α=1, and α is also varied in one of the sweeps; since this object aggregates multiple values, we record baseline α=1.",0.6,4,Baseline β=4; also varied in one sweep; baseline recorded here.,0.6,0,No reward mechanism is modeled across these simulations.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/R,Model specifies payoffs directly without an explicit endowment.,0.8,N/R,"Main outcome is probability to defect vs punish in response to defection (q2 and r2), not contribution rates.",1,N/R,No c