in study conditions.,0.8,Mean age 20.19 years; undergraduates,Same sample as other main study conditions.,1,69% female,Sample-level gender composition applies to all three main study conditions.,1,Undergraduate students,Participants described as undergraduates.,1,On site,Conducted in the university lab using computers.,1,"One-shot incentivized trust game: participant as investor interacts with a partner described as having previously punished an unfair allocator by spending €1.50 out of €5, reducing allocator’s payoff by €3 in the prior third-party punishment scenario. The partner is programmed to return 50% of the tripled amount.",Highlights that this condition models a strong altruistic punisher signal in the main trust game.,1
