ism.,1,0,No rewarding mechanisms are modeled.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,1,"Section 4: ""b = 1"" in Fig. 2 caption; Section 3 and 7 also use b=1.0 in examples.",0.9,N/R,"They analyze fraction of cooperators and group achievement, but no single normalized contribution rate is reported.",0.6,N/R,"Individual contribution is c·b per cooperator, but no aggregate amount is summarized as a main DV.",0.6,N/R,"They compute group achievement η_G and stationary distributions, but not payoff efficiency as defined.",0.7,N/R,"Expected payoffs are defined, but no summarized group payoff outcome is reported as a central DV.",0.7,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely theoretical/simulation study.,1,"Threshold public goods game with risk of collective loss: population size e.g. Z=50, group size N=6, threshold n_pg=3, contribution cost fraction c=0.1, risk r varied, mutation rate μ=0.005, selection intensity β=5.0.",Values taken from Fig. 1 caption and model description in Section 2.,0.9
