10.1016_j.jebo.2009.03.022.md,"No-punishment condition (periods 1–10, pooled across Baseline, Sequential, Consensual sessions)",Part 1 of every session is a public good game without punishment; same structure across all three treatments so results are pooled.,0.9,Punishment availability = No punishment,Part 1 explicitly has no punishment opportunity; this is the control condition before punishment institutions are introduced.,1,True,Human undergraduates played the public good game.,1,True,Controlled randomized lab sessions with specified rules and treatments.,1,True,Sessions conducted at University of Siena using z-Tree software in a lab setting.,1,False,No agent-based or numerical simulations; all data from human subjects.,1,False,"Paper reports experimental and econometric results, not purely analytical models.",1,5,“In every period the participants are randomly partitioned into four groups of N=5 individuals.”,1,10,Part 1 is “periods 1–10” with no punishment.,1,1,"Subjects choose gi in [0,20], a continuous range, not an all-or-nothing decision.",1,0,Each period subjects receive an endowment of 20 tokens in a private account and then choose how much to contribute.,1,0.4,Payoff function specifies a=0.4 as the marginal per capita return from the public good.,1,0,“No communication among subjects is allowed.”,1,1,After each period subjects are informed about total contribution and contributions and earnings of every member in their group.,1,0,No punishment exists in this part; set to 0 as inapplicable display of identities.,0.5,0,No rewards mechanism in the design.,1,1,"Standard in z-Tree public good experiments; instructions mention “two parts” and specific periods; though not verbatim, it is very likely subjects knew the number of periods.",0.7,0,Part 1 explicitly has no punishment opportunity.,1,N/A,No punishment stage in this condition.,1,N/A,No punishment stage in this condition.,1,0,Only costly punishment is described; no positive rewards.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism exists.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism exists.,1,20,“Each subject i receives an endowment of 20 tokens.”,1,0.1655,Average individual contribution without punishment across all treatments is 3.31 tokens (text: 3.31); divide by endowment 20 gives 3.31/20≈0.1655.,0.95,3.31,Reported as “average individual contribution across all treatments is 3.31 tokens” without punishment.,0.95,N/R,No explicit or easily reconstructable measure of efficiency (total payoff relative to maximum) reported separately for the no-punishment condition.,0,N/R,Earnings data only reported in normalized or comparative terms including punishment; not directly for no-punishment group payoff.,0,Italy,Subjects recruited at the University of Siena in Italy.,1,N/R,Only described as general undergraduate student population; no age statistics given.,0.3,N/R,No information on gender composition.,0,Undergraduate students,“Recruited among the general undergraduate student population of the University of Siena.”,1,On site,Lab sessions at University of Siena with physical payment in cash; not online.,1,Linear public goods game with random rematching of 5-player groups each period; 20-token endowment; MPCR 0.4; payoffs: π_i = 20 - g_i + 0.4 Σ g_j.,Summarized directly from design description in Section 1.,1
