10.1098_rspb.2010.1275.md,"Simulation – perception errors, low benefit b (electronic supplementary material, Figure S2a–c)","Text describes additional simulations introducing errors in perceiving scores, particularly noting that with low benefit b, errors hinder emergence of punishment and cooperation (""figure S2a–c"").",0.8,"Error rate ε in reputation perception varied, with relatively low benefit b (exact value not reported), cost of helping c=1, n=500, m=30, mutation rate μ=0.02; punishment parameters s and e as in main simulations (exact values not reported).","They describe adding perception errors with probability ε and state that low b plus higher ε hinder punishment; precise numeric b, s, e, ε values are only said to be in supplementary figures.",0.4,False,Agent-based simulations with modified error mechanism.,1,False,Simulation study.,1,False,No physical lab with subjects.,1,True,These are described as tests done by simulation in the same framework.,1,False,Not a closed-form analytical error model.,1,500,They used n=500 in all simulations; errors added on top.,0.9,30,m=30 throughout simulations.,0.9,1,Binary help decisions.,1,N/A,No public good.,1,N/A,Not a PGG.,1,N/A,No communication in simulation.,1,N/A,No interface.,1,N/A,"Reputation scores, not identity, and no human interface.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,1,Punishment still available; only perception of scores is noisy.,1,N/R,"Punishment cost s used as in baseline simulations, but specific numeric values for this condition are not stated in main text.",0.4,N/R,"Damage e used, but specific numeric values not given here.",0.4,0,No mention of rewards in error simulations.,1,N/A,No rewards modeled.,1,N/A,No rewards modeled.,1,N/A,No token endowment.,1,N/R,"Main text qualitatively states that errors hinder emergence of cooperation when b is low, but gives no numerical cooperation rates.",0.2,N/R,No raw help counts reported.,0.2,N/R,No payoff efficiency values described.,0.2,N/R,No payoff numbers reported.,0.2,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Computer simulation.,1,"Same 40-strategy helping/punishment game as baseline, but with perception errors in reputational scores. After each interaction, with probability ε, donor’s image score Is is randomly replaced by Is−1, Is+0 or Is+1; similarly, receiver’s punishment score ki is randomly changed by −1, 0 or +1. Errors are more influential at beginning of each generation when scores are less informative. For relatively low benefit b, increasing ε often hinders emergence of punishment and cooperation.","Summarized from paragraph describing error inclusion and its effects (electronic supplementary material, figure S2).",0.9
