s are introduced in both cooperation scores Is and punishment scores ki with probability ε after each interaction. For higher benefit b, punishment and cooperation can still emerge despite errors, but increasing ε reduces the relative success of reputation-based punishing discriminators (z_P) and punishing image scorers (a_P) compared to punishing cooperators (y_P), which do not rely on reputation.","Summarized from paragraph discussing impact of errors for greater b and referencing electronic supplementary material, figure S2 d–i.",0.9
