ity students; exact age not reported,Participants are from general student population; no age stats.,0.6,N/R,No gender information provided.,0,University students (undergraduate/graduate; level not further specified),Recruited from a university student pool.,0.8,On site,Subjects sat at isolated computer terminals in a lab.,1,Strangers design; random reassignment to groups each round; 10 periods; sequence: contribution stage then punishment stage; contributions and individual others’ contributions displayed in random order; payoff: π_i = w[σ_i + q(1-σ̄)] - Σ_j s_ij - 2 Σ_j s_ji with q such that q/n=0.7; endowment 25 EMUs; punishment technology 1→2; no rewards.,"Summarizes rules for this treatment (n=4, high q/n) from design description.",1
10.1016_j.jebo.2009.03.011.md,"Large team, low productivity (n=8, MPCR=0.3)","Condition with eight-person teams and q/n=0.3 (large n, low q/n).",1,Team size n=8; MPCR=q/n=0.3; punishment allowed with cost 1 and impact 2; strangers matching over 10 rounds,This treatment combines large group size (8) with low productivity q/n=0.3.,1,True,Human-subject experiment.,1,True,Controlled lab experiment manipulating n and q/n.,1,True,Sessions at computer terminals on site.,1,False,No simulation component in this condition.,1,False,Row does not refer to purely analytical model.,1,8,Eight-person team treatment as specified in design.,1,10,Ten periods in all sessions.,1,1,Any fraction of 25 EMU endowment could be contributed.,1,0,Endowment is initially in private account; contributions transfer tokens to public account.,0.95,0.3,Low productivity treatment with q/n=0.3.,1,0,No communication reported.,0.9,1,"Total group contribution, own gross earnings, and contributions of each other member shown.",1,0,Punishment directed at anonymous co-players; no indication of revealed personal identities.,0.6,0,No reward option.,1,1,Fixed 10-round horizon is standardly communicated; implied though not verbatim.,0.9,1,Design explicitly includes punishment stage after contributions.,1,1,Punisher spends 1 EMU to impose 2 EMU loss.,1,2,"Payoff formula includes '-2 Σ s_ji', implying 2 EMU loss per 1 EMU spent.",1,0,Only negative 'reductions' allowed.,1,N/A,Rewards not available.,1,N/A,Rewards not available.,1,25,w=25 EMUs per player per round.,1,0.54,Only pooled average trajectory is reported; use pooled period-10 value (54%) as approximate contribution rate.,0.4,N/R,No separate mean contribution level by treatment is reported.,0,N/R,Efficiency is discussed qualitatively but not quantified by treatment.,0,N/R,Group payoff statistics by treatment are not given.,0,United States,Participants from University of Massachusetts in the US.,1,Primarily university students; exact age not reported,Drawn from