10.1016_j.ejor.2008.01.021.md,"Continuous-strategy e-collaboration game without explicit social punishment (quadratic payoff, generic parameters)",Section 3.2 introduces an asymmetric 2-player continuous-strategy e-collaboration game with quadratic benefit and cost functions (Eqs. 8–12) and analyzes equilibrium effort levels p* and q*.,0.95,"Players’ maximum budgets x_m, y_m; benefit parameters α1, α2, β1, β2; cost parameters c1, c2, d1, d2; interaction parameter λ.",These parameters shape the payoff functions and determine equilibrium effort levels p* and q*.,0.98,False,No human data; model is solved analytically.,1,False,Not a controlled experiment; formal model only.,1,False,No laboratory setting is used.,1,False,"Although some sensitivity analyses are plotted (Figs. 2–4), they are direct evaluations of analytical formulas, not a separate simulation model with agents.",0.75,True,"Closed-form first-order conditions, propositions, and corollaries are derived for the continuous-strategy game.",1,2,Defined as a two-player e-collaboration game (Player 1 and Player 2).,1,1,"This section analyzes a static continuous game, not an explicitly repeated interaction; dynamic aspects enter later in Section 3.3 and Section 4.",0.85,0,"Players choose continuous effort levels p and q between 0 and 1, representing partial contributions.",1,N/A,No endowment or automatic allocation is defined and there are no human subjects.,1,N/R,Model is not framed as a linear public good; no MPCR is stated.,1,N/A,Theoretical continuous-control game; no communication protocol.,1,0,Static model with no in-game feedback display.,0.9,N/A,"In this version of the continuous game, punishment is embedded implicitly in cost; there is no explicit punisher with identity.",0.9,N/A,No explicit rewards mechanism.,1,0,Single-stage static analysis only.,0.95,0,"At this point, social punishment is said to be implicitly included in the cost term; there is no explicit, separate punishment parameter or action in the