10.1257_aer.102.7.3317.md,Noise – Regular punishment,Treatment with noisy monitoring and regular punishment technology.,1,"Monitoring: noise (10% misreport of contributions as no contribution); Punishment: regular (3:1 damage, capped, up to 5 points to each other)",Noise dimension with small noise; punishment dimension with standard 3:1 capped technology.,1,True,Human participants in lab.,1,True,Treatment in controlled experiment.,1,True,Conducted on site at lab.,1,False,No purely simulated treatment.,1,False,No closed-form analytical experiment.,1,3,Groups of 3 fixed throughout.,1,50,Same 50-round design.,1,0,Contribution must be all or none of 20 tokens.,1,0,All tokens start in private account.,1,0.5,Same contribution-payoff mapping.,1,0,No communication mentioned.,0.8,1,Subjects observe public records of each member’s contribution; payoffs derived from these true decisions.,0.7,1,"As in other punishment treatments, anonymous IDs allow targeted punishment.",0.9,0,No rewards.,1,1,Repeated game horizon known.,0.6,1,Regular punishment treatment with second stage.,1,1,Each assigned deduction point costs punisher 1.,1,3,Each deduction point reduces target’s income by 3; capped at earnings.,1,0,No reward stage.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,20,20 tokens each round.,1,9.6,Table 1: average contribution = 9.60 tokens. Normalized fraction 9.60/20 = 0.48; we compute this as rate.,0.6,9.6,Average contribution 9.60 tokens (Noise – Regular punishment row in Table 1).,1,N/R,No explicit net-earnings-to-max-payoff ratio.,0,19.1,Table 1: average net profits per participant = 19.10 for Noise – Regular punishment.,0.7,Australia,Same UNSW lab sample.,1,N/R,Not reported.,0.3,N/R,Not reported.,0,University students,All subjects drawn from university student population.,1,On site,Same lab setting as other treatments.,1,"Same binary public good with imperfect public monitoring (10% probability a contribution is misrecorded as no contribution); punishment stage with regular technol