t cost of punishment is not defined; use base tax component as minimal per-round cost to enable punishment.,0.2,1,Fine for each defector and tax evader is €1.00 per offense; treating tech as 1 unit fine per offense per round.,0.7,0,"Design only includes punishment, no rewards.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,0.9,"Players can choose to be loners with fixed payoff €0.40 or participate: if they contribute €0.50 and pay up to about €0.55 tax (0.05+0.5), their gross amount per round is roughly €0.90 at stake (0.40 alternative plus 0.50 contribution less tax). However, explicit per-round monetary endowment is not clearly specified; 0.90 is an approximate stake based on described amounts.",0.2,0.965,Fraction of cooperators with second-order punishment in block II is 96.5%. Binary contribution decision so contribution rate equals that fraction.,1,N/R,"Average raw contribution amount in euros not reported, only fraction of cooperators.",0.1,N/R,"Average payoff per round is €0.86, but maximum possible payoff under full cooperation without taxes is not clearly given due to varying taxes and loner option, so efficiency ratio cannot be computed reliably.",0.2,4.3,Average individual payoff €0.86 per round with 2OP; group of 5 so average group payoff 0.86×5 = €4.30.,0.9,Germany,"Experiments conducted at University of Kiel, Germany, with local first-year biology students.",1,N/R,Only that they are first-year biology students; no age statistics given.,0.4,N/R,Gender composition not reported.,0.1,First-year university biology students,Subjects recruited from a first-year course in biology.,1,On site,Standard lab experiment at a university; no indication of online implementation.,0.9,"Voluntary participation with loner option paying €0.40; if they participate, subjects decide whether to pay taxes to a central authority and whether to contribute €0.50 to a public good; total contributions multiplied by 3.1 and redistributed to all participants; if at least one 