 pool as other conditions.,1,Mean 23.1 years (s.d. 3.13),Overall sample description.,1,52.5% female,Overall sample composition applies here.,0.9,University students,Participants are students from University of Zurich and ETH Zurich.,1,On site,Laboratory experiment in person.,1,"Volunteer’s dilemma with asymmetric punishment costs: persons 1, 2, and 3 each start with 140 MU; person X may steal 70 MU from each (total 210 MU). If at least one of 1–3 chooses 'up', the steal is undone and all other players return to 140 MU; person 2 pays 30 MU when choosing 'up', persons 1 and 3 pay 40 MU. No additional penalty is imposed on X in this part.",Summarizes the asymmetric no-penalty rules given in design section and table 1.,1
