10.2307_2095953.md,"Simulation – Material sanctions (baseline, Figure 3 type)","Represents the main simulation condition with material sanctions: N=100, J=0.5, J'=0.5, m=1, E=0.5, hypocrites influential.",0.93,"Sanction regime: material sanctions with partial jointness (J'=0.5), linear second-order production (m=1), hypocrites influential; Group size N=100; First-order jointness J=0.5; Learning rate E=0.5.","Derived from the description of the condition underlying Figure 3 and the first material-sanction curve in Figure 4: N=100, J=J'=0.5, m=1, E=0.5, hypocrites fully influential.",0.9,False,Study is explicitly described as computer simulations with no human subjects.,1,False,"The work is a theoretical computer simulation, not a controlled behavioral experiment with subjects.",1,False,No physical lab or human participants; purely computational.,1,True,Author repeatedly refers to simulations based on specified equations and parameters.,1,True,Paper develops and analyzes formal mathematical model along with simulations.,1,100,"Group size N=100 is specified for these simulations (e.g., 'Consider a group of 100 members.').",1,N/R,Number of iterations simulated is not given as a fixed horizon; figures show time steps but total count not specified.,0,0,"Decisions are modeled as binary 'volunteer' or 'defect' (nondivisible), not continuous contribution amounts; this corresponds to all-or-nothing contributions.",1,N/A,No endowments or starting allocations; purely theoretical binary participation model with no human players.,1,N/R,No linear public-goods multiplier or marginal per capita return specified; only a logistic production function L(P).,0,N/A,No human subjects or interface; chat not applicable.,1,N/A,No user interface or feedback screens; only model variables.,1,N/A,No identities or observability modeled; just aggregate rates.,1,N/A,No identities or observability modeled.,1,N/A,No human subjects or interface.,1,1,Sanctions exist and include both positive and negative material incentives in this condition.,1,N/R,Model gives cost of sanctioning as C' = V'/N^{J'} or side-payment formulation but not as a discrete 'coins per unit' parameter.,0.4,N/R,Effectiveness of sanctions is embedded in S_ij = P'^m(...) but not decomposed as a per-coin technology factor.,0.4,1,"Selective incentives include positive side payments to volunteers, not just punishments.",0.9,N/R,Cost of positive material incentives is part of C'_ij but not parameterized as cost per reward unit.,0.4,N/R,No explicit reward technology parameter; folded into S_ij function.,0.3,N/A,No tokens or endowments for agents; only abstract utilities.,1,N/R,"Time paths of contribution rates P_i and equilibria (e.g., Pe≈0.6–0.78) are described qualitatively but no single summary DV is reported.",0.3,N/A,Binary volunteer/defect decisions; no numeric contribution amounts.,1,N/R,No explicit ratio of achieved payoff to maximum is provided.,0,N/R,Outcomes O_i and L_i are discussed but no aggregate payoff figures reported.,0,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely computer-based simulations without subjects.,1,"Theoretical collective action/public good game with binary participation; first-order public-good production via S-shaped logistic function L(P)=1/(1+e^{(0.5-P)10}); costs depend on jointness J=0.5; second-order sanctioning with material incentives: jointness of supply J'=0.5, linear sanction production m=1, hypocritical sanctioners fully influential; learning via Bush–Mosteller reinforcement with learning rate E=0.5.",Summarizes core structural and parametric aspects of the modeled interaction in this condition.,0.95
