ons discussed qualitatively (overcooperation), but no numeric value.",0.1,N/R,No numeric group payoff reported.,0,N/A,No participants.,1,N/A,No participants.,1,N/A,No participants.,1,N/A,No participants.,1,No human,Purely computational model.,1,"Only first-order participation decision; no explicit second-order enforcement choice. Internal moral pressure implemented by modifying S_ij = P_i^m d V_ij - P_i^m d (1-V_ij) with m=2 and d=0.5; J'=1 so cost of self-imposed norms does not scale with group size. First-order public-good production uses J=0.5 and logistic L(P); learning rate E=0.5. This regime tends to produce very high, potentially excessive, cooperation once mobilized.",Captures the structural features of the internal-fairness condition at d=0.5.,0.95
