ls of participants.,1,Field experiment,"Although not an experiment in the strict sense, data collection took place in participants’ natural village environment; closest category is field experiment rather than on-site lab or observational-with-no-intervention. Instructions and structured tasks (pile sorts) were administered in the field.",0.7,"Observational field study of Shuar village where pro-community behaviors (years in public office, attendance at compulsory mingas and meetings with monetary fines for absence, and perceived work effort) predict perceived altruism and social status; no formal public goods game with tokens or explicit payoff function.",Summary of design details explicitly described under Method for Study One.,1
