10.1098_rsbl.2012.0470.md,Treatment C – P1 punishment decision,Third treatment with distinct initial endowments (C); punishment decision of P1 is main dependent behavior.,1,"Treatment C: Initial endowments P1=$0.70, P2=$0.70; P2 cheating decision (cheat vs not cheat)",Treatment C defined by equal initial endowments and P2’s cheating action; both influence P1’s punishment.,1,True,"Same AMT-based human experiment, treatment C subset.",1,True,Pre-registered style experimental design with random assignment to treatment C.,1,False,"Online environment via AMT, not an on-site lab.",1,False,"Human decisions, no simulation.",1,False,No purely analytical game-theoretic model; empirical study.,1,2,Two players: P1 and P2.,1,1,Subjects play a single interaction in one role and treatment.,0.9,1,Not a contribution game; record as non all-or-nothing per generic rule.,0.3,N/A,No contribution decision exists.,1,N/R,No public goods component.,1,0,No mention of any participant communication; interactions purely via the experiment interface.,0.9,0,No reporting that players saw summaries of others' outcomes.,0.7,0,Anonymity via worker IDs and statement that IDs would not be revealed.,1,0,No rewarding option implemented.,1,0,Design is one-shot; no explicit mention of any round counter.,0.8,1,"P1 can punish P2 at a cost of $0.10 to themselves, reducing P2's income by $0.30.",1,0.1,Punishment decision cost is specified as $0.10.,1,0.3,Each $0.10 spent inflicts $0.30 loss on P2.,1,0,No rewarding mechanism in the described game.,1,N/A,Rewards not available.,1,N/A,Rewards not available.,1,1.4,Total pair endowment: P1=$0.70 + P2=$0.70 = $1.40.,1,N/R,No contribution variable measured.,1,N/R,Only punishment and cheating choices are outcomes.,1,N/R,"Paper discusses punishment rates, not efficiency metrics.",1,N/R,No aggregate group payoff results are provided.,1,N/R,Country distribution for AMT workers not provided.,0,"16–69, mean 29",Overall age stats given; not broken down by treatment.,0.9,"361