e stats available.,0.8,Mostly undergraduate university students from various disciplines,Stated for whole sample.,0.9,On site,Laboratory setting.,1,"Linear public goods game without punishment but with symmetric between-group competition: in each pair of groups (8+8), higher total contributors gain and lower total contributors lose twice the contribution difference, divided equally among group members; contributions and earnings feedback plus opposing group total contributions provided after each period; no punishment or reward stage.",Captures symmetric competition structure when neither group can punish.,1
