10.1111_j.1542-4774.2011.01059.x.md,Third-party punishment two-way sequential,Described as 'Third Party Sequential' in Table 1 and 'two-way sequential TPP treatment' in text.,1,"Punishment opportunities: two-way sequential TPP (both groups can punish within and across groups; one group moves first, other observes total TPP by each first-mover before punishing)",Design: each participant can punish any other; one group makes TPP choices first and second group observes how much each first-mover spent on TPP before deciding.,1,True,Lab experiment with human subjects.,1,True,Controlled sequential vs simultaneous treatments.,1,True,Computer lab at Middlebury.,1,False,No mention of purely simulated agents.,1,False,Empirical contribution.,1,4,Groups of four.,1,1,One-shot game.,1,1,Flexible contribution amounts.,0.9,0,Endowment fully in private account initially.,1,0.5,Same MPCR across all treatments.,1,0,No chat or communication allowed.,0.9,1,Feedback after contribution stage identical in all punishment treatments.,1,0,"Anonymity maintained; only aggregate punishment info of first movers shown to second movers, not identities of targets.",0.8,0,No rewards.,1,1,Participants informed experiment is one-shot.,1,1,Two-way sequential TPP includes punishment.,1,1,Same punishment technology: 1 EMU cost per unit punishment.,1,2,Each EMU spent reduces target by 2 EMUs.,1,0,Rewards not available.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism present.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,25,Participants endowed with 25 EMUs.,1,14.5,Mean contribution 14.50/25 = 0.58; we report normalized fraction.,0.6,14.5,Table 1: Contribution = 14.50 EMUs.,1,N/R,No explicit efficiency ratio by treatment.,0.1,N/R,Group payoffs not broken down by treatment.,0.1,United States,Middlebury College location.,0.9,N/R,Age not given.,0.1,Mixed; proportion female 0.30,Table 1: Female = 0.30 in this treatment.,1,Primarily college undergraduates,Sample drawn from Middlebury student body.,0.95,On site,Large lab at Middlebury College.,1,"One-