derived for this heterogeneous technology.,0.3,N/R,Only per-player average earnings seem to be reported; group totals not clearly distinguished.,0.3,Netherlands,Same CentER Lab participant pool as in other treatments.,0.9,N/R,No age statistics reported.,0,50% female,Overall sample composition 50% female; sessions per treatment balanced (3 each).,1,Primarily university students; graduate-level Economics majors excluded,Same recruitment and exclusion criteria as T1.,0.9,On site,Same lab setting at Tilburg University.,1,"Four-person linear VCM with partner matching and heterogeneous productivity: in each group two subjects have MPCR 0.9 and two have MPCR 0.3. Productivity (type A/B) is publicly known and fixed over rounds. Income each round: I_i = 10 - C_i + 0.9 * sum of contributions of high-MPCR players + 0.3 * sum of contributions of low-MPCR players. After each round, subjects see the formula, contributions, and earnings of all members. No punishment stage.",Details from Section 4.2 describing heterogeneous payoffs and information.,1
10.1007_s10645-008-9094-1.md,T3 – Heterogeneous MPCR (0.9 & 0.3) with Monetary Punishment,Treatment 3 described in Section 4.3 and Table 1; same heterogeneous MPCR as T2 but adds a punishment stage.,1,"Productivity structure: heterogeneous MPCR (two players with MPCR 0.9, two with MPCR 0.3); Sanction institution: monetary punishment stage with 1 token cost to punisher and 2-token loss to recipient per point",T3 replicates contribution stage of T2 and varies sanction institution by adding a monetary punishment mechanism with specific cost/impact parameters.,1,True,Human subjects participating in lab experiment.,1,True,Controlled treatment varying availability of punishment.,1,True,Run in CentER Lab as with other treatments.,1,False,No indication of simulated agents.,1,False,Focus is on experimental data.,1,4,Four subjects per group; two high- and two low-MPCR types.,1,15,All treatments share same 15-round partner-matching structure.,1,1,Subjects choose integer tokens 0–10 to contribute.,1,0,10 tokens are initially private and then can be allocated to public account.,1,0.6,Average MPCR across four members equals 0.6 (two at 0.9 and two at 0.3).,1,0,Communication strictly forbidden; same protocol for all treatments.,1,1,"End-of-stage display shows each member’s contributions, total points sent/received by ego, and incomes; at minimum, ego observes all contributions and their own sanction information.",0.9,0,Random ID reassignment each period and explicit statement that agents do not know individual punishment sent by a specific player; thus identities of punishers are not revealed.,1,0,No reward mechanism exists.,1,1,"Game has a fixed, known 15-period horizon.",0.6,1,T3 added a punishment stage where subjects could send points to reduce others’ earnings.,1,1,Every point sent costs the punisher one token.,1,2,Every point sent reduces the recipient’s earnings by two tokens.,1,0,Only a costly punishment mechanism is described; no opportunity to award bonuses.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,10,Same 10-token per-round endowment as other treatments.,1,0.4933,Text: 'The mean contribution is 18.67% for T2 and 49.33% for T3.',1,N/R,"Only contribution percentages reported (e.g., 49.33% of endowment); average tokens per period not directly computed in the paper.",0,N/R,Average earnings in different period ranges discussed qualitatively; exact normalized efficiency vs. maximum cooperation-without-punishment not provided.,0.3,N/R,Paper reports comparisons of average earnings between treatments and over periods but not a single summary group payoff number for T3.,0.3,Netherlands,Same university lab and subject pool as other treatments.,0.9,N/R,No age info reported.,0,50% female,Overall sample 50% female across nine sessions.,1,Primarily university students; graduate-level Economics majors excluded,Same recruitment protocol as T1/T2.,0.9,On site,"Laboratory sessions at CentER Lab, Tilburg University.",1,"Same four-person heterogeneous-productivity VCM as T2, but with an additional punishment stage each round. Stage 1: players simultaneously choose contributions from 0–10 tokens. Stage 2: after learning others’ contributions, each subject may send 0–10 'points' to each of the three group members; each point costs the sender 1 token and reduces the recipient’s payoff by 2 tokens. Income in T3: I_i = 10 − C_i + 0.9 * sum of contributions of high-MPCR players + 0.3 * sum of contributions of low-MPCR players − sum_{k≠i} P_{ik} − 2 * sum_{k≠i} P_{ki}. Random anonymized IDs 1–4 re-assigned each period prevent tracking of specific individuals over time. End-of-stage feedback shows each subject their own type, all group members’ contributions, total punishment points sent and received, and the calculation of their own income.",Synthesized from Section 4.3 description of T3’s two-stage structure and feedback.,1
