iency.",0,N/R,Group payoff per period not tabulated by treatment-phase.,0,USA,Brown University location.,1,N/R,Only ‘undergraduate’ mentioned.,0.3,N/R,Not reported.,0,Undergraduate university students,Same pool as other treatments.,1,On site,Lab at Brown.,1,"FS phase of 4 periods. Each period: subjects first vote whether to fine allocations to private or public account, then choose a sanction rate from {0,0.4,0.8,1.2}; the median rate is implemented. After observing others’ contributions, automatic fines are applied: for each unit allocated to the sanctioned account, the individual loses r points, with additionally 1/3 of total fines charged to group and shared equally; fines cannot exceed first-stage earnings; fixed cost f=0 in this treatment.",Summarized from FS description and earnings Eq. (3); f=0 for N treatments.,1
