n site,Lab-based at Vernon Smith Experimental Economics Laboratory.,1,"Common pool resource game: each subject allocates 12 tokens between private account (return α=2 per token) and group account representing extraction effort. Total group payoff from group account: F(G)=18G−0.4G^2; each subject’s share: (g_i/G)F(G). Quadratic CPR as in Ostrom et al. Nash total group extraction G*=[n/(n+1)](a−w)/b with n=4,a=18,w=2,b=0.4, giving G*=32 (8 per subject); social optimum G^s.o.=(a−w)/(2b)=20 (5 per subject).",From CPR payoff function description and parameter explanation.,1
