ns 1 unit budget increases cooperator payoff by 1.,1,1,Initial endowment B = 1 from Fig. 1 and Methods.,1,N/R,They inspect fraction of cooperators k/Z but do not provide numerical summary values per condition.,0.6,N/R,"Individual contribution is c·B = 0.1, but total/group contributions are not summarized as DV per condition.",0.7,N/R,No explicit measure of payoff efficiency relative to maximum is tabulated.,0.5,N/R,They focus on group achievement η_G; no raw group payoff numbers per condition.,0.5,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,"Condition is part of a computational model, not an empirical environment.",1,"Collective-risk dilemma with population size Z = 50, group size N = 10, cost of cooperation c = 0.1, endowment B = 1, reward budget per group N·δ with δ = 0.025 and w = 1, risk r varied, thresholds M = 3 and M = 7 depending on panel, intensity of selection β = 5, mutation rate μ = 0.01.","Taken from Fig. 1 caption and Methods, specifying parameters for pure-Reward analyses.",1
