10.1103_PhysRevE.91.022121.md,"Well-mixed population – generic condition (parameters b, α, ρ0)","The paper analyzes a single well-mixed model where outcomes depend on temptation b, punishment fine α, and initial cooperator density ρ0; no discrete named treatments, so this row summarizes that condition family.",0.7,"Temptation to defect b, punishment fine α, initial cooperator density ρ0 (continuous parameters in a well-mixed population PDG with mutual punishment).","Section III derives outcomes ρc as functions of b, α, and ρ0 in a well-mixed (non-structured) population.",1,False,No human or animal subjects; work is theoretical plus numerical simulation.,1,False,No controlled lab/field experiment with participants; only mathematical analysis.,1,False,No lab setting with subjects.,1,False,"For the well-mixed case they use analytical replicator dynamics, not numerical agent-based simulation.",0.9,True,Section III derives closed-form expressions using replicator equation and analyzes equilibria.,1,2,Underlying game is a two-player prisoner's dilemma; well-mixed population interacts pairwise.,0.8,1,Replicator dynamics models infinitely repeated evolutionary process but underlying PDG is single-shot; set as 1 round per encounter.,0.5,1,"Strategies are pure cooperate or defect in each encounter; contribution is binary, encoded as 2-strategy PDG.",1,N/A,No explicit endowment or contribution decision; binary cooperate/defect in PDG without public-good framing.,1,N/R,MPCR concept not used; PDG payoffs specified instead.,1,N/A,"No human subjects, thus no communication.",1,0,No information display to human players; purely analytical model.,1,N/A,No identities; model consists of homogeneous strategies in a population.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in the model.,1,0,No explicit display of rounds to agents in an analytical model.,1,1,Payoff includes −α(1−sx^T sy) term representing mutual punishment.,1,N/R,They state cost is absorbed into the punishment fine; separate cost per unit is 