orld), but no explicit punishment option is implemented in a game.",1,N/A,No implemented punishment mechanism.,1,N/A,No implemented punishment mechanism.,1,0,Rewards/cooperative benefits are discussed as payoffs but not as a selectable game option.,1,N/A,No implemented reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No implemented reward mechanism.,1,0,No tokens/endowments are defined for players in any formal game.,1,N/A,No measurable contributions or rates are reported.,1,N/A,No contribution amounts are part of an implemented experiment.,1,N/R,No empirical or simulated efficiency outcomes are computed.,1,N/R,Only qualitative payoffs and a symbolic inequality pc > m are given; no numerical payoffs.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,The work is purely theoretical/analytical with no human data collection.,1,"No explicit game-theoretic experiment; only a conceptual comparison of three strategies (Ancestrals, Atheists, God-fearers) via an inequality pc > m under Error Management Theory.",Summarizes the only structured strategic content (Table 2) as a conceptual model rather than an implemented game.,1
