tokens; no participant monetary endowment.,0.2,N/R,"Dependent variables are social judgments, not contributions.",1,N/R,No contribution decisions by human subjects.,1,N/R,No payoff-based efficiency metric reported.,1,N/R,No numeric payoffs for participants or agents reported.,1,United States,Participants were American users of Amazon Mechanical Turk.,1,17–76 (median 31),Age range and median reported for Study 1 sample.,1,43% female (remaining presumably male),Gender composition given as 43% female; others not explicitly broken down but implied male.,0.9,N/R,Education levels not described.,0.1,Online,Study 1 conducted as an online experiment via MTurk.,1,"Participants watched an animation of four colored triangles sequentially harvesting circles (resource units) from a common pool; purple violates a turn-taking norm by taking all remaining circles; no one sanctions the norm violation. Participants rated each triangle’s appropriateness, likeability, and whether it would be a problem for the group, plus character traits for blue, on Likert scales; trait aggression was measured afterward.",Summarizes procedural and scenario details specific to this no-sanction condition.,1
