10.1093_restud_rdv040.md,"NT-SP (Neighbourhood Treatment – Self-Protection, n=8)","Treatment NT-SP where neighbourhood choice is one-sided, removing punishment element.",1,"Neighbourhood choice with one-sided links (self-protection only); group size 8; if i proposes to interact with j, j enters i’s neighbourhood regardless of j’s choice; payoffs determined by i’s outgoing links only; same payoff parameters and scaling as NT; full history information.",Section 5.6 describes NT-SP and differences from NT.,0.98,True,"Three sessions, nine groups of 8, lab experiment.",1,True,Controlled manipulation of link technology (self-protection vs mutual consent).,1,True,Conducted at BEElab.,1,False,Human subjects only.,1,False,No analytical-only condition.,1,8,Nine groups of size 8 in NT-SP.,1,30,Same 30-round horizon.,1,1,Effort choice 1–7.,1,0,"Same underlying cost-benefit game as NT, only link externalities altered.",0.6,N/R,Not a standard public-good setting.,1,0,No chat / communication allowed.,1,1,Instructions same as NT except neighbourhood choice; NT had full history for all; NT-SP inherits that.,0.9,0,No punishment decision.,1,0,No reward mechanism.,1,1,Same finite 30-round design.,0.85,0,Design explicitly removes punishment element of exclusion; exclusion does not affect excluded player’s payoff.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism.,1,0,No explicit rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,Same payoff specification as NT; no endowment mentioned.,0.5,N/R,Only effort levels reported.,1,6.76,Mean group average effort in NT-SP is 6.76 (Table 8).,1,N/R,They describe welfare gains qualitatively but do not give a normalized efficiency statistic for NT-SP.,0.7,N/R,Average welfare for NT-SP is not numerically reported; only mean earnings per participant (€16.83). Mapping from euros to points and group sums not explicitly given.,0.4,Netherlands,Conducted at Maastricht University.,0.98,N/R,No age stats reported.,0.4,N/R,Not reported.,1,University 