or Experiment 2.,0.9,81.7% female in Experiment 2; not broken down by role/condition.,Overall sample gender share provided.,0.9,Likely university students; exact info not reported.,Participant pool from the university.,0.6,On site,Tasks done in the lab using psynteract / OpenSesame.,1,"Extended URG identical to other Experiment 2 condition; here, focus is on unfair player 1 allocation (7.5,2.5). Player 2 can select one of four reduction levels (0, 2.5, 5, 7.5 MU). SVO Slider Measure with monetary incentives was administered earlier in the same lab session but is analytically distinct from this retaliation task.",Summarized from Experiment 2 description and SVO/URG procedure.,1
10.1126_sciadv.aau7296.md,"Experiment 1 – Baseline, ci = 40",First experiment without punishment; condition with individual cost ci = 40 listed among five blocks; treated as separate condition.,0.9,"Cost-benefit ratio of individualism i = 1.0 (ci = 40, cc = 160, n = 4), no peer punishment","Paper defines ci levels (40,50,60,70,80) and corresponding i, with fixed cc and group size; Experiment 1 has no punishment stage.",0.95,True,Human participants in computerized experiment at University of Leiden.,1,True,Controlled lab experiment with random assignment and manipulation of costs and punishment.,1,True,"Conducted at University of Leiden lab with computers, not in the field or online.",0.98,False,No agent-based or numerical simulation reported.,1,False,"Although theoretical motivation exists, this condition describes behavioral experiment, not purely analytical model.",0.95,4,Participants randomly allocated to groups of four (40 groups in total).,1,10,Ten rounds of allocation before final outcome evaluation.,1,1,"Participants could freely distribute 10 RPs among options each round, not all-or-nothing.",1,0,Endowment is given as private RPs; participants must actively invest into individual or shared pools.,0.95,N/R,Public pool threshold cc = 160 for 4 players but no multiplier or per capita return per unit contributed is specified.,0.2,0,No mention of communication; standard anonymous computer interaction.,0.9,1,"After each round, participants saw accumulated RPs in public and individual pools and others’ allocation decisions.",1,0,No punishment stage in baseline; identity revelation of punishment not applicable but coded 0 as there is no mechanism.,0.7,0,No reward mechanism described.,1,1,Instructions state 10th and final round; typical design implies participants know total rounds; also figures show threshold announcement at start of block.,0.8,0,Punishment introduced only in second experiment; this is first experiment baseline.,1,N/A,No punishment option in this condition.,1,N/A,No punishment option in this condition.,1,0,No rewarding or positive point assignment described.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism present.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism present.,1,10,Each group member received 10 RPs in each round.,1,N/R,"Paper reports qualitative strategy shares, not average fraction of endowment invested per round or overall.",0.2,N/R,"Only thresholds (ci, cc) and some aggregate wasted resources are given; no average raw contributions by condition.",0.2,N/R,"They discuss waste and potential savings, but no explicit normalized efficiency values per condition.",0.3,N/R,Average group earnings per condition are not reported in main text.,0.2,Netherlands,Experiment conducted at University of Leiden in the Netherlands; participants likely local subject pool.,0.9,N/R,Only states that participants answered demographic questions such as age; no summary statistics provided.,0.1,N/R,"Demographic questions include gender, but no distribution reported.",0.1,University students,"Experiment at university lab; typical pool is students, and they report field of study in demographics.",0.7,On site,Described as computerized experiment at the university; no indication of online participation.,0.95,Dynamic threshold public-good-like game with both individual and collective targets; 5 blocks with varying individual threshold ci = 40–80; this condition uses ci = 40 and fixed public threshold cc = 160. Participants keep RPs kept for themselves if either their individual pool ≥ ci or group public pool ≥ cc after 10 rounds; otherwise they lose all kept RPs. One block randomly selected for payment; each RP worth €0.08 plus €6.50 show-up and payment from SVO task.,"Summarized from Materials and Methods and main text description, specific to cost parameter for this condition.",1
