mate 0.60 recorded.",0.4,6,Using approximate 60% cooperation on 10 Kina endowment gives average contribution 6 Kina.,0.4,N/R,"Although payoffs including punishment costs are compared, efficiency ratio (payoff/max) for this treatment is not provided.",0.3,N/R,Only average individual payoff comparisons are given; PUN payoff not numerically specified in excerpt.,0.3,Papua New Guinea,Same Teop participant pool.,1,Adults; exact age distribution N/R,No detailed age statistics in excerpt.,0.4,Mixed; exact split in PUN treatment N/R,Only overall gender composition is reported.,0.7,Varied; education level used as control; per-treatment distribution N/R,Only summary effect reported.,0.5,Field experiment,Same field context in Teop as other treatments.,1,"After the one-shot PD decision with Endowment I, participants have a punishment stage where each can spend K0, K2, or K4 from Endowment II (K4) to reduce counterpart’s payoff by K0, K10, or K20. Strategy method used: each participant specifies punishment decisions conditional on whether the other kept or gave K10.",Described in 'We modelled altruistic punishment' section.,1
