 9.32/20 = 0.466.,0.95,9.32,Table 2: Contribution Baseline = 9.32 (SD 7.77).,1,N/R,No explicit report of average efficiency or total payoffs relative to maximum.,0,N/R,"Only individual mean contributions and some earnings examples reported, not average group payoff.",0,France,"Sessions conducted at GATE in Lyon, France; subjects recruited from local schools.",1,N/R,Described only as undergraduates; no age statistics provided.,0.3,41.67% male,Procedures section: 48 subjects of whom 41.67% were males; same pool across treatments.,1,Undergraduate students in local business and engineering schools,Recruitment described as from undergraduate courses in local business and engineering schools.,1,On site,Physical laboratory experiments at GATE with electrodes and lab computers.,1,"Standard linear public goods (VCM) with partner matching, groups of 4, 20 ECU per period, return per contributed ECU = 0.4 to each member, 20 periods, full feedback on individual contributions each round. Emotions measured via skin conductance and 10-point valence self-reports at decision and feedback moments.","Summarized from Experimental Design, Skin Conductance Response Acquisition, and Procedures sections for Baseline (no second-stage sanctions).",1
