,1,100,Same theft parameters (steal half endowment = U_i = 50 MU) as other conditions.,0.95,N/R,"Study reports defection and punishment rates, not normalized contributions.",1,N/R,No aggregate MU contributions presented.,1,N/R,"Efficiency discussed only qualitatively (e.g., efficient punishment by one person) without numeric efficiency indices.",1,N/R,Only overall average earnings (CHF 38) across experiment; no condition-specific group payoff.,0.4,Switzerland,Same Swiss university student pool.,0.95,"Mean 23.1 years (sd = 5.57), university students",Single pool used for all conditions.,1,57.9% female,Reported once for entire sample.,1,University students (University of Zurich and ETH Zurich),Subjects recruited from university subject pool.,1,On site,Computerized lab experiment at DeSciL.,1,"Same 4-player thief/punishment structure as MHD conditions, but here U_i > K_i: stealing yields 50 MU taken from each of three victims; any non-thief can choose to punish (reclaim) at cost K_i = 25 MU. If at least one punishes, endowments are restored; from round 16 the thief also pays penalty P = 60 MU. Groups are randomly rematched every round; roles randomly determined.",Summarized from VOD definition and Table 1 for symmetric VOD.,1
