e target.",1,2,Authority pays a cost of 2 tokens to target a group member for enforcement.,1,30,"If enforcement is successful, the targeted group member pays a penalty of 30 tokens.",1,0,Design only includes penalties for targeted citizens; no rewarding institution.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Each citizen has an endowment of 20 tokens each period; salaried authority receives fixed 20-token salary per period (distinct from citizen endowment).,1,N/R,Paper reports average number of contributors per group (2.46 per period) but not normalized fraction per individual across the entire treatment.,0.6,N/R,Only binary contribute/keep decisions reported; no aggregate number of tokens contributed per person across all periods.,0.3,N/R,No explicit measure of realized vs. maximum possible group payoff is reported.,0.1,N/R,"Average citizen and authority earnings per period in dollars are reported, but not aggregated to group payoffs in tokens or dollars.",0.4,United States,Experiment conducted at NYU (New York University) with undergraduates from a local subject pool in the U.S.,0.9,Undergraduate students; exact ages N/R,Participants recruited from a preexisting pool of undergraduate subjects; no specific age statistics provided.,0.8,N/R,Gender composition is not reported; only note is that balance checks were done on sex but not the distribution itself.,0.3,Primarily university undergraduates,Subjects are drawn from an undergraduate pool and are not recruited from authors’ courses.,0.9,On site,Conducted in a physical lab (NYU CESS) with subjects at networked computers.,1,"Linear public goods game with 4 citizens and 1 authority; citizens choose binary contribute/keep from 20 tokens; pot is multiplied by 0.4 and shared among all 5 players; authority decides whether to target one citizen at cost 2; baseline enforcement success probability 0.5, adjusted by ±1/6 per helping/hindering citizen (up to 0 or 1); successful enforcement yields 30-token penalty to target; authority receives fixed salary of 20 tokens per period and also 0.4 share of public good; no communication; repeated for 20 periods with fixed roles but citizen IDs randomly reassigned each period.","Summarizes key structural elements of the extensive-form game described in the protocol, specific to the salary and full information condition where citizens observe all contributions and who is targeted.",1
