ncy metric.,0.1,N/R,"Period earnings per role reported only in dollars (citizens: $0.67; authorities: $0.72), not summed to group payoff.",0.4,United States,Same subject pool at NYU in the U.S.,0.9,Undergraduate students; exact ages N/R,Recruited from undergraduate pool; no age stats provided.,0.8,N/R,"Sex used as a balance covariate, but actual distribution not reported.",0.3,Primarily university undergraduates,Same recruitment pool.,0.9,On site,Run in a lab using networked computers.,1,"Same extensive-form structure as in salary treatment: 4 citizens with 20 tokens each choose contribute/keep; authority observes contributions; can target one citizen at cost 2; prior success probability 0.5 adjusted by ±1/6 per helper/hinderer; successful enforcement costs target 30 tokens; in this treatment, authority has no fixed salary but instead receives 30 tokens for each successful sanction, plus 0.4 share of public good; full information on all contributions and target ID is provided to citizens before they choose whether to help or hinder.",Summarizes game rules highlighting difference in compensation and full transparency for this condition.,1
