e for this condition.",0.5,N/R,Raw tokens contributed per person not tabulated.,0.3,N/R,No group efficiency figure is reported.,0.1,N/R,"Average per-period earnings are reported (citizens $0.54, authorities $0.71) but not converted to group totals.",0.4,United States,Same lab and recruitment pool.,0.9,Undergraduate students; exact ages N/R,Subjects from an undergraduate pool.,0.8,N/R,Only balance on sex is discussed; no actual shares.,0.3,Primarily university undergraduates,Same as other treatments.,0.9,On site,In-person sessions at NYU CESS.,1,"Game structure identical to salary/full information except that untargeted citizens, after authority targets someone, observe only that targeting occurred (not who was targeted or any individual contributions). They later learn the group’s total contribution level at end of period. Public good and enforcement technologies remain unchanged; authority receives fixed 20-token salary and 0.4 share of public good.","Highlights that the only difference from salary/full information is the informational environment faced by citizens; enforcement, payoffs, and repetition remain the same.",1
