simulated here; only spectral and structural network properties.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Numerical computations on synthetic networks.,1,"Watts-Strogatz networks with n=2000 and average degree ⟨k⟩=10 are generated for various rewiring probabilities in [0,1]. For each network, the largest eigenvalue λ̃_n of the normalized Laplacian is computed and selfishness tolerance 1/λ̃_n is plotted versus rewiring probability. Inset shows normalized average path length and clustering coefficient vs rewiring probability, indicating that selfishness tolerance is positively related to both path length and clustering.",Describes the topological analysis as stated in Fig. 4.,1
