10.1177_1474704917742720.md,"Study 2 – Offense, labor sufficient",This row captures responses to the offensive vignette in Study 2 when labor is described as sufficient.,1,Conflict domain = Offense; Labor condition = Sufficient (current eager volunteers should be enough to seize a city even if reluctant people do not join).,"Offense vignette has added text: “the current amount of eager volunteers should be enough to seize a city, even if the reluctant people do not join the war party.”",1,True,Human-subject survey experiment.,1,True,"Manipulated offense vs. defense within subjects, labor sufficiency between subjects.",1,True,Same on-site undergraduate setting.,0.8,False,No simulations.,1,False,No purely analytical work.,1,1,Individual decision in hypothetical scenario.,1,1,Single evaluation of each vignette by each subject.,1,1,"Likert-scale willingness, not all-or-nothing.",0.9,0,No explicit endowment; same assumption as other conditions.,0.3,N/R,No marginal per capita return structure.,1,0,No communication in the survey task.,1,0,No feedback about others' responses.,1,0,Punishment is hypothetical/attitudinal only.,1,0,Reward is hypothetical only.,1,0,No multiple rounds.,1,0,No real punishment option.,1,N/A,Not applicable.,1,N/A,Not applicable.,1,0,No real rewarding option.,1,N/A,Not applicable.,1,N/A,Not applicable.,1,N/R,No numeric endowment specified.,1,N/R,No numeric contribution data.,1,N/R,No contribution amounts.,1,N/R,No efficiency metric.,1,N/R,No quantified group payoff.,1,USA,Same Study 2 undergraduate sample in a U.S. context.,0.7,N/R,Age distribution not provided for Study 2.,0.2,"74 male, 114 female (total N = 188)",Entire Study 2 sample.,1,Undergraduate university students,Stated explicitly.,1,On site,Same setting as other Study 2 conditions.,0.8,"Study 2 offense vignette with labor-sufficient cue: text indicates that existing eager volunteers are enough to seize a city even if reluctant people do not join. Measures focus on willingness to participat