10.1016_j.obhdp.2016.02.004.md,Experiment 1 – Individual responsibility – Punishment,Condition defined by Responsibility (Individual) × Sanction Type (Punishment) in Experiment 1.,1,Responsibility = Individual; Sanction Type = Punishment (fixed fine equal to 10 chips harvested by Person C),Paper describes a 2 (Responsibility: Individual vs Joint) × 2 (Sanction Type: Punishment vs Reward) design; this row is the Individual–Punishment cell.,1,True,Human student participants at Leiden University performed decisions in a lab task.,1,True,Random assignment to conditions and controlled manipulation of responsibility and sanction type.,1,True,Conducted in a laboratory; participants seated in separate cubicles with computers.,1,False,No agent-based or computational simulations; only human subjects.,1,False,No formal mathematical modeling as a standalone method.,1,4,Common resource task was performed with three fellow participants (4 persons total).,1,1,Single one-shot common resource decision followed by one sanction decision; no repetition reported.,0.9,1,"Participants could harvest any number of chips from 0 to 10; contributions/harvest are continuous, not binary all-or-nothing.",1,0,"All 10 chips per person are initially in the common pool; private account starts at zero, so no initial endowment in private account.",0.7,0.5,"Chips left in pool are doubled (multiplied by 2) and divided among 4 players, so MPCR = 2/4 = 0.5.",1,0,No communication or chat mentioned; only private computer-based decisions.,0.9,0,Participants only see Person C’s harvest; no summaries of others’ payoffs or sanctions are described.,0.7,0,Sanction target is labeled as Person C and other participants are anonymous; no identities revealed for who punishes.,0.8,0,Same anonymity structure; no information that identities of rewarders would be revealed.,0.8,0,One-shot setting; no information about number of rounds displayed.,0.9,1,Punishment condition allows assigning a fine to Person C.,1,0,Sanctions could be administered without any cost to participants (“even though participants could administer the sanction without any cost to themselves”).,1,10,"Fine equals the number of chips Person C harvested; Person C harvests 10 chips, so punishment reduces payoff by 10 chips if applied (technology: 10 chips lost per sanction decision).",0.8,0,"This is the punishment condition; only a fine is possible, no bonus.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism in this condition.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in this condition.,1,10,Each person could harvest up to 10 chips from the common pool; treated as per-person resource endowment.,0.9,N/R,Only overall average harvest (2.92/10) is reported across all conditions; no condition-specific contribution fraction given.,0,N/R,Mean harvest is pooled across all four cells; condition-specific contribution amounts not reported.,0,N/R,No efficiency measure or total payoffs by condition are reported.,0,N/R,Group earnings are not broken out by condition beyond stating an additional €1 from the task.,0,Netherlands,Participants were students at Leiden University in the Netherlands.,1,"M = 21.22, SD = 4.62 (student sample)",Age distribution reported for Experiment 1 sample.,1,"111 women, 54 men",Gender breakdown reported for Experiment 1.,1,University students,All participants were students at Leiden University.,1,On site,Participants came to the laboratory and were seated in cubicles.,1,"One-shot common pool (common resource) game with 4 players, 40 chips in pool, each can harvest 0–10 chips; remaining chips doubled and split equally. After harvests, participant decides individually whether to impose a fixed punishment (fine equal to 10 chips harvested by non-cooperative Person C who took 10) at no personal cost.",Summarizes described task structure and sanction implementation for this condition.,1
