ter.,0.95,N/R,Text reports that altruism does not evolve from A=0 but provides no numeric steady-state contribution rates.,0.2,N/R,No explicit contributions in tokens reported.,0.2,N/R,Outcome is described qualitatively (altruism does not evolve) without efficiency numbers.,0.1,N/R,No group payoff data are given.,0.1,N/A,No human participants in simulation.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Condition is within a computational evolutionary simulation.,1,"Same grouping, contribution, and reproduction process as other runs, but punishment is disabled by setting D=0 so cheaters, once detected, cannot be removed; authors note that under this condition altruism does not evolve from an all-selfish starting population.",Summarized from the description in Section 3.1 comparing D>0 vs. D=0.,0.9
