.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Simulation scenarios only.,1,"Same three-player evolutionary game and baseline structural parameters. Multiple policy tools are jointly adjusted: (i) increase ecological weight δ2 and reduce economic weight δ1 in LG performance appraisal, (ii) increase punishment F on LGs that only partially implement policies, (iii) impose and increase marine ecological damage compensation φ, and (iv) increase fines D on SEs for partial compliance. Under parameter combinations satisfying conditions (λ2−1)(C2+δ1L−δ2E)+λ1F>0 and (λ3−1)C3+(1−λ3)φQ2+D+γS>0, the system converges to ESS E7(0,1,1): CG irregular partial supervision, LGs full implementation, SEs full compliance. Figure 6 shows that higher F and higher δ2 (lower δ1) speed convergence of y→1, while higher φ and D accelerate z→1. x remains at 0 (irregular partial supervision), indicating that proper policy mix can induce cooperative behavior of LGs and SEs even without strict CG supervision.",Synthesizes description of combined-policy simulations in 4.3.5 and the formal ESS condition for E7.,1
