liance strength under partial compliance). Example case: λ1=0.2, λ2=0.3, λ3=0.4. Results (Fig. 10) show that changing λ1, λ2, λ3 does not alter the final equilibrium state (still x→0, y→1, z→1), but affects convergence speeds: increasing λ1 slows CG’s convergence to x=0 yet speeds up LGs’ convergence to full implementation; increasing λ2 slows LGs’ convergence to full implementation but leaves CG and SE convergence speeds largely unchanged; increasing λ3 accelerates SEs’ convergence to full compliance. Thus the ESS is robust, but transient dynamics depend on implementation strengths.",Summarizes sensitivity analysis in 4.4.2 and Fig. 10.,1
10.1016_j.jtbi.2008.09.004.md,"Lattice-structured population, evolving c, c0, p0 with fixed punishment strictness s",Paper describes a simulation condition where s is fixed and other traits evolve in a lattice-structured population; treated as one condition aggregated over varying s values.,0.7,"Population structure: lattice-structured; punishment strictness s fixed (varied across separate simulation runs: s = 0.5, 1, 5, 10, 1000)","Methods and Fig. 1 text specify lattice-structured population and that punishment strictness s is fixed at different values across runs while c, c0, p0 evolve.",0.9,False,Model is an individual-based evolutionary simulation with no human or animal participants.,1,False,Not a controlled human/field experiment; purely theoretical/simulation study.,1,False,No laboratory with human subjects; computational model only.,1,True,"Described as an individual-based model with stochastic birth/death events and mutation, implemented on a lattice.",1,False,"Main condition here is numerical simulation, not closed-form analysis.",1,900,"Square lattice 30×30 sites; text implies each site is a potential individual location. Although 50% are empty initially, the structural player count is 30×30.",0.6,0,Continuous-time birth-death process with asynchronous events; no discrete rounds.,1,1,"Cooperation level c is a continuous non-negative trait, not restricted to all-or-nothing.",1,N/A,No human endowments or stage-game contributions; continuous investment model without an endowment split.,1,N/R,No public goods multiplier or per-capita return is defined; benefits enter via increased birth rate b_i depending on neighbors’ c_j.,1,N/A,"No human subjects, hence no communication protocol.",1,0,Agents do not observe earnings summaries; interactions depend only on local trait values.,1,0,No identities or information structure analogous to human experiments; punishment is modeled mechanistically.,1,0,No rewards or IDs in the simulation.,1,0,Agents are not informed abou