10.1016_j.jtbi.2008.09.004.md,Well-mixed population analytical model (no joint evolution of cooperation and punishment),Appendix analytically examines a well-mixed population and shows that cooperation and punishment cannot evolve.,0.95,"Population structure: well-mixed; traits c, c0, p0, s subject to selection analyzed analytically under rare-mutant invasion","Appendix explicitly states 'well-mixed populations' and derives selection gradients for c, c0, p0, s.",1,False,Pure mathematical analysis with no subjects.,1,False,Not an experiment; analytical derivation.,1,False,No experimental lab setting.,1,False,"Appendix focuses on analytical expressions, not simulations.",1,True,Derives selection gradients and equilibrium frequencies using calculus and standard adaptive dynamics framework.,1,N/R,Analytical model treats population frequencies in the limit; no explicit finite player count specified.,0.7,0,Continuous-time differential equation model; no rounds.,1,1,"Traits like cooperation level c are continuous, not binary.",1,N/A,No economic endowments; continuous trait model.,1,N/R,No MPCR defined; benefits via terms in birth rate.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,0,No information structure; only frequencies and traits matter analytically.,1,0,No identities; analytical population model.,1,0,No rewards discussed.,1,0,No rounds in analytical dynamics.,1,1,Model includes punishment reaction norms p(c) and associated cost function C_p(p); then shows selection drives p0 to 0.,1,N/R,Cost function C_p(p)=a_p p^{e_p} is referenced but specific parameter values for well-mixed case are not provided in appendix.,0.5,N/R,"Punishment impacts fitness via analytic expressions, not a discrete technology scalar.",0.5,0,No rewards considered analytically.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No endowment concept.,1,N/R,Appendix concludes selection drives c to 0 but does not frame it as a normalized contribution rate.,0.7,N/R,Analytical result is qualitative (c evolves to 0) rather than a numeric equilibrium amount reported as data for a specific parameter set.,0.7,N/R,No efficiency calculation given.,1,N/R,Only growth rates and selection gradients are analyzed.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Pure mathematical analysis.,1,"Analytical invasion analysis of a rare mutant (c', p'(·)) in a resident population (c, p(·)) in a well-mixed setting. Variant’s per capita growth rate f' is derived, and selection gradients g_c, g_{c0}, g_{p0}, g_s are computed using adaptive dynamics methods. Resident equilibrium frequency \hat{x} is obtained from balance of birth and death rates: (b0 + c \hat{x})(1-\hat{x}) = d0 + [p(c) + C_p(p(c)) + C_c(c)] \hat{x}. Selection gradient expressions show g_{p0} < 0, driving p0 to 0, after which g_{c0}=g_s=0 and g_c<0, leading to c→0. Concludes that in well-mixed populations, costly cooperation and punishment cannot jointly evolve.",Based on Appendix derivations and narrative summary.,1
