ion all periods is 17.2 EDs (Table 3) out of 50 ED endowment: 17.2 / 50 = 0.344.,1,17.2,"Table 3: Homogeneous, No Pun., All periods = 17.2 EDs.",1,0.9,"Text: Average earnings in HomPun are 90% of what they are in HomNoPun; implies HomNoPun efficiency baseline = 1 and HomPun = 0.9. So HomNoPun efficiency normalized to 1.0; but they report 90% in HomPun relative to HomNoPun, and nothing about max-theoretical. To avoid fabrication, set HomNoPun efficiency to N/R instead. Correction: use N/R.",0,N/R,Only individual monetary earnings per subject are reported; no aggregate group payoff given.,0.2,United States,"Subjects recruited from University of Massachusetts Amherst, located in the U.S.",1,N/R,No age information provided; only that subjects are students.,0,Proportion male: 0.47,"Table 2: Homogeneous, No punishment: Male = 0.47.",1,"University students (undergraduate/graduate, specific level N/R)",Subjects recruited from the student population; no further breakdown.,0.8,On site,Standard physical lab experiment with students; on-site sessions in May 2012.,0.9,"Non-linear interior-solution public good; payoff: π_i = w(e_i - x_i) + (1/n)[a Σx_j - b(Σx_j)^2] with w=1, a=6, b=0.025, n=4. Symmetric Nash contribution 10 EDs, social optimum 25 EDs each (Σx=100). Aggregate group endowment fixed at 200 EDs. Information feedback after each period includes own and others’ contributions and earnings.",Summarized from Section 2 and payoff function description.,1
