ficiency is given.",0,N/R,Group payoffs not quantified.,0,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Analytical evolutionary game model.,1,"Strategy H (hybrid-punisher) pays both G to punishment pool and γ to punish defectors, and contributes c to public good; not punished by central authority. For M=100, stationary distribution over (X,Y,Z,V,W,C,H) is [0.001, 0.004, 0.008, 0.013, 0.004, 0.007, 0.96], indicating near dominance of hybrids and high cooperation across all levels of centralized punishment.",Directly from text with brief paraphrase.,1
