 numeric average efficiency by treatment reported.,0.2,N/R,No explicit average group payoff per treatment in text.,0.2,Canada,Same subject pool and lab as baseline treatment.,1,N/R,Only 'undergraduate students' specified.,0.3,N/R,No gender breakdown provided.,0,Undergraduate university students,Stated for the entire experiment.,1,On site,Conducted in a physical laboratory using z-Tree.,1,"Same linear VCM as baseline. Added Stage 2: after seeing all contributions, each subject can assign 0–6 disapproval points (integers) to each of 3 others, up to 18 total; points are anonymous, costless, and do not affect payoffs; subjects see aggregate disapproval each member received alongside contributions.",Summarizes specific extension (non-pecuniary punishment) beyond baseline.,1
