 contribution variable.,1,N/R,Paper does not quantify efficiency numerically in this case; only describes strategic outcome.,0.5,N/R,No numeric aggregate payoff under this parameter set is reported.,0.6,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Simulation-only condition.,1,"Replicator dynamics for x_t (probability local government chooses strong implementation) and y_t (probability MWR chooses strong supervision) simulated in Matlab with η=0.2, σ=0.4, π_i=10, c_i=20, ω=0.5, m=0.3, P=2, M=3, ε=3. Inequalities σc_i−(ε+ηπ_i)>P and ωP>mM hold. Four different initial conditions (0.8,0.3), (0.3,0.8), (0.8,0.8), (0.3,0.3) all converge to equilibrium (0,1): local government weak implementation, MWR strong supervision.",Summarizes the specific numerical case I as described around Fig. 3.,1
