ducted in physical economics lab.,1,"Same Piracy Game core: 4 consumers, 1 record label with 32-song inventory; 8-token consumer endowment and 2 initial songs; buy yields net 0.1 tokens, download yields 0.5 tokens; no parents in this advice channel; advice from record label sent via computer after rounds 8 and 14 with info on its earnings, group piracy, and moral statements about piracy.",Only advice source differs; incentives and timing remain as described in implementation.,1
10.2753_mis0742-1222310208.md,REG – Industry regulator advice treatment,Condition where the advice source is an external regulator; labeled REG in Table 1.,1,Source of advice: External regulator with no social tie and no stake in the game.,Table 1 cell with ‘No social tie’ and ‘No stake in the game’ is Industry regulator (REG).,1,True,Lab experiment with human consumers and record-label subjects; regulator role played by experimenter.,1,True,Randomized treatment in controlled environment.,1,True,Run in Vernon Smith Experimental Economics Laboratory.,1,False,Not a simulation-only study.,1,False,Empirical data from human play.,1,4,Groups in all treatments have 4 music consumers.,1,20,Each session has 20 rounds.,1,1,"Free choice each click within 25 seconds, not all-or-nothing.",1,0,All 8 tokens start privately for each consumer.,0.8,N/A,Not a linear PGG.,1,0,“Communication between subjects was not allowed”; advice only from administrator as regulator.,1,1,Advice includes group-average piracy and label earnings.,0.9,0,No punishment mechanism in REG.,1,0,No rewards mechanism.,1,1,Total number of rounds known to subjects.,0.8,0,Neither parents nor regulator incur/take endogenous punishment in this treatment.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism.,1,0,No rewarding.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,8,Each consumer receives 8 tokens every round in all treatments.,1,N/R,No normalized contribution metric reported.,0,2.36,"From Table 6, REG treatment rounds 9–20: average songs purchased per consumer = 2.36.",0.95,N/R,Efficiency not computed in the paper.,0.2,N/R,Only record label profit and average purchases/piracy are reported.,0.2,United States,Same Purdue University lab setting.,0.9,Primarily university-age for consumers and record labels,Subjects in non-parent treatments recruited via lab’s online system; typical undergraduates and seniors.,0.7,N/R,No gender information.,0,University students,Recruitment from experimental economics lab subject pool at Purdue; record labels specified as senior students.,0.9,On site,Laboratory environment with physical computers.,1,"Same core Piracy Game: 4 consumers, 1 record label; 25-second continuous decision rounds; 8-token and 2-song consumer endowment; payoffs for buying (1.1−1) and pirating (0.5) per song; external regulator (played by experiment administrator) sends standardized advice via computer after rounds 8 and 14 with info about group piracy and label earnings plus moral statements; regulator has no monetary stake.","REG differs only in the non-staked, non-tied advice source; game rules and parameters unchanged.",1
10.1016_j.tpb.2006.01.003.md,Reward Model – deterministic recursion system,Paper defines a distinct analytical model labeled 'Reward model' with its own recursion system and parameters.,1,"Costs and benefits: s (cost of observing norm), π (cost of being punished for violation), γ (cost of punishing), ρ (reward for punishing), δ (cost of rewarding), ξ (probability of internalization); phenotype frequencies X11, X12, X21, X22",These parameters and phenotype frequencies are varied symbolically to study system behavior in the Reward Model.,1,False,Model contains no human participants; it is a theoretical population model.,1,False,No controlled experiment; purely mathematical/replicator dynamics model.,1,False,No lab or field setting; only equations.,1,False,"This specific component is presented as analytic recursions and local stability analysis, not as a numerical Monte Carlo or agent-based run.",0.9,True,Section 2.1 and subsequent analysis derive and study closed-form recursion equations and equilibria.,1,0,No discrete game with a fixed number of players; infinite population approximation is used.,1,0,Generational or discrete-time dynamics without a finite repeated-game horizon.,1,1,No contribution decision structure is modeled; cooperation is encoded as norm adoption and punishment traits in a population-genetic style model.,0.5,N/A,No endowment or contribution mechanism; not a public goods game with contributions.,1,N/R,"No marginal per capita return is defined; payoffs are fitness effects from costs and rewards, not a linear public-good multiplier.",1,N/A,No human subjects or strategic communication modeled.,1,N/A,No user interface or feedback mechanism; theoretical model only.,1,N/A,No identities or information structure; only aggregate frequencies.,1,N/A,Identity of rewarders/punishers is not modeled.,1,N/A,No participant interface or awareness of time horizon.,1,1,Core of the model is punishment of norm-violators with cost γ and penalty π.,1,N/R,"Punishment cost is represented symbolically as γ per act, but not in game tokens; schema expects numeric game cost, not applicable here.",0.7,N/R,Magnitude of punishment per unit cost (technology) is not parameterized separately from π and γ.,0.5,1,Reward Model explicitly assumes norm-observers reward punishers; benefit ρ and cost δ.,1,N/R,"Reward cost is δ per act in fitness units, but no numeric token value or exchange rate is given.",0.7,N/R,No separate reward technology factor beyond δ and ρ.,0.5,N/A,"No per-period endowment; model is framed in terms of viability (fitness), not monetary payoffs.",1,N/R,"Outcome variables are frequencies of phenotypes and mean fitness, not contribution rates in a public goods game.",1,N/R,No contributions measured.,1,N/R,No explicit efficiency ratio (total payoff relative to maximum) is reported.,1,N/R,"Model tracks mean viability, but no specific numeric group payoff amount is given.",1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely theoretical analytical model.,1,"Analytical cultural evolution model with four phenotypes (non-punishing non-adopters, non-punishing adopters, punishing non-adopters, punishing adopters); dynamics governed by recursions under Reward Model metanorm.",Summary of model structure from Section 2.1 and Table 1.,1
