ded.,1,Online,Conducted on Amazon Mechanical Turk.,1,One-shot allocation task using five real donors whose average annual donations and income ranges mirror US household donations by income quintile. Revealed condition shows both donation amounts and donor income ranges.,Summarized from Experiment 1 methods.,1
10.1017_bpp.2019.4.md,"Experiment 2 – Hidden income, Punishment only",Condition in Experiment 2 where participants can only punish and other players’ incomes are hidden.,1,Income visibility: hidden; Sanction type: punishment only,Experiment 2 uses 2 (hidden vs revealed) × 2 (punishment vs reward) between-participants design.,1,True,Human MTurk subjects play an incentivized repeated public goods game.,1,True,Random assignment to sanction type and income-visibility conditions.,1,False,"Conducted online via MTurk, not a physical lab.",1,False,Behavioral experiment with humans.,1,False,No analytical model is the focus of this condition.,1,5,Explicitly states groups of five players.,1,10,Game is played over 10 rounds.,1,1,In each round participants could contribute any amount of their income (continuous choice).,1,0,Standard PGG: income is initially private; participants choose how much to contribute.,1,0.4,"Contributions are doubled (multiplier 2) and divided equally among 5 players, so MPCR = 2/5 = 0.4.",1,0,No communication mentioned; only contribution and sanction decisions.,1,1,"After Stage 2, players see group members’ decisions to reward/punish them and a summary of their payoff.",0.9,0,Players are identified only by random letters which change every round; no stable identity linking sanctions to persons.,0.9,N/A,Reward option is not available in punishment-only condition.,1,0,Text does not indicate that total or remaining rounds are displayed to participants.,0.5,1,Punishment condition allows paying to decrease others’ payoffs.,1,1,“Pay 1 unit to decrease any other participant’s payoff by 3 units.”,1,3,Each 1 unit spent on punishment reduces target’s payoff by 3 units.,1,0,"In punishment condition, only punishment is available.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism in this condition.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in this condition.,1,100,Group income totals 100 units (55+19+13+9+4) each round; individual endowments are heterogeneous. We record total group endowment.,0.7,N/R,Paper reports contributions by quintile and condition but not a single aggregate fraction per condition.,0.6,N/R,Absolute contributions per condition are discussed qualitatively; no single summary amount per condition is reported.,0.6,N/R,Efficiency relative to maximum possible payoffs is not reported and cannot be inferred without full payoff data.,0.5,N/R,Only round payoffs by quintile trends are provided; no aggregate group payoff per condition.,0.5,USA,Participants recruited on MTurk with incomes referenced as US; explicitly ‘from the USA’ earlier and again for Experiment 3; Experiment 2 uses US income distribution and same platform.,0.9,N/R,No age statistics reported for Experiment 2.,1,N/R,Gender distribution not provided.,1,N/R,Education demographics not discussed.,1,Online,Explicitly states all participants were recruited via Amazon Mechanical Turk.,1,"Repeated two-stage public goods game for 10 rounds in groups of 5. Heterogeneous fixed incomes each round (55, 19, 13, 9, 4 units) based on US pre-tax income quintiles. Stage 1: contribute any amount of income to a common project; contributions doubled and split equally among 5. Stage 2 in this condition: participants can spend up to 2 units per other player on costly punishment (1 unit spent reduces target’s payoff by 3), constrained by Stage 1 earnings. Incomes of other players are hidden; participants only see their own income, the sum of all incomes, and others’ absolute contributions.","Summarized from Experiment 2 methods, focusing on hidden punishment condition.",1
10.1017_bpp.2019.4.md,"Experiment 2 – Hidden income, Reward only",Condition where incomes are hidden and participants can only reward others in Stage 2.,1,Income visibility: hidden; Sanction type: reward only,Part of the 2×2 design: hidden vs revealed × punishment vs reward.,1,True,Same MTurk behavioral experiment as other Experiment 2 conditions.,1,True,Controlled assignment to four cells of the 2×2 design.,1,False,Online via MTurk.,1,False,Involves human subjects.,1,False,No closed-form analytical model used as the primary method.,1,5,Groups of five players specified for Experiment 2.,1,10,Game lasts 10 rounds.,1,1,Players can contribute any amount from their income each round.,1,0,Income starts as private; decisions are how much to move to public pool.,1,0.4,"Contributions doubled and split among 5, so MPCR = 2/5.",1,0,No communication allowed according to description.,1,1,"End of each round, participants see others’ sanctioning decisions and payoff summary.",0.9,N/A,Punishment is not available in reward-only condition.,1,0,Players are anonymized with changing random letters; no stable identity associated with reward decisions.,0.9,0,No explicit mention of round-count display.,0.5,0,"This cell provides only reward, as per 2×2 design.",1,N/A,No punishment option.,1,N/A,No punishment option.,1,1,Reward condition lets players pay to increase others’ payoffs.,1,1,“Pay 1 unit to increase any other participant's payoff by 3 units.”,1,3,Each 1 unit spent increases target’s payoff by 3 units.,1,100,Group endowment totals 100 units per round across five heterogeneous incomes.,0.7,N/R,No aggregate fraction for this specific condition reported.,0.6,N/R,Descriptive statistics by visibility but not by sanction-type cell given in main text.,0.5,N/R,Efficiency measures per condition not presented.,0.5,N/R,"Only some per-quintile round payoffs and Gini coefficients by visibility are given, not by sanction-type.",0.5,USA,Same MTurk population as other Experiment 2 conditions; context uses US incomes.,0.9,N/R,Age not reported.,1,N/R,No gender information.,1,N/R,No education information.,1,Online,Performed on Amazon Mechanical Turk.,1,"Same 10-round heterogeneous-income public goods game as other Experiment 2 conditions. In Stage 2, participants in this condition can spend up to 2 units per other player to reward (1 spent yields +3 to target), constrained by their Stage 1 income. Incomes of other players are hidden; only own income, sum of incomes, and absolute contributions are visible.","Synthesized from general Experiment 2 description, specific to hidden reward-only cell.",1
