10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,"Simulation – ESS (0,0,1) condition","Section III-A.1 describes numerical simulations where parameters are set to satisfy conditions for equilibrium point (0,0,1) to be ESS.",1,"Parameter set: C1=8, C2=10, C3=6, α=0.7, V1=5, V2=3, R1=2, L1=2, L2=2, P=8, R2=5, F=3; initial strategy fractions x=y=z=0.5.","Authors explicitly list these parameter values for Fig. 2(a), representing this simulation condition.",1,False,Study uses an evolutionary game model and numerical simulations only; no human participants.,1,False,No controlled experiment with subjects; purely computational simulations of ODEs.,1,False,No laboratory or field setting; simulations only.,1,True,"Section III uses numerical simulations (Python, scipy.integrate.odeint) to solve replicator dynamics.",1,True,Section II develops an analytical evolutionary game model and derives ESS conditions.,1,3,"Model has three stakeholder populations: data providers, data users, data regulators.",1,0,"Continuous-time replicator dynamics over time, not discrete game rounds; coded as 0.",0.9,1,"Players choose between two discrete strategies, not continuous contributions; but all-or-nothing field is defined for contribution games and here is not applicable; encode as 1 by default.",0.3,N/A,No public goods contributions or endowments; evolutionary game on strategy fractions only.,1,N/R,No public goods or MPCR defined in this model.,1,N/A,No human subjects or communication; simulation of strategy dynamics only.,1,0,Not defined; no user interface or feedback summaries in simulations.,1,N/A,No identity or individual-level punishment visibility; only aggregate payoffs.,1,N/A,No identity or individual-level reward visibility; only aggregate payoffs.,1,0,Continuous-time simulation; no notion of showing number of rounds.,1,1,"Parameter F is described as reward (penalty) from regulators; negative payoff terms include -F, so punishment exists in model.",1,N/A,Model uses abstract payoff parameters; no explicit per-unit punishment cost specified as a separate variable.,0.5,N/A,No explicit mapping from punishment spending to impact; F enters payoffs directly.,0.5,1,F is also described as a reward from regulators; positive F terms reward cooperative behavior.,1,N/A,No explicit cost parameter for giving rewards; F is treated as net payoff term.,0.5,N/A,No explicit technology mapping reward spending to benefit; F directly modifies payoffs.,0.5,N/A,Model does not involve endowments; only payoffs from strategies.,1,N/A,"No contributions or public goods decisions; outcomes are cooperation ratios x, y, z.",1,N/A,No contribution amounts defined.,1,N/R,Authors do not define overall efficiency measure; only show strategy fractions.,1,N/R,No aggregate payoff values reported from simulations; focus on cooperation ratios.,1,N/A,No human participants; model stakeholders are abstract populations.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Numerical simulations of differential equations without human subjects.,1,"Three-population evolutionary game with two strategies per population (providers: high- vs low-quality data; users: acquire vs not acquire data; regulators: regulate vs not regulate). Replicator dynamics with payoffs parameterized by costs C1–C3, values V1,V2, rewards/penalties F,R1,R2, losses L1,L2, regulator income P, and data mining capability α. This condition’s parameter set satisfies ESS (0,0,1): providers defect (low-quality), users defect (not acquire), regulators cooperate (regulate).",Summarizes the modeled game structure and specific ESS targeted by this parameterization.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,"Simulation – ESS (0,1,1) condition","Section III-A.2 describes numerical simulations for parameters satisfying conditions where equilibrium point (0,1,1) is ESS.",1,"Parameter set: C1=15, C2=10, C3=6, α=0.8, V1=10, V2=8, R1=4, L1=2, L2=5, P=10, R2=8, F=3; initial strategy fractions x=y=z=0.5.",Parameter values explicitly provided for Fig. 2(b).,1,False,Purely computational evolutionary game simulations; no human data.,1,False,Not a behavioral experiment; simulation of ODEs.,1,False,No lab or field setting; numerical analysis only.,1,True,"Authors explicitly state they use numerical simulations via Python, scipy, matplotlib.",1,True,"Condition derived from analytical ESS Theorem 2, then checked via simulation.",1,3,Same three stakeholder populations as defined in model.,1,0,Continuous-time replicator dynamics; no discrete rounds.,0.9,1,"Players choose between two discrete strategies, analogous to all-or-nothing; contribution framework not strictly applicable.",0.3,N/A,No contributions or initial allocations.,1,N/R,No public good or MPCR defined.,1,N/A,No interacting human agents.,1,0,No UI or disclosures; only equations and state variables.,1,N/A,No individual identities; abstract populations.,1,N/A,Same as above.,1,0,No rounds; continuous time.,1,1,Negative F terms in payoffs when behavior is penalized.,1,N/A,No explicit cost-per-punishment-unit defined.,0.5,N/A,"Punishment enters via F directly in payoffs, not as separate technology.",0.5,1,Positive F terms reward desired actions.,1,N/A,No explicit cost for providing rewards specified.,0.5,N/A,Reward modeled as direct payoff term F.,0.5,N/A,No endowment structure described.,1,N/A,"Dependent variables are cooperation ratios x, y, z, not contributions.",1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Authors do not compute efficiency; only show strategy evolution.,1,N/R,No aggregate payoff trajectories reported.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Simulation-only study.,1,"Same three-population evolutionary game as defined in the model. This parameterization yields ESS (0,1,1): providers defect (low-quality), users cooperate (acquire), regulators cooperate (regulate). Simulation tracks time evolution of cooperation ratios under these parameters.",Describes strategic configuration corresponding to this ESS-focused simulation.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,"Simulation – ESS (1,0,1) condition","Section III-A.3 presents simulations with parameters satisfying conditions where equilibrium point (1,0,1) is ESS.",1,"Parameter set: C1=4, C2=13, C3=6, α=0.2, V1=8, V2=5, R1=3, L1=5, L2=1, P=7, R2=6, F=3; initial strategy fractions x=y=z=0.5.",Parameters explicitly specified for Fig. 2(c).,1,False,No human data; only simulations of mathematical model.,1,False,Not an experimental design with subjects.,1,False,No lab setting involved.,1,True,Uses numerical integration of replicator dynamics as described in Section III.,1,True,ESS conditions come from analytical derivations.,1,3,Three stakeholder populations.,1,0,Continuous-time dynamics.,0.9,1,Binary strategies per role; contribution framework not central but this matches discrete choice.,0.3,N/A,No endowment contributions.,1,N/R,No public goods game.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,0,Not applicable; no displayed summaries.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,No rounds.,1,1,Penalty F applied when behavior is disfavored.,1,N/A,No explicit punishment cost per unit.,0.5,N/A,Punishment implemented via F in payoff functions.,0.5,1,Reward component of F for cooperative actions.,1,N/A,No separate reward cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,Reward modeled as payoff shift.,0.5,N/A,No endowments.,1,N/A,Outputs are cooperation ratios.,1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency not reported.,1,N/R,Aggregate payoffs not shown.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Computational simulation only.,1,"Same tri-partite evolutionary game. This parameter set leads to ESS (1,0,1): providers cooperate (high-quality data), users defect (not acquire), regulators cooperate (regulate). Simulation examines time needed for x,z→1 and y→0.",Summarizes strategy profile and purpose of this simulation scenario.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,"Simulation – ESS (1,1,1) condition","Section III-A.4 presents simulations with parameters that satisfy the conditions making equilibrium point (1,1,1) an ESS.",1,"Parameter set: C1=8, C2=6, C3=7, α=0.7, V1=10, V2=8, R1=4, L1=4, L2=3, P=9, R2=5, F=4; initial strategy fractions x=y=z=0.5.",Parameter values directly given for Fig. 2(d).,1,False,No participant-based data collection.,1,False,"Model validation through simulation, not controlled experiment.",1,False,No lab context; entirely computational.,1,True,Replicator dynamics numerically integrated to show trajectories.,1,True,Analytical ESS conditions underpin this configuration.,1,3,Three-player-type evolutionary game.,1,0,ODE over continuous time; not round-based.,0.9,1,"Binary strategies, no continuous contribution; approximated as all-or-nothing.",0.3,N/A,No contributions/endowments.,1,N/R,No MPCR concept in this model.,1,N/A,No human players.,1,0,No display or feedback mechanism.,1,N/A,No individual identities modeled.,1,N/A,No individual identities modeled.,1,0,Continuous-time process.,1,1,Regulators impose penalties represented by F under some strategy profiles.,1,N/A,Punishment not broken into cost and impact parameters.,0.5,N/A,Impact encoded directly by F.,0.5,1,Regulators also reward cooperative behaviors via F and R2.,1,N/A,No explicit cost-of-reward variable.,0.5,N/A,Reward magnitude appears directly in payoff terms.,0.5,N/A,No endowment-based decisions.,1,N/A,"Outcomes tracked are cooperation ratios (x,y,z) approaching 1.",1,N/A,No contribution levels.,1,N/R,Paper does not quantify efficiency of this ESS in payoff terms.,1,N/R,Group payoffs not simulated or reported.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Environment is purely computational.,1,"Tri-party evolutionary game. This configuration yields full cooperation ESS (1,1,1): providers supply high-quality data, users acquire data, regulators regulate. Simulation in Fig. 2(d) shows all three cooperation ratios rapidly converge to 1, with users stabilizing fastest.",Captures essence of cooperative ESS the authors emphasize and how this simulation illustrates it.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,Parameter sweep – effect of C2 on users’ cooperation vs α,"Section III-B, Fig. 3(a) describes simulations varying C2 while holding other parameters fixed to study users’ cooperation as a function of data mining capability α.",1,"Independent variables: α (continuous over a range, not numerically specified) and C2 ∈ {3.4, 3.6, 3.8, 4.0}; fixed parameters C1=6, C3=5, V2=1, R1=2, L1=5, L2=7, P=3, R2=4, V1=2, F=1.",Text for Fig. 3(a) lists the C2 values and constants; α is plotted on x-axis.,1,False,These are simulations of the analytical model.,1,False,No controlled experiment; parameter sweep in simulation.,1,False,Not conducted in lab with human participants.,1,True,Authors compute steady states of replicator dynamics for various parameter values.,1,True,Evolutionary game and replicator equations are analytically derived; simulations explore their phase behavior.,1,3,Same three-population structure.,1,0,"Steady-state of continuous dynamics, not rounds.",0.9,1,Binary strategies per player class.,0.3,N/A,No contribution decisions.,1,N/R,No MPCR defined.,1,N/A,No human communication.,1,0,Not relevant for simulations.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,Continuous-time model.,1,1,Parameter F=1 used as reward/penalty in payoffs.,1,N/A,No explicit punishment cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,F directly modifies payoffs.,0.5,1,Same F acts as reward for desired behavior.,1,N/A,No cost-of-reward term.,0.5,N/A,Reward magnitude given directly by F.,0.5,N/A,No endowment concept.,1,N/A,Dependent variable here is fraction of users choosing to acquire data at equilibrium.,1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,"Heat maps show cooperation fractions, not efficiency.",1,N/R,No group payoff statistics reported for this sweep.,1,N/A,No humans involved.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Parameter-sweep simulations only.,1,"For each combination of α and C2 (with other parameters fixed), the replicator dynamics are run to steady state and the 