10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,Parameter sweep – effect of V1 on users’ cooperation vs α,"Section III-B, Fig. 3(b) reports simulations varying V1 while monitoring fraction of users acquiring data as α varies.",1,"Independent variables: α (continuous range) and V1 ∈ {1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5}; fixed parameters C1=6, C3=5, V2=1, R1=2, L1=5, L2=7, P=3, R2=4, C2=4, F=1.",Text for Fig. 3(b) lists V1 values and constant parameters; α is horizontal axis.,1,False,Simulation study.,1,False,No behavioral experiment.,1,False,No lab with people.,1,True,Steady states of replicator equations computed under varying V1 and α.,1,True,Simulations extend analytical model.,1,3,Three population game structure.,1,0,Continuous dynamics.,0.9,1,Binary strategies.,0.3,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Not a public goods game.,1,N/A,No human players.,1,0,No displays.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,Continuous time.,1,1,Regulator rewards/penalties included via F=1.,1,N/A,Not parameterized separately.,0.5,N/A,Punishment modeled directly in payoffs.,0.5,1,Reward F used.,1,N/A,No separate cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,Reward magnitude given by F.,0.5,N/A,Endowments not modeled.,1,N/A,"Output is cooperation fraction of users, not contributions.",1,N/A,No contribution variable.,1,N/R,"Authors discuss phase transitions in user cooperation, not efficiency.",1,N/R,No payoffs reported for these simulations.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Entirely simulation-based.,1,"For each pair (α, V1), with other parameters fixed, the system is simulated to stable equilibrium and the fraction of users choosing to acquire data is measured. Fig. 3(b) shows that raising the value of high-quality data V1 generally increases user cooperation, with diminishing marginal effect when V1 is already large.",Summarizes design and central finding for this parameter-sweep condition.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,Parameter sweep – effect of F on users’ cooperation vs α,"Section III-B, Fig. 3(c) presents simulations varying regulator reward/penalty F and observing users’ cooperation as α varies.",1,"Independent variables: α (continuous range) and F ∈ {0.3, 0.7, 1.1, 1.5}; fixed parameters C1=6, C3=5, V2=1, R1=2, L1=5, L2=7, P=3, R2=4, C2=4, V1=3.","Text for Fig. 3(c) lists F values and constants; α on x-axis, user cooperation on y-axis.",1,False,Model-only simulations.,1,False,No experimental manipulation on subjects.,1,False,No lab with human subjects.,1,True,Computational exploration of replicator dynamics for varying F and α.,1,True,Based on analytically derived model.,1,3,"Three populations (providers, users, regulators).",1,0,Continuous equilibrium analysis.,0.9,1,Two discrete strategies per role.,0.3,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Not a multplier-based public good.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No displays or interfaces.,1,N/A,No identities modeled.,1,N/A,No identities modeled.,1,0,Continuous time.,1,1,F acts as penalty in some payoff entries.,1,N/A,No cost parameter distinct from F.,0.5,N/A,Impact fixed by F.,0.5,1,F also acts as reward.,1,N/A,No separate reward-cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,Reward impact is F.,0.5,N/A,No endowments defined.,1,N/A,Outcome is user cooperation fraction at equilibrium.,1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency not analyzed.,1,N/R,Group payoffs not reported.,1,N/A,No human experiments.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Entirely computational study.,1,"For each pair (α, F), with other parameters fixed, simulations compute the stable fraction of users choosing to acquire data. Fig. 3(c) shows strong sensitivity: small increases in F can cause abrupt changes in user cooperation and overall strategy configuration.",Describes purpose and observed behavior of this F-sweep.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,"Heat maps – users’ cooperation as function of V1 and C2 at α=0.30,0.60,0.90","Section III-B, Fig. 4(a–c) show heat maps of users’ cooperation fraction over grid of V1 and C2 for different fixed α values.",1,"Independent variables: V1 in [3,7], C2 in [1,5] (exact grid not numerically listed), and three separate conditions for α ∈ {0.30, 0.60, 0.90}; fixed C1=6, C3=5, V2=1, R1=2, L1=5, L2=7, P=3, R2=4, F=1.","Text for Fig. 4 specifies ranges of V1, C2 and three α values, with other parameters fixed.",0.9,False,These are simulation phase diagrams.,1,False,No experiments with people.,1,False,Purely computational.,1,True,"For each grid point, replicator dynamics are simulated to equilibrium and cooperation fraction recorded.",1,True,Based on analytically specified game; simulation explores its parameter space.,1,3,Three stakeholders in evolutionary game.,1,0,Equilibrium of continuous dynamics.,0.9,1,Binary strategies.,0.3,N/A,Not a contribution game.,1,N/R,No MPCR.,1,N/A,No human communication.,1,0,Not applicable.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,Continuous time.,1,1,Reward/penalty F=1 used.,1,N/A,No cost separate from F.,0.5,N/A,Punishment impact directly specified.,0.5,1,F also rewards some behaviors.,1,N/A,No explicit cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,Reward size is F.,0.5,N/A,Endowments not modeled.,1,N/A,Outcome: fraction of users acquiring data (color scale from 0 to 1).,1,N/A,No contribution metric.,1,N/R,"Heat maps depict cooperation, not efficiency.",1,N/R,Group payoffs not provided for these diagrams.,1,N/A,No real participants.,1,N/A,No real participants.,1,N/A,No real participants.,1,N/A,No real participants.,1,No human,Simulated phase diagrams.,1,"For each fixed α (0.30, 0.60, 0.90), and for each grid point in (V1, C2), replicator dynamics are run to equilibrium and the fraction of users acquiring data is recorded. Fig. 4 shows regions of full cooperation (value 1) and full defection (0), with a discontinuous phase transition boundary shifting as α increases, illustrating that higher data mining capability relaxes requirements on V1 and C2 for user cooperation.","Summarizes what is varied, what is measured, and key qualitative result.",1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,3D traces – effects of C2 and α on full-group cooperation,"Section III-C, Fig. 5(a–c) displays 3D trajectories of x,y,z under different C2 and α values to study reaching full cooperation.",1,"Independent variables: C2 ∈ {3.4, 3.6, 3.8, 4.0} and α ∈ {0.30, 0.60, 0.90}; fixed parameters C1=6, C3=5, V2=1, R1=2, L1=5, L2=7, P=3, R2=4, V1=3, F=1; initial x=y=z=0.5.",Text for Fig. 5(a–c) specifies these C2 and α values and fixed parameters.,1,False,No empirical data; simulations.,1,False,"3D trajectories are simulation outputs, not experiments.",1,False,No laboratory setting.,1,True,Trajectories obtained by numerically integrating replicator dynamics.,1,True,System equations derived analytically; 3D plots visualize their solutions.,1,3,Three-population game.,1,0,Continuous-time simulation until convergence.,0.9,1,Binary strategies remain.,0.3,N/A,Not a contribution game.,1,N/R,No MPCR.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No interfaces.,1,N/A,No agents with identities.,1,N/A,No individual identities.,1,0,Time is continuous.,1,1,Reward/penalty F=1 present.,1,N/A,No explicit cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,Punishment encoded via F.,0.5,1,Reward parameter F present.,1,N/A,No reward-cost parameter.,0.5,N/A,Reward magnitude specified by F.,0.5,N/A,No endowment.,1,N/A,"Measured outcome is whether x,y,z converge to 1 or 0; not contributions.",1,N/A,No contribution measures.,1,N/R,"Focus on reaching cooperation state, not efficiency.",1,N/R,Group payoffs not shown.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,3D traces are from simulations.,1,"For each combination of (C2, α), trajectories of (x,y,z) starting from 0.5,0.5,0.5 are plotted in 3D. Fig. 5(a–c) illustrate that higher C2 can drive all three fractions toward 0, while higher α can counteract this and lead to full cooperation (x=y=z→1) even for larger C2.",Describes role of these parameters and qualitative behavior seen in 3D plots.,1
10.1109_tcss.2023.3324087.md,3D traces – effects of V1 and α on full-group cooperation,"Section III-C, Fig. 5(d–f) shows 3D traces for varying V1 and α with other parameters fixed.",1,"Independent variables: V1 ∈ {1.5, 2.5, 3.5, 4.5} and α ∈ {0.30, 0.60, 0.90}; fixed C1=6, C3=5, V2=1, R1=2, L1=5, L2=7, P=3, R2=4, C2=4, F=1; initial x=y=z=0.5.",Text for Fig. 5(d–f) lists V1 values and α levels; other parameters same as earlier and explicitly given.,1,False,Simulation only.,1,False,Not an experiment with subjects.,1,False,No lab.,1,True,Trajectories from integrating replicator dynamics.,1,True,Uses analytical model; 3D traces visualize its trajectories.,1,3,Three-population game.,1,0,Continuous time.,0.9,1,Binary choices.,0.3,N/A,No endowment contributions.,1,N/R,No MPCR.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,0,Not relevant.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,Continuous dynamics.,1,1,Reward/penalty F included.,1,N/A,No separate cost variable.,0.5,N/A,Punishment enters via F.,0.5,1,Reward effect of F.,1,N/A,No separate reward-cost term.,0.5,N/A,Reward magnitude specified by F.,0.5,N/A,No endowment.,1,N/A,Interest is whether cooperation ratios converge to 1.,1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency not addressed.,1,N/R,Payoffs not plotted here.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Simulation-only trajectories.,1,"For each (V1, α), trajectories show how x,y,z evolve. Fig. 5(d–f) indicate that when V1 is too low and α modest, cooperation may not emerge, but increasing α and/or V1 allows the system to reach full cooperation in most cases, except perhaps when both parameters are low.",Describes parameter interactions highlighted in these 3D traces.,1
