ct not reported.,0,N/R,Cooperation described qualitatively as 'relatively more cooperation'; no quantitative rates.,0,N/R,No token amounts given.,0,N/R,Improved 'performance' is mentioned but not quantified as efficiency.,0,N/R,Group payoff levels not specified.,0,United States,Kroll et al. (2007) co-authors based in US; experiment known to be with US students though not stated here.,0.5,N/R,No age data reported.,0,N/R,Gender composition not described.,0,University students,Typical subject pool for such lab experiments; not detailed here but inferred.,0.6,On site,"Laboratory voting/public goods experiment, not online or field.",0.8,Non-binding voting mechanism for a public good where voting outcome suggests a contribution norm; subjects can impose costly within-group punishment on deviators; punishment presence increases cooperation relative to a no-punishment voting baseline.,Summarized from description of 'non-binding voting mechanisms' with 'within-group punishment'.,0.9
