 treatment: four players each receive 40 ECUs (tokens) in Part I.,1,0.467,Average contribution in equal VCM treatment ranges from 46.7% to 40% (rounds 1–6). Using initial round 46.7% as representative average share reported.,0.7,N/R,"Only percentages of endowment per round are reported, not raw ECU averages.",0.1,N/R,No explicit or computable ratio of total payoff to maximum payoff reported by treatment.,0.1,N/R,No aggregate or per-group payoff levels reported.,0.1,South Africa,Participants from nine South African fishing communities.,1,Mean 41 years; adult participants from rural fishing communities.,Sample description: participants were on average 41 years old.,1,"58% male, 42% female",Sample description: 58% of sample were male.,1,"Low education; 14% completed primary school, 8% completed high school.",Reported in sample description.,1,On site,Manual experiments conducted in field laboratories in nine communities; controlled but not online.,0.9,"Linear public goods game (VCM) with heterogeneous treatments overall, but this condition uses homogeneous endowments. Group size 4, MPCR=0.5, fixed matching over 6 rounds, tokens convertible to cash at 10 cents per token.",Compiled from design and procedures sections.,1
