to 1 as base since each punished defector loses α tokens in total.,0.3,0,No rewards are included in the model; only punishment.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,1,Each cooperator contributes cost c=1 to the public pool; effective per-round endowment is normalized to 1.,0.8,N/R,They report fraction of cooperators ρ_c as main outcome; no explicit normalized contribution rate beyond that.,0.9,N/R,Only strategy fractions and phase boundaries are shown; not raw contribution totals.,0.9,N/R,No report of total payoffs relative to social optimum.,1,N/R,Payoff structure defined but numerical group payoffs are not reported.,0.8,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Simulated agents on a lattice only.,1,"Spatial public goods game on 400×400 regular lattice (degree 4, G=5 overlapping groups). Agents have memory counter t_i for consecutive defections, compared to common tolerance threshold M=3. If t_i > M and agent defects, they receive fine α=0.5 in each group; cooperators in group share total sanction cost equally. Strategy update via Fermi rule with selection intensity K, scanning over K and synergy factor r.","Summarized model mechanics plus specific parameter setting M=3, α=0.5 in phase diagram.",1
