10.1007_s10458-010-9122-9.md,"UG inequity aversion – 3 agents, α=0.6, β=0.3","Section 7.1.1, third experiment: three-agent Ultimatum-style allocation game with α=0.6, β=0.3 for all three.",1,"Homo Egualis inequity aversion parameters α=0.6, β=0.3 for all three agents",Only stated manipulation is inequity aversion parameters plus number of agents.,1,False,"No human subjects, only simulated agents.",1,False,Not a human experiment or field trial; computational simulation.,1,False,No lab with human participants.,1,True,Agents use CALA to learn allocations in a 3-agent Ultimatum-like game.,1,False,Analytical predictions exist but the section reports simulation learning curves.,0.9,3,Third experiment explicitly uses three agents.,1,2000,"Section 6.1.3 specifies 2,000 UGs for 'every experiment' in this model; applied to 3-agent case.",0.9,1,Resource allocations among 3 agents are continuous; not binary.,1,N/A,Not a public goods contribution frame.,1,N/A,Not a PGG; MPCR not defined.,1,N/A,No humans and no communication channel is modelled.,1,N/A,No experimental UI; purely programmatic.,1,N/A,No notion of identity revelation; rejection is the only sanction.,1,N/A,No explicit reward mechanism besides base payoffs.,1,N/A,Round count not 'shown' to simulated agents.,1,1,"Any player with utility below 0 may reject the allocation, which sets every agent’s utility to 0.",1,N/R,No explicit cost e vs c defined; only that rejection changes utilities to 0.,0.3,N/R,No numeric punishment-to-impact mapping parameter reported.,0.3,0,No separate reward phase or mechanism described.,1,N/A,Reward mechanism absent.,1,N/A,Reward mechanism absent.,1,100,Section 6.1.3: 'we start with an amount of 100 being equally divided over the n agents' (here n=3).,1,N/R,"They highlight that each agent should obtain at least 15.8, but do not present normalized contribution or division rates.",0.3,N/R,Exact final split among the 3 agents is not numerically listed; only bounds on the third agent’s payoff (>=15