hanism.,1,N/R,Payoffs derive from b and c; there is no explicit initial endowment per agent.,1,N/R,"Outputs are frequencies of C, D, P, not contribution proportions of an endowment.",1,N/R,No explicit contribution amount variable; only strategy type.,1,N/R,Paper does not compute total-payoff efficiency measures for simulations.,1,N/R,No aggregate group payoff statistics from simulations are reported.,1,N/A,"Simulated agents, not humans.",1,N/A,"Simulated agents, not humans.",1,N/A,"Simulated agents, not humans.",1,N/A,"Simulated agents, not humans.",1,No human,Purely computational simulation.,1,"Population of 𝒩=9000 agents each assigned C, D, or P (initially 1/3 each). At each time step: randomly choose target i, form ad hoc group of size N=5 by sampling N−1 others, compute payoff Pi via Eq. (2); choose reference j, form its group, get Pj; if Pi<Pj, i adopts j’s strategy with probability (Pj−Pi)/Ω, where Ω is maximum possible payoff difference.",Directly summarizes the simulation algorithm described in Sec. 4 for the Fig. 1 condition.,1
