,Only punishment (disapproval or sanctions) is available; no positive points.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Participants start each round with an initial endowment of 20 ECU.,1,0.7059,"Use HF variable (share choosing Harmful) as the key behavioral DV. For NL, Harmful (HF) mean=0.958 (Table 4). Map to contributionRate as the primary action variable.",0.6,N/R,No token contributions; binary action with state-dependent payoffs; no single raw ‘amount’ reported.,1,N/R,Paper discusses efficiency qualitatively but does not report normalized efficiency index by treatment.,0.3,N/R,No treatment-level average group payoff reported in ECU.,0.3,Canada; France,Sessions run in Québec (Canada) and Strasbourg (France).,1,N/R,Only that participants are from university pools; no age statistics given.,0.1,N/R,Gender asked in questionnaire but not summarized.,0.1,University students (exact distribution N/R),"Recruited via university subject pools (ORSEE etc.); typical for lab experiments, but no explicit level shares.",0.6,On site,Conducted in physical laboratories in Québec and Strasbourg with z-Tree; no online mention.,1,"Negative-externality liability game. Each round: endowment 20 ECU; choose Harmless (Y: +6 self, 0 others) or Harmful (X: private benefit 14/16/20/22 depending on private state A/B/C/D; −4 ECU to each of 3 others, deterministic). States are i.i.d., equiprobable, private, and redrawn each round. Stranger matching over 4-person groups. Liability: none; losses borne by victims. After payoff feedback, subjects can assign 0–6 disapproval points (stage 1–10) or 0–6 monetary sanction points (stage 11–20) to each other group member; sanction point costs 0.5 ECU to both parties. Under NL, no legal liability information is displayed, only number of harmful acts by others.","Summarizes stage structure, payoffs, and information from the design section for this treatment.",1
