ishment option in this condition.,1,N/A,No punishment option in this condition.,1,0,No positive reward mechanism described; only punishment systems are manipulated.,1,N/A,No reward option implemented.,1,N/A,No reward option implemented.,1,30,Symmetric groups: all four group members received equal endowments of 30 MUs at the beginning of each period.,1,0.528,"Without punishment, participants contributed on average 52.80% of their endowment; this is across symmetric and asymmetric, but no split is provided, so use overall rate.",0.7,N/R,"Only percentages of endowment are reported, not absolute MUs by condition.",0.1,N/R,Total payoff relative to maximum possible is not reported or derivable per condition from text alone.,0,N/R,"Only average individual profits and differences are reported, not full group totals by condition.",0.2,Germany,Participants were recruited on the campus of a German university.,1,"M=21.34, SD=3.72",Reported for the full sample; not broken down by condition.,1,"98 male, 112 female, 2 n/a",Reported for the full sample; not broken down by condition.,1,University students (undergraduates),Described as participants recruited on the campus of a German university; typical lab subject pool is students.,0.9,On site,Participants entered the lab and sat in cubicles; z-Tree was used in a lab setting.,1,"Linear public goods game, endowment 30 MUs each; contributions multiplied by 1.6 and evenly redistributed; groups fixed across 24 periods; member labels reshuffled each period to prevent targeting.",Summarizes structural features that apply across all punishment systems in symmetric condition.,1
