10.1257_mic.20180336.md,Part II – Exogenous Institution Treatment – PGG Rule,Condition is Part II exogenous institution treatment; this row is the regulated game PGG Rule with exogenously imposed MCR=20.,1,Institution presence and type: Exogenous minimum contribution requirement (MCR=20) with forfeiture of income if violated.,In this treatment the MCR in PGG Rule is fixed exogenously at 20 each period.,1,True,Human participants in lab.,1,True,Controlled treatment with imposed institution.,1,True,Ran in on-site laboratories.,1,False,No non-human simulation.,1,False,Not a formal theory-only condition.,1,4,Groups of four in Part II.,1,20,20 repeated periods.,1,1,"Any integer from 0 to 20 allowed; however, only 20 avoids punishment.",1,0,All 20 points start as private endowment.,1,0.5,Payoff if not punished uses same PGG technology: π_i=20-g_i+0.5∑g_j.,1,0,No communication channel in design.,1,1,End-of-period info includes all contributions and payoffs.,1,0,Monitoring and punishment by central authority; individual identities of punished players are not indicated beyond contribution list; no names or persistent IDs.,0.7,0,No reward mechanism separate from public good returns.,1,1,Subjects know there are 20 periods.,0.6,1,Institution monitors contributions and punishes g_i<20 by forfeiting all income from PGG Rule that period.,1,0,"Punishment is automatic via central authority, not chosen by peers; no per-unit cost borne by other players.",0.8,1,"If punished, subject loses 100% (1×) of their PGG Rule income for that period (forfeiture of all income).",0.9,0,No extra positive transfers beyond standard PGG returns for compliance.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Endowment 20 points per subject per game.,1,0.9975,"Average contribution to PGG Rule is 19.95 out of 20, so rate≈19.95/20≈0.9975.",1,19.95,"Text: MCR=20 satisfied in 1,753 of 1,760 decisions, yielding average contribution 19.95.",1,N/R,Paper reports welfare gain relative to baseline but no