rate agents in a public goods game setting matching the 1-punisher lab treatment. Confederates follow the same probabilistic contribute/punish rules as in Tables 2 and 3; the EMIL-I-A agent updates norm salience from punishment cues and combines individual and normative drives to set its contribution probability. Simulation results (5,000 replications) show intermediate contribution rates between 0- and 3-punisher treatments.",Summarized from Simulation Design and Figure 3 discussion.,1
10.1177_0894439313511396.md,Simulation – EMIL-I-A agents – 2 Punishers treatment,Agent-based simulation condition with EMIL-I-A agents replicating 2-punisher lab treatment.,1,Agent type = EMIL-I-A; Number of punisher confederate players in group = 2; Initial norm salience = 0,Simulation mirrors 2-punisher human treatment with EMIL-I-A architecture.,1,False,No human subjects.,1,False,"Agent-based model, not empirical study.",1,False,No on-site human lab component.,1,True,Described as agent-based simulation with EMIL-I-A agents.,1,False,"Behavior explored via simulation, not analytical derivation.",1,4,One EMIL-I-A plus three confederates.,1,40,Replicates 40-round game.,1,0,Binary contribute/defect decision reproduced.,0.9,N/A,No human monetary endowment.,1,N/R,Simulation payoff parameters not explicitly stated.,0,N/A,Not applicable without humans.,1,N/A,Applies to information shown to humans; simulation agents receive whatever data the model requires.,1,N/A,No human identities.,1,N/A,No reward and no human participants.,1,N/A,Round horizon is a simulation control.,1,1,Punishment and sanctions implemented as part of EMIL-I-A environment.,1,N/R,Numerical cost parameter not detailed.,0,N/R,Fine magnitude per punishment unspecified.,0,0,Simulations include only punishment.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,Simulation uses abstract payoffs rather than human token endowments.,1,N/R,Contribution trajectories by treatment shown graphically (Figure 3) but numeric outcomes not provided.,0,N/R,Raw contribution amounts not tabulated.,0,N/R,No efficiency metrics for simulations reported.,0,N/R,Simulation results only reported for contributions.,0,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Computation-only agent-based model.,1,"EMIL-I-A agent interacts with three confederate agents in 2-punisher configuration. Confederates follow the same probabilistic rules as in the human experiment; varying number of punishers changes the norm-salience effect of punishment on the EMIL-I-A agent. The model shows that higher numbers of punishers increase norm salience and thus contribution probability, reproducing qualitative human patterns.",From 'Simulation Design' and Figure 3 explanation.,1
