10.1016_j.econlet.2017.01.016.md,Punish 1 (single-stage peer punishment),Paper labels one treatment 'Punish 1' with a single punishment stage following contribution decisions.,1,Punishment opportunity: one stage of first-order peer punishment after seeing others’ contributions.,"Compared to Baseline, Punish 1 adds 'now-standard opportunities to punish fellow group members after being shown their contributions, in a second stage of each period.'",1,True,Human subjects in lab; Punish 1 is one of the main experimental treatments.,1,True,Controlled manipulation of punishment opportunities across treatments.,1,True,Same lab setting as other treatments; called 'laboratory experiment'.,1,False,No indication of computational-only simulations.,1,False,"Study is experimental, not purely analytical.",1,4,General design: 'each of 240 subjects is grouped with three others in sessions of 20 participants'; applies to all main treatments including Punish 1.,1,15,Main treatments are '15 periods in fixed groups'; Punish 1 is one of these.,1,1,"Same 'standard voluntary contribution design' as Baseline, with continuous allocation between private and group accounts.",0.9,0,Same as Baseline; endowment initially in private account.,0.7,N/R,Marginal per capita return is not numerically specified.,0,0,No communication mentioned for any treatment; standard protocol disallows chat.,0.8,0,"Subjects see others’ contributions to decide punishment, but summary statistics are only explicitly mentioned for Punish 2'.",0.6,1,"In punishment treatments, punishment is 'directed at' specific group members; identification is standard, although explicit statement appears for Punish 2 (subjects 'learn the amount and originator of any punishment they received'). By design symmetry this likely holds for Punish 1.",0.7,0,No reward mechanism described.,1,0,Not reported that interface displayed number of remaining periods.,0.3,1,Punish 1 adds a 'second stage' with opportunities to punish fellow group members.,1,N/R,Exact cost per punishment unit is not given in the excerpt.,0,N/R,Exact punishment impact per unit spent is not reported.,0,0,No positive reward option is mentioned.,1,N/A,No reward scheme.,1,N/A,No reward scheme.,1,20,Fig. 1 notes contributions are 'out of 20 tokens' in the standard design that applies to all main treatments.,0.9,N/R,"Numerical average contributions fraction not provided, only that Punish 1 contributions are higher than Baseline and show a rising trend.",0,N/R,No exact mean contribution per period or overall is given for Punish 1.,0,N/R,Only relative statements that earnings are higher than Baseline; no normalized efficiency index.,0,N/R,Fig. 2 compares average earnings but does not list numeric values in the excerpt.,0,China,"Same pool: 'students at universities in Tianjin, China'.",1,N/R,Age is not reported.,0,N/R,Gender composition not reported.,0,University students,Same subject pool across treatments.,1,On site,Lab experiment with university students in Tianjin.,0.9,"Standard 4-player linear public goods game with 20-token endowment per period, 15 periods, fixed groups, followed by a single punishment stage where subjects can assign costly punishment to group members after seeing contributions.",Summarizes design details described for Punish 1.,1
