emma as in NP-students: payoffs (25,25), (5,30), (30,5), (10,10); groups of 4; random pairwise matching; δ=0.95; 5 cycles per session; private monitoring; no communication.",Design identical across treatments except for subject pool and punishment availability.,1
10.1016_j.jebo.2012.12.024.md,"PP – Students (personal punishment, student pool)",PP treatment with undergraduate students; adds a costly personal punishment stage to the PD.,1,Personal punishment availability: Yes (PP); Subject pool: Students,Treatment variable PP indicates presence of personal punishment; this is with students.,1,True,Human student participants.,1,True,Controlled randomized laboratory experiment.,1,True,Conducted in Vernon Smith Experimental Economics Lab.,1,False,No simulations reported for this treatment.,1,False,Outcomes based on experimental data.,1,4,Same four-person groups used in all treatments.,1,84,"Average session length across treatments is 84 periods, applied here.",0.5,1,Binary cooperate/defect choice in PD stage.,0.6,0,Not a typical contribution game; no pre-set public fund.,0.3,N/R,MPCR concept not used for this PD.,1,0,Subjects could not communicate.,1,0,Only own pair outcomes observable; no evidence of aggregate feedback.,0.9,0,Interactions anonymous; others outside pair cannot see punishment or identities.,1,0,No reward mechanism.,1,0,Random continuation rule; no indication that subjects were shown remaining periods.,0.9,1,PP treatment introduced a costly personal punishment stage.,1,5,Subjects could pay 5 points to reduce opponent’s earnings by 10 points.,1,10,Each 5-point cost lowered opponent’s payoff by 10 points; technology ratio is 10 points reduced per punishment act.,1,0,"Only punishment, no personal reward opportunities.",1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,Per-round endowment not stated; only resulting payoffs from action profiles given.,0.2,0.704,PP treatment cooperation rate for students reported as 70.4%; interpreted as contribution rate.,0.95,N/R,No numeric contribution amounts beyond binary action reported.,1,N/R,No efficiency ratio reported.,1,N/R,No treatment-specific average group payoff in points given.,0.2,United States,Students from Purdue University in the U.S.,0.9,Mean ≈ 21.2 years,Same student pool a