10.1007_s10683-015-9452-1.md,Third-party punishment game – within-subject ethnicity conditions,Single 3PP game where punishers specify minimum acceptable offers contingent on ethnicities of sender and receiver using strategy method.,0.9,Ethnicity of dictator (player 1) and recipient (player 2) relative to punisher’s ethnicity (own group vs out-groups Vietnamese/Khmer/Chinese),"Study examines whether punishers defend in-group receivers and/or punish out-group dictators, varying identities via tag colors.",1,True,Human participants playing incentivized 3PP.,1,True,Controlled payoffs and random assignment of roles; strategy method for punishment thresholds.,1,True,Run in controlled on-site sessions rather than naturally occurring settings.,0.7,False,No simulations used.,1,False,No purely analytical modeling.,1,3,"Game has player 1 (dictator), player 2 (receiver), player 3 (third-party punisher).",1,1,One decision per contingency (threshold) without feedback; one-shot structure.,0.7,1,Dictator-like first stage where player 1 can choose any allocation of 10k between self and receiver; not restricted to all-or-nothing.,0.7,0,"Funds start as dictator’s endowment, not in a public pot.",0.8,N/A,Not a public goods game.,1,0,No communication between players is mentioned.,0.9,0,No summaries of others’ punishment or allocations presented.,0.9,0,No indication that identities of punishers or dictators are revealed; only ethnic-group information via color.,0.7,0,No reward mechanism.,1,0,No explicit information about displaying total number of games/rounds.,0.6,1,Third party can pay to reduce dictator’s payoff; core of the game.,1,1,Each 1k dong spent by player 3 reduces their own 5k endowment by 1k.,1,3,Spending 1k by punisher reduces player 1’s payoff by 3k.,1,0,"No option to reward, only punish.",1,N/A,No reward technology.,1,N/A,No reward technology.,1,10,Player 1 decides what portion of 10k dong to send to player 2; punisher has 5k separate endowment.,1,N/R,"Outcomes reported a