Text gives only approximate percentages and graph; no numeric average for this specific phase and treatment.,0.2,N/R,No explicit or computable efficiency ratio reported by treatment and phase.,0,N/R,No aggregate payoff numbers per treatment/phase reported.,0,Norway,Subjects recruited at BI Norwegian Business School in Oslo.,0.9,N/R,Only described as bachelor students; no age statistics provided.,0.1,N/R,No gender composition information reported.,0,Bachelor students,Subjects recruited from among bachelor students at the institution.,1,On site,Conducted in a physical lab with cubicles and z-tree; not online.,1,"Voluntary participation; 3-stage game but here only stages 1–2 active. Participation decision reduces endowment by fraction d=1/11 (cost 2 ECUs). Endowment z=22; insiders’ contribution choice c_i∈[0,20]. Contributions by insiders multiplied by α=1.6 and benefits shared equally among all 4 players (insiders and outsiders). Groups fixed over 20 periods (partner matching). Feedback each period on all group members’ participation and contributions in anonymized columns.",Summarizes structural details of VP game and this phase from design section.,1
