e sweeps.,0.6,N/R,No explicit efficiency values.,0.7,N/R,Not reported.,0.6,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Simulation-only parameter sweep.,1,"Same baseline multi-group harvesting model without between-group transfer mechanisms, but group size n is varied from 5 to 50 while keeping number of groups N = 25 and other parameters fixed. Long-run average frequency of resource-conserving individuals and number of group collapses are tracked over 10 runs (each 10,000 periods, averaging last 5000) to examine a threshold effect: for small n, larger groups speed diffusion of defection; above a threshold, larger groups increase collapse risk for defector-heavy groups and thereby favor conservation.",Summarizes Section 4.1.2’s description of how n is varied and what outcomes are observed in baseline condition.,0.9
