10.1016_j.jrp.2019.103907.md,"Baseline constant r, pool punishment, K=0.5, τ=0","Condition underlying Fig. 1(c): pool punishment regime, enhancement factor r constant (no time variation), stochastic noise K=0.5, no delay mentioned so τ=0.",0.9,Enhancement factor r varied over a range at fixed K=0.5 with pool punishment and no delay,Fig. 1(c) shows frequencies after 5000 MCS as a function of r for K=0.5 under pool punishment.,0.9,False,Explicitly described as Monte Carlo simulations on a spatial grid; no human participants.,1,False,Not a controlled lab/field experiment with human subjects; it is a numerical simulation study.,1,False,No laboratory setting; purely computational.,1,True,Described as Monte Carlo simulation on a square lattice with evolutionary dynamics.,1,False,No closed-form or purely analytical results; all results are from simulations.,1,90000,They state L=300 for these simulations (unless stated otherwise). Player count N=L^2=300^2=90000.,0.95,5000,They report frequencies after 5000 MCS in Fig. 1.,0.9,1,"Players are strategies C, D, P with fixed contribution: C and P contribute 1, D contributes 0. No choice of intermediate amounts; all-or-nothing at the strategy level.",0.9,0,"Standard PGG formulation with individuals choosing whether to contribute from their own endowment; contributions are made from private assets, so initial public fund share is 0.",0.7,0.2,MPCR = r/G. Group size G=5. r itself is varied; MPCR therefore varies as r/5. Taking representative MPCR at r=1 would be 0.2; however r range is not numerically given. Using expression MPCR=r/5; to fit numeric requirement we provide 0.2 and note dependence.,0.3,0,No communication or messaging between agents in the simulation is described.,1,0,Agents are simple strategies with no explicit information displays; no summaries reported.,1,0,No notion of identity revelation; spatial neighbors interact but no IDs or reputation are displayed.,1,0,There is no rewarding mechanism in this model.,1,0,No hu