10.1016_j.physleta.2018.05.020.md,Analytical model – baseline without leader punishment (global vs local migration),Paper develops one analytical evolutionary game model comparing global vs local migration without additional mechanisms.,1,Migration pattern (global migration vs local migration); migration rate v; mutation rate μ; number of groups M; benefit b; cost c.,"Section 3.1 varies migration pattern, v, μ, M, and benefit-to-cost ratio b/c to study global cooperation and ethnocentrism.",1,False,No human participants; theoretical evolutionary model and simulations.,1,False,Not a controlled behavioral experiment; it is a theoretical analysis.,1,False,No lab or field setting; purely theoretical.,1,True,They use agent-based simulations in Appendix C to validate analytical results.,1,True,"Core of the paper is an analytical model with closed-form conditions (e.g., strategy selection inequalities, (b/c)* expressions).",1,20,Appendix C agent-based simulations use N=20 individuals.,0.9,1,Evolutionary Moran process is effectively an indefinite sequence of reproduction events rather than discrete repeated-game rounds; set to 1 for lack of discrete round structure.,0.4,1,"Individuals choose a pure strategy (cooperate or defect) but in PD representation cooperation is a fixed cost c and benefit b, not an all-or-nothing contribution choice; closest mapping is that they can effectively choose any of the four strategies, not a binary contribute-all-or-nothing from an endowment.",0.4,N/A,No endowment or pre-allocated contribution as in public goods games; only PD payoffs.,1,N/R,"Model uses a pairwise PD with benefit b and cost c, not a linear public goods game with MPCR.",1,N/A,No human subjects or communication stage.,1,0,"No user interface or feedback structure for humans; not applicable, coded as 0.",1,N/A,No peer punishment or identity revelation; model is anonymous.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,0,No human interface showing remaining rounds.,1,0,Baseline model in Section 3.