10.1016_j.physleta.2018.05.020.md,Analytical model – equality-oriented leader punishment,Section 3.2 and Appendix D introduce equality-oriented leader punishment and derive conditions for global cooperation and ethnocentrism.,1,Presence of equality-oriented leader punishment with fine β; migration pattern (global vs local); migration rate v; mutation rate μ; number of groups M; benefit b; cost c.,"They vary β and compare scenarios with this punishment, also considering migration parameters as in baseline.",1,False,No human participants; theoretical analysis.,1,False,"Analytical evolutionary model, not an empirical experiment.",1,False,No lab or field setting.,1,True,"Although details for leader punishment simulations are not expanded, the paper overall uses simulations to check analytical predictions.",0.6,True,They derive algebraic conditions such as c < β/2 for global cooperation and inequalities involving φ.,1,20,"Appendix C simulation parameters (N=20) likely also apply when checking leader-punishment scenarios, though not explicitly restated.",0.4,1,Same Moran-process evolutionary setting as baseline; no discrete round count.,0.4,1,"Interaction remains a pairwise PD, not an all-or-nothing contribution; mapping as in baseline.",0.4,N/A,No endowment or contribution stage.,1,N/R,Not a public goods game; PD with b and c.,1,N/A,No human experiment or communication.,1,0,No interface or reporting to human subjects.,1,N/A,Leader punishment is not linked to observable identities of human players; this construct is theoretical.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,0,No human subjects or round display.,1,1,Equality-oriented leader punishment imposes fine β on defectors exploiting cooperators.,1,N/R,Model specifies a fine β to defectors but does not specify leaders’ cost per punishment; thus cost to punisher is not defined.,0.3,N/R,"They define only the fine magnitude β to punished defectors, not a mapping from punisher expenditure to fine.",0.3,0,No rewarding mechanism; only punishment by leaders.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,"Game is specified purely by b, c, and β, without an endowment interpretation.",1,N/R,"Outcomes discussed are abundances of strategies and conditions when global cooperation is favored, not explicit contribution fractions.",1,N/R,No explicit contribution amount variable reported.,1,N/R,"Although they mention efficiency-oriented punishment, they do not report normalized efficiency outcomes.",1,N/R,No explicit numerical group payoffs; only qualitative strategy success conditions.,1,N/A,No human data.,1,N/A,No human data.,1,N/A,No human data.,1,N/A,No human data.,1,No human,Analytical evolutionary model with leader punishment; no experimental subjects.,1,"Same group-structured Moran-process PD as baseline, but leaders impose equality-oriented punishment: defectors who exploit cooperators (i.e., unequal outcomes) are fined β, while defectors meeting defectors are not punished. This modifies the intra- and intergroup payoff matrices and yields conditions such as c < β/2 for global cooperation to be favored and inequalities involving φ for global cooperation to dominate ethnocentrism.",Summarized from Section 3.2 and Appendix D payoff matrices and derived conditions.,1
10.1016_j.physleta.2018.05.020.md,Analytical model – efficiency-oriented leader punishment,"Section 3.2 and Appendix D describe efficiency-oriented leader punishment, distinct from equality-oriented punishment.",1,Presence of efficiency-oriented leader punishment with fine β; migration pattern (global vs local); migration rate v; mutation rate μ; number of groups M; benefit b; cost c.,They vary β and consider this alternative punishment rule under same migration and mutation settings.,1,False,No human participation.,1,False,Not an empirical or lab experiment.,1,False,No lab or field setting.,1,True,Paper overall uses simulations to validate analytical results; likely also applied here though details are in appendices.,0.6,True,They derive algebraic conditions such as c < β and inequalities for global cooperation vs ethnocentrism using φ.,1,20,Adopt N=20 from Appendix C simulations as representative for the simulated implementation of the analytical model.,0.4,1,Same ongoing Moran-process evolutionary dynamics; no fixed repeated-game rounds.,0.4,1,Underlying interaction remains a pairwise PD with discrete cooperate/defect rather than an all-or-nothing threshold public good.,0.4,N/A,No endowment-based contribution decision.,1,N/R,Not a linear public goods game; MPCR not defined.,1,N/A,No human communication.,1,0,No subject-level feedback interface.,1,N/A,"Leader punishment is a model construct, not a visible decision to human subjects.",1,N/A,No rewards.,1,0,No human experimental rounds shown.,1,1,Efficiency-oriented leader punishment fines all defectors by β.,1,N/R,Model states defectors incur a fine β but does not define cost to the leader/punisher.,0.3,N/R,No mapping from punisher expenditure to imposed fine is specified; only fine level β is given.,0.3,0,No reward or positive incentives; only punishment.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,"Payoffs are parameterized by b, c, and β without explicit endowment.",1,N/R,"Reported outcomes are conditions for strategy prevalence, not contribution fractions.",1,N/R,No explicit contribution-variable outcomes.,1,N/R,"Though efficiency-oriented punishment refers to maximizing global interest, the paper does not compute normalized efficiency values.",1,N/R,No explicit numerical group payoff outcomes are presented.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,"Purely theoretical plus simulations, no behavioral experiment.",1,"Same group-structured Moran-process PD as baseline, with efficiency-oriented leader punishment: all defectors (regardless of partners) incur a fine β for violating the efficiency norm. This changes the payoff matrices and yields the condition c < β for global cooperation to be favored and further inequalities (involving φ) for global cooperation to outperform ethnocentrism. They also compare global vs local migration effects via φ_global = 2 + μ + 2v/(M−1) and φ_local.",Summarized from Appendix D’s description of efficiency-oriented punishment matrices and derived conditions.,1
