ogical card choice.,1,N/A,No contributions; task is not a resource allocation game.,1,N/A,No group payoff or efficiency concept in this task.,1,N/A,No group payoffs; single-person reasoning task.,1,N/R,This article does not identify the countries of the WST samples; multiple prior studies exist.,0.1,N/R,No demographic data are given.,0.1,N/R,No demographic data are given.,0.1,N/R,Subjects not specified as students or others in this generic description.,0.1,On site,Classical Wason tasks are administered in lab or classroom settings; online not indicated.,0.7,"Standard Wason Selection Task with four cards (two letters, two numbers) testing selection of logically relevant cases to falsify a conditional; fewer than 10% of subjects typically choose the correct pair of cards (E and 7).",Based on explicit description and summary performance statistic.,0.95
