anism.,1,20,Each individual receives an endowment of 20 MUs per round.,1,0.6465,Low-return average contribution overall is 12.93 MUs (Table 1); divide by endowment 20 → 12.93/20 ≈ 0.6465. No condition split reported; assume similar across agreement/disagreement since no treatment effect and same game.,0.5,12.93,Table 1 reports 12.93 (SD 5.67) for low-return members averaging across conditions; used as best available estimate because no per-condition means reported and no treatment effect found.,0.5,N/R,Paper does not report total group payoffs or efficiency ratios.,0,N/R,No raw group payoff data reported.,0,"Mixed; 87 Dutch, 105 other nationalities",Methods section describes composition of full sample; no indication of differences by condition.,0.9,Mean 24 years,Participants were on average 24 years old; no per-condition data.,0.9,"127 female, 62 male, 3 other",Given for full sample; assignment to conditions randomized.,0.9,Mostly Utrecht University students,Almost all participants were students at Utrecht University.,0.9,On site,Conducted in physical lab (ELSE) with participants in cubicles.,1,"Linear public goods game with heterogeneous marginal returns (one high-return m=0.75, two low-return m=0.50) and peer punishment; fixed groups; information on others' contributions and payoffs each round; anonymity of punishers.",Summarizes key structural features described in Methods.,1
