ents but not simple overall mean contribution per period or per subject by treatment.,0,N/R,No aggregate payoff relative to maximum summarized as an efficiency ratio.,0,N/R,"Only individual average earnings per treatment reported, not per-group totals.",0,Germany,Experiment in Bonn (Germany) with local subject pool; standard assumption for EconLab; country not explicitly named but inferred.,0.7,N/R,Not reported; only that participants are students from a subject pool.,0,Approximately half female,Paper: approximately half of participants were female for the first set of treatments.,0.8,University students (various majors),"Participants randomly drawn from a pool of ~3,500 subjects with various majors; implies university students.",0.9,On site,Run in Bonn EconLab with participants seated in individual cubicles.,1,"Standard linear public good game with fixed groups of 4, endowment 20 per period, MPCR 0.4, 30 known periods, feedback each period on each member’s contribution; payoff: π_i = e - c_i + m * sum_j c_j.",Summarized directly from the design description.,1
