10.1111_ecin.12187.md,Representative – PGG-Standard,Representative treatment (general population sample) playing the baseline Public Goods Game without punishment (PGG-Standard).,1,Subject pool = Representative (general adult population); Punishment institution = No (PGG-Standard),This condition differs from others by participant pool (Representative vs Student) and by presence/absence of punishment (Standard vs Punishment).,1,True,Human participants from the general population played incentivized public goods games.,1,True,"Randomly rematched groups, controlled payoffs, pre-specified treatments indicate a lab experiment.",1,True,"Sessions held in controlled locations (hotel conference room with mobile lab), standard lab software (z-Tree).",1,False,No agent-based or computer-only simulations; all data from human subjects.,1,False,"Although some analytical discussion appears, the reported results are from experiments, not closed-form models.",1,4,"Text: ""participants were divided into groups of N=4"".",1,8,"Text: ""each subject first played 8 periods of a PGG-Standard and then 8 periods of a PGG-Punishment.""",1,0,"Contributions could take four discrete levels {0,6,14,20}, not a binary all-or-nothing choice.",1,0,Each subject received an endowment and chose how much to allocate; initial endowment entirely in private account.,0.9,0.5,"Text: ""the marginal per capita return (MPCR) of the public good was a=0.5.""",1,0,"Text: ""no form of communication was allowed during the experiment.""",1,1,"After each period, subjects observed individual contributions and earnings for each group member.",1,0,"No punishment stage exists in PGG-Standard; identities of any sanctions are N/A, treated as not shown.",0.9,0,No reward mechanism in the design.,1,1,"Standard in repeated PGGs; sessions described as 8 periods; while not explicit, subjects almost certainly knew the horizon.",0.6,0,PGG-Standard has no second-stage punishment opportunities.,1,N/A,No punishment stage in this condition.,1,N/A,No punishment stage in this condition.,1,0,"Design only mentions costly punishment, no rewards.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,"Text: ""each subject received an endowment of wi=20 tokens"".",1,N/R,Only average contribution amounts in tokens are reported; rate (normalized 0–1) is not explicitly given.,0.4,9.11,"Table 3: ""Average individual contributions"" for Representative, PGG-Standard, all periods = 9.11 tokens.",1,N/R,They report earnings drops qualitatively but not normalized efficiency measures.,0.2,N/R,Average per-period or total group payoff is not directly reported for this specific condition.,0.2,Italy,"Participants were born and resident in the province of Ravenna, in Emilia-Romagna, Italy.",1,"Adults, stratified: 24.3% aged 18–39, 44.7% aged 40–59, 31.1% aged 60+",Table 2 provides age distribution for the Representative sample.,1,"51.5% male, 48.5% female",Table 2: Male 51.5% for Representative sample; remainder assumed female.,1,"18.5% 8th grade or lower, 47.5% high school, 34.0% college/Master/PhD",Education levels for Representative sample in Table 2.,1,On site,"Representative sessions held in a hotel conference room with mobile lab, not online or in the field.",1,"Repeated linear public goods game with discrete contribution levels {0,6,14,20}; strangers matching each period; feedback on individual contributions and earnings; 1 Euro per 40 tokens.",Summarizes additional structural details from Section II.,1
10.1111_ecin.12187.md,Representative – PGG-Punishment,Representative treatment (general population sample) playing the Public Goods Game with peer punishment (PGG-Punishment).,1,"Subject pool = Representative (general adult population); Punishment institution = Yes (PGG-Punishment, peer punishment allowed)",Varies from Standard by adding a second-stage punishment opportunity while keeping the same participant pool.,1,True,Human adult participants played the PGG with punishment.,1,True,Controlled lab implementation with random matching and specified treatments.,1,True,Conducted in a hotel conference room outfitted as a mobile lab using z-Tree.,1,False,"Outcomes come from human choices, not simulations.",1,False,Results are empirical; formal model only used for interpretation.,1,4,Groups of N=4 are maintained in the punishment variant.,1,8,Eight periods of PGG-Punishment after eight periods of PGG-Standard.,1,0,"Same contribution options {0,6,14,20} as in PGG-Standard.",1,0,"Endowment of 20 tokens each period, all initially private.",0.9,0.5,Payoff function of stage 1 identical to PGG-Standard with a=0.5.,1,0,Same no-communication rule applies.,1,1,"Subjects observe individual contributions and earnings, then in punishment stage see received deduction points and own final earnings.",1,0,"Text: ""The punisher's identity was not revealed.""",1,0,No reward stage in the design.,1,1,"Repeated 8-period design; horizon likely known as in similar experiments, though not explicitly stated.",0.6,1,Second-stage peer punishment with deduction points is central to PGG-Punishment.,1,1,"""a deduction point had a cost of 1 token for the punisher"".",1,4,"Each deduction point ""reduced the earnings of the targeted subject by b=4 tokens.""",1,0,"Only costly deductions are available, no positive rewards.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Stage 1 is identical to PGG-Standard with wi=20 tokens.,1,N/R,Average contributions reported in tokens; normalized fraction of endowment is not explicitly provided.,0.4,8.88,"Table 3: ""Average individual contributions"" for Representative, PGG-Punishment, all periods = 8.88 tokens.",1,N/R,They mention profit decreases but not efficiency ratios relative to maximum.,0.2,N/R,Mean group payoff per period is not reported separately for this condition.,0.2,Italy,"Same Representative sample of residents in Ravenna province, Italy.",1,"Adults, stratified: 24.3% aged 18–39, 44.7% aged 40–59, 31.1% aged 60+",Same sample as Representative PGG-Standard.,1,"51.5% male, 48.5% female",Same Representative sample as in Table 2.,1,"18.5% 8th grade or lower, 47.5% high school, 34.0% college/Master/PhD",Education distribution unchanged across tasks.,1,On site,Same physical mobile lab environment as PGG-Standard for Representative sample.,1,"Two-stage repeated linear PGG: stage 1 contribution with discrete levels {0,6,14,20}; stage 2 peer punishment where each subject can assign 0–2 deduction points to each other member at own cost 1 per point, reducing target’s payoff by 4 per point; strangers matching across 8 periods.",Summarizes the key structural features of the punishment treatment.,1
