ject pool description applies to all treatments.,0.9,On site,Conducted in same physical lab using zTree.,1,"Same linear public good with centralized third-party punishment as baseline; only role labels changed to 'public official' and 'citizens'. 18 groups, 90 participants.",Treatment manipulates only labels per Section 5.2 and Table 1.,1
10.1086_691630.md,"Frame – Judge (appointed, no announcement)",Treatment where the outsider is labeled 'judge' and active players 'citizens'.,1,Framing of authority role: labeled Judge; authority selection: appointed; no policy announcement; no election; no prior experience,Differs from Public official by label 'judge' for authority.,1,True,Laboratory experiment with human subjects.,1,True,Controlled treatment manipulation (role label) and random assignment.,1,True,Conducted at Cologne Laboratory for Economic Research.,1,False,No simulations reported.,1,False,Study focuses on empirical behavior.,1,5,4 citizens + 1 judge per group.,1,10,Each treatment has 10 periods (Table 1).,1,1,Continuous contribution choice from 0 to 20 ECUs.,1,0,Endowment is private; contributions voluntary.,1,0.4,Same payoff function: pi_i = 20 - c_i + 0.4 * sum c_k.,1,0,No chat or communication reported.,0.9,1,"Citizens see contributions, punishments, and incomes each period.",1,0,Anonymity of judges and citizens preserved.,1,0,No rewards available.,1,1,Finite 10-period horizon known to subjects as in other treatments.,0.9,1,Judge has same punishment capabilities as authority in baseline.,1,1,Cost structure unchanged: 1 ECU per punished citizen.,1,80,"Judge can reduce a citizen’s income by up to 80 ECUs, total 80 per period.",1,0,Only punitive options described.,1,N/A,No reward option.,1,N/A,No reward option.,1,20,Citizens receive 20 ECUs each per period.,1,N/R,No average contributions by treatment provided.,0,N/R,Paper does not report numeric mean contribution in ECUs for Judge frame.,0,N/R,No explicit efficiency metrics per treatment.,0,N/R,Only mean individual earnings: authorities €23.21; active participants €16.36.,0.3,Germany,Same laboratory and recruitment context.,0.9,Mean 22.88,Table 1 lists mean age 22.88 for Judge treatment.,1,64.44% female,Table 1 lists percentage female 64.44.,1,University students (various majors),Same student pool.,0.9,On site,Conducted in same physical lab with zTree software.,1,"Same repeated linear public good with centralized punishment; frame labels authority as 'judge' and active players as 'citizens'. 90 participants, 18 judges.",Section 5.2 and Table 1 specify only framing differences.,1
