10.1086_691630.md,"Elect – Elected judge (announces policy, elected, no experience)",Election treatment where two candidates announce policies and are elected by two voters; elected one becomes judge.,1,Judicial frame with ex ante policy announcement and election of judge by voters; non-elected candidate receives lower fee; no prior judicial experience,"Builds on Announce: adds two candidates, two voters, and electoral selection.",1,True,Lab experiment with human subjects.,1,True,Controlled manipulation of selection mechanism (appointed vs elected).,1,True,Done in Cologne lab.,1,False,No simulated agents mentioned.,1,False,Primarily empirical results.,1,5,"Per group in the public-goods part there are still 4 citizens and 1 judge; voters and unelected candidate are additional roles, not in the contribution group.",0.9,10,Table 1 indicates each treatment has 10 periods.,1,1,Citizens choose any contribution 0–20 ECUs.,1,0,Endowments remain private before contributions.,1,0.4,Public goods technology unchanged.,1,0,No interactive discussion channel; voters only see policies.,0.9,1,"Citizens see within-group contributions, punishments, earnings.",1,0,Judges and citizens remain anonymous.,1,0,No reward scheme.,1,1,Finite 10 rounds as in other treatments.,0.9,1,Elected judge has same punishment power.,1,1,"One ECU cost per punished citizen, unchanged.",1,80,"Judge can reduce up to 80 ECUs per citizen, 80 total per period.",1,0,No reward option.,1,N/A,Rewards are unavailable.,1,N/A,Rewards are unavailable.,1,20,Citizens’ endowments remain 20 ECUs.,1,N/R,No explicit average contribution fraction reported for Elect treatment.,0,N/R,Paper does not provide numeric contributions for this treatment.,0,N/R,Efficiency not computed per treatment.,0,N/R,"Only mean earnings (authorities €23.21, active participants €17.82) reported.",0.3,Germany,Same German lab and student pool.,0.9,Mean 23.39,Table 1 lists mean age 23.39 for Elect.,1,54.69% female,Table 1: percentage female 54.69.,1,Un