and does not quantify average generosity rate.,0.1,N/R,No numeric donations reported for this run.,0.2,N/R,No aggregate efficiency metrics for this configuration.,0.1,N/R,No total payoff/wealth per group reported.,0.1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Agent-based simulation only.,1,"Same Sociodynamica environment as baseline. Here, agents start with altruistic strategy (ASt=1). The shame gene Sha is allowed to take positive values so agents can increase generosity after being punished. Punishment is present with its cost set to minimal value for both punisher and punished. Over time, most agents remain shameless (Sha=0), but unlike the baseline, alleles for punishers and non-punishers maintain similar frequencies, and punishment is not selected against.","Summarized from Results section description of column 1, row 2 and the general model.",0.9
