aging in non-commercial social behavior (ASt>0).',0.2,N/R,No numeric donation amounts.,0.2,N/R,No aggregate wealth figures for this condition.,0.1,N/R,No group payoff numeric results.,0.1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Simulation only.,1,"Row 3 simulations extend ASt to three alleles: 0 (avoid non-commercial), 1 (pure altruistic donations without direct personal gain), and 2 (egoistic reciprocity where donations increase mineral wealth via Gain). In cases where altruistic punishment (Cost>0) is present but shame is absent, evolution leads to many generous individuals (Gen>0), many punishers (Pun=1), and a substantial fraction of agents with ASt>0 (engaging in social donations or mutualistic investments).",Paraphrase of the Row 3 description focusing on the variant without shame.,0.7
