10.1016_j.joep.2017.03.007.md,TOP – Restricted single punisher ('Top Contributors as Punishers'),"Treatment described in 3.1.3 as 'restricted single punisher (TOP): The ""top contributors as punishers"" mechanism'.",1,"Punishment institution: centralized peer punishment with a single punisher each round, selected as one of the highest contributors; that punisher is immune from punishment.",3.1.3: 'only the “Top Contributor” is allowed to sanction'; footnote: selected top contributor is immune; non-selected top contributors have only hypothetical punishment.,0.95,True,Laboratory treatment with human subjects.,1,True,Part of controlled between-subjects experimental design.,1,True,Conducted at CEEL Lab.,1,False,No simulations used for this treatment.,1,False,No separate analytical derivations specific to this treatment.,1,4,Groups of 4 in all treatments.,1,20,20 periods.,1,1,Same 0–20 token contribution choice.,1,0,20-token private endowment each round.,1,0.4,Same payoff formula based on Fehr & Gächter parameters.,1,0,Instructions for TOP (Appendix A) explicitly forbid communication.,1,1,"Appendix A: at stage 2, top contributor sees how much others contributed and group average; others also receive similar info except they don’t punish.",1,0,Instructions and design emphasize anonymity and rotating labels; no identities of punishers revealed.,0.9,0,No rewards.,1,1,Appendix A: 'The experiment is composed by 20 rounds'; round number displayed on screen.,1,1,Top contributor can assign up to 10 costly points to each lower-contributing member.,1,0,Same convex cost table as UP (Appendix A); non-linear per point so encoded as 0 with explanation.,0.4,0.1,Appendix A: each point reduces recipient’s stage-1 earnings by 10%; max 100%.,1,0,Only punitive points are available.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,20,Appendix A: 'At the beginning of each round each participant will receive 20 tokens.',1,N/R,Only mean contribution amounts in tokens reported.,0.3,13.34,Table 2: 'Mean' contributions for TOP is 13.34 tokens.,1,N/R,"Earnings differences discussed and plotted, but no numeric efficiency measure.",0.2,N/R,Average earnings per treatment not tabulated numerically.,0.2,Italy,Same subject pool.,0.9,N/R,Not reported.,0.1,45% female overall sample,Aggregate sample description only.,0.6,Undergraduate students (55% Economics/Management majors),Same pool description.,0.8,On site,Same physical lab environment.,1,"Linear public goods game, partner matching, MPCR 0.4, 20 rounds, groups of 4, anonymous relabeling each round. In each round, only one top contributor (highest g_i) is randomly chosen among tied top contributors to be the sole actual punisher and is immune from punishment; others answer hypothetical punishment questions. Punisher can assign 0–10 points per co-player at convex cost; each point reduces recipients’ stage-1 payoff by 10%.","Compiled from Sections 3.1.3, 3.2 and Appendix A.",1
10.1016_j.joep.2017.03.007.md,FOUR – Restricted single punisher for four periods,Treatment labeled FOUR in 3.1.4: 'Restricted single punisher for FOUR periods (FOUR)'.,1,"Punishment institution: centralized peer punishment with a single punisher selected as top contributor in key periods (1,5,9,13,17); this punisher keeps the right to punish and is immune for four consecutive periods.","3.1.4: 'Top Contributor ... is the only subject who is allowed to sanction'; 'obtains this right not only for the current period, but also for the following three periods'; and for those four periods they are 'immune from others’ punishments'.",1,True,Lab treatment with human participants.,1,True,Part of controlled experimental design.,1,True,Conducted at CEEL Lab.,1,False,No simulation reported.,1,False,No standalone analytical model.,1,4,Same group size.,1,20,All treatments have 20 periods.,1,1,Same 0–20 contribution decision.,1,0,Endowment starts in private account.,1,0.4,Same parametric structure as Fehr & Gächter.,1,0,General instructions forbid communication; no exceptions for FOUR.,1,1,"As in TOP, subjects get information on others’ contributions.",0.9,0,Anonymity and rotating labels; no identity revelation of punishers.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism.,1,1,20-period horizon made common knowledge as in other treatments.,1,1,Top contributor has right to assign punishment points during the four-period tenure.,1,0,Same convex cost function as in UP/TOP.,0.4,0.1,Each point still reduces the target’s payoff by 10%; no change reported.,1,0,No reward option.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,20,Same 20-token endowment per round.,1,N/R,Only contributions in tokens reported.,0.3,8.82,Table 2: 'Mean' contributions for FOUR is 8.82 tokens.,1,N/R,Only qualitative and graphical comparisons of earnings across treatments.,0.2,N/R,No numeric group payoff table.,0.2,Italy,Same Italian undergraduate subject pool.,0.9,N/R,Not specified.,0.1,45% female overall sample,Only overall gender proportion 