gle-valued.,0.4,N/R,p (loss to thief per unit victim cost) is sampled; no single constant magnitude reported.,0.4,0,Game only includes costly punishment; no prosocial reward action.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/R,"Model specifies per-round payoffs s, c, p but not an explicit endowment per round.",0.2,N/R,No contribution variable; outcomes categorized as ‘punisher exploited’ vs ‘thief exploited’.,1,N/R,No contribution decisions; binary steal/punish actions only.,1,N/R,"They report proportions of learning outcomes, not efficiency ratios.",1,N/R,No aggregate payoff statistic over games reported.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely computational Monte Carlo simulation.,1,"Two-player repeated steal/punish game; thief action set: {steal, nothing}; victim action set: {punish, nothing}; payoffs parameterized by s (benefit to thief, loss to victim when stealing), c (cost to victim to punish), p (additional loss to thief when punished). RL agents use Q-learning with 8 internal states tracking last two moves; softmax action selection.",Summarized from Learning Dynamics for RL Agents and RL Simulations sections.,0.9
