10.3390_buildings12010019.md,"Numerical simulation – punishment mechanism, high punishment (2a+E above critical)",Section 4.4 also discusses the case when 2a+E is above the critical threshold causing both enterprises to move toward positive cooperation.,0.9,"Combined punishment parameter 2a+E set above a critical value between 4.5 and 6.0; other parameters at baseline (R=10, γ=0.45, α=1.5, β=0.6); initial x=y=0.5.","Section 4.4: 'When 2a+E is greater than a certain critical value between 4.5 and 6.0, the larger its value, the more the evolutionarily stable strategies ... tend to cooperate positively.'",0.8,False,Simulation without human participants.,1,False,No empirical experimental control.,1,False,Not lab-based.,1,True,MATLAB simulations with high punishment parameter.,1,True,Understood via analytical replicator conditions involving punishment term 2a+E.,0.9,2,Two enterprises modeled.,1,20,Same simulation structure.,0.7,1,Binary choice positive/negative cooperation.,0.7,N/A,No contributions/endowment.,1,N/R,No MPCR used.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No summaries/interface involved.,0.9,N/A,No human IDs.,1,N/A,No human IDs.,1,0,Not applicable.,1,1,Explicitly models punishment through 2a+E.,1,N/R,No detailed cost measure per punishment unit.,0.2,N/R,No tech parameter identified.,0.2,1,Indirect reward income a is part of punishment-reward mechanism.,0.8,N/R,Reward costs not modeled.,0.2,N/R,No such mapping.,0.2,N/R,Endowment not specified.,0.4,N/A,"Cooperation share is the outcome, but no human contributions.",1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency for high punishment not numerically reported.,1,N/R,No explicit payoff levels for high 2a+E case.,0.6,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Purely computational.,1,"Punishment mechanism treatment: when 2a+E is above the critical 4.5–6.0 range (strong punishment and indirect rewards), both enterprises’ evolutionarily stable strategies tend toward positive cooperation, as high punishment cost discourages opportunistic behavior.","Section 4.4: 'When 2 a+E is greater than a certain critical value between 4.5 and 6.0, the larger its value, the more the evolutionarily stable strategies of construction enterprises 1 and 2 tend to cooperate positively.'",1
