10.1186_1744-9081-9-3.md,"Implemented punishment block (central authority, punishment implemented on 2 of 13 trials)",One of the two punishment blocks where the central authority punishment rule was actually implemented in two of the 13 trials.,1,"Punishment condition: central authority punishment, implemented (participants told punishment may occur AND fines applied automatically on two high-contribution trials if individual contribution < group average).",Block differs from others by having both threat of punishment and actual implementation on specified trials.,1,True,Same human participant sample as other blocks.,1,True,Part of controlled lab experiment with randomised block orders and fixed punishment contingencies.,1,True,Conducted in on-site computer lab.,1,False,No computer-only agents; only payoff calculation was automated.,1,False,No standalone analytical model.,1,4,Groups of four per trial.,1,13,Explicitly states punishment blocks had 13 trials each.,1,1,Participants chose how much of 20 MUs to allocate to public vs private accounts.,1,0,All 20 MUs start in private account.,1,0.5,Same payoff function across blocks; MPCR derived from π_i = 20 - g_i + 0.5 * Σ g_j.,1,0,No communication mentioned.,0.9,1,Participants saw average group contribution and own earnings after each trial.,1,0,Centralized automatic punishment based on contributions; groups anonymous and no identities attached to fines.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism used.,1,0,Not told how many blocks or trials; no indication that remaining rounds were displayed.,0.5,1,Central authority punishment rule applied; participants could be fined if they contributed less than group average.,1,N/R,Paper does not specify size of the fine or its cost structure in MUs.,0,N/R,Magnitude of payoff reduction per punishment event is not reported.,0,0,No explicit reward mechanism beyond standard PGG payoffs.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Same 20 MU endowment per trial as all blocks.,1,N/R,Average contributions by block (in MUs) are discussed qualitatively but not given numerically; normalized rates not computed.,0,N/R,"Figure 2 shows mean contributions graphically, but values are not stated in numbers.",0.3,N/R,No statistics on total or relative efficiency per block.,0,N/R,"Only overall average monetary earnings from whole experiment reported, not by block.",0,UK,Same undergraduate sample from University of Nottingham.,0.9,"Mean 20.96, range 18–36",Single sample across all blocks.,1,67.1% female,Single sample across all blocks.,1,Undergraduate students,Same participant pool.,1,On site,Lab-based with physical attendance.,1,"Central authority punishment: on two designated high-contribution trials (group average 16–18 MUs), any participant contributing less than the group average was automatically fined; punishment contingencies were identical for all participants and did not depend on other players’ real behaviour across most trials (conditional information lottery with one real trial). Approximately 74.7% of participants experienced punishment.",Synthesizes punishment-rule description and endnote about proportion punished.,1
10.1186_1744-9081-9-3.md,"Non-implemented punishment block (central authority, punishment never implemented)","Second punishment block where participants were told about the same punishment rule, but fines were never actually applied.",1,"Punishment condition: central authority punishment, non-implemented (participants told they might be fined if they contribute less than group average, but punishment never occurs on any trial).",Only difference from implemented block is that the rule is never executed.,1,True,Same human subject experiment.,1,True,Part of manipulated within-subjects block design.,1,True,Same lab setting.,1,False,Human subjects only.,1,False,No separate analytical model.,1,4,Groups of four per trial.,1,13,States two punishment blocks had 13 trials each.,1,1,Participants freely chose allocation of 20 MUs between private and public accounts.,1,0,Entire endowment starts private.,1,0.5,Same payoff formula as other blocks.,1,0,No communication channels described.,0.9,1,Participants received average group contribution and own earnings feedback each trial.,1,0,"Punishment never implemented; in any case, mechanism was automatic and anonymous.",0.9,0,No reward mechanism.,1,0,Number of trials not described as being shown to participants.,0.5,1,"Rule is described and believed by participants; independent variable is whether expectation is implemented, not whether the rule formally exists.",1,N/R,Size/structure of hypothetical fine is not specified.,0,N/R,Magnitude of hypothetical deduction per punishment event not reported.,0,0,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Same game parameters as other blocks.,1,N/R,Only relative differences vs implemented punishment and standard blocks are reported; no absolute numerical contributions.,0,N/R,Figure 2 shows mean MU contributions graphically but values not given in text.,0.3,N/R,No per-condition efficiency values.,0,N/R,No per-block payoffs reported.,0,UK,Same participant pool.,