d or bonus allocation decision stage aside from basic allocation.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,100,“Dictators…were endowed with 100 points of money/candy.”,1,0.174,Mean generosity in DG with money is 17.4 points out of 100; normalized 17.4/100 = 0.174.,1,17.4,Reported as M_DG=17.4 in money condition (allocation to other).,1,N/R,No group payoff vs maximum payoff ratio reported; simple transfers between players.,1,N/R,"Only average allocations reported, not combined payoffs per pair.",1,United States,“We recruited 239 American participants…via Amazon Mechanical Turk.”,1,"M=30.6, SD=8.9 (adults)",Demographics section of Study 1.,1,91 women; remainder men/others (exact male count not specified),Study 1 demographics list 91 women out of 239.,0.9,N/R,No education data for MTurk sample reported.,1,Online,Participants recruited and tested via Amazon Mechanical Turk; tasks completed online.,1,One-shot DG repeated for 8 rounds with different ostensible partners; payoffs in money points converted probabilistically into a ~$20 monetary bonus; incentives framed as affecting chance of bonus.,"Procedure describes repeated one-shot rounds, virtual counterparts, and conversion of total earnings into lottery-like bonus.",1
