10.1177_0170840610372202.md,Abraham–God punishment-forgiveness process (textual hermeneutic analysis),"Paper is a conceptual/theological-ethical analysis of the Abraham myth and modern cases (SOX, TRC); no discrete experimental or simulation conditions are implemented.",1,N/A,No manipulated variables or contrasted empirical conditions; purely interpretive and theoretical.,1,False,"No human participants or empirical data collection; analysis is of texts, myths, and secondary literature.",1,False,"No randomization, control, or intervention; not an experiment.",1,False,No laboratory or experimental setting.,1,False,No computational or agent-based models; only conceptual discussion.,1,True,"Paper develops a conceptual/analytical framework (Knight of Faith, Scheler’s punishment model) via hermeneutic and philosophical reasoning without data.",1,0,No game or players; not a behavioral study.,1,0,No repeated-game structure is implemented; narrative has multiple incidents but not as an experiment.,1,0,"No contribution decision exists; not applicable, but schema requires numeric so set to 0.",0.5,N/A,No endowments or contributions; no humans in a game context.,1,N/A,No public goods game or multiplier.,1,0,No experimental communication channel; not applicable but set to 0 per schema.,0.5,0,No payoff or punishment summaries shown; not a game.,1,0,No experimental punishment mechanism with identities; theoretical discussion only.,1,0,No experimental rewards mechanism.,1,0,No rounds information presented to participants (none exist).,1,0,"Punishment is discussed conceptually, but no implemented punishment mechanism in an experiment or game.",1,N/A,No numeric punishment cost parameter.,1,N/A,No mapping from punishment points to losses is specified.,1,0,"Rewards/cooperation benefits are conceptual, not an experimental reward mechanism.",1,N/A,No numeric reward cost parameter.,1,N/A,No technical mapping from reward points to gains.,1,N/A,No tokens or monetary endowments assigned.,1,N