t game with two investor strategies (cautious C, unthinking K) and two trustee strategies (trustworthy T, untrustworthy U). Group composition: NI=10 investors, NT=5 trustees, repeated with continuation probability ω=0.9 (R=10 expected rounds). Government joins after T=5 rounds, then allows investors to report untrustworthy trustees. Punishment fine intensity δ=0.02; rewards δ to each successful reporting investor and punishes untrustworthy trustee with n·δ where n is number of successful reports. Dynamics modeled by two-population replicator equations for x (fraction of unthinking investors) and y (fraction of trustworthy trustees).",Summary of model description and parameters for the specific numerical example.,0.98
