ly.,1,N/A,Simulation only.,1,No human,Purely computational evolutionary dynamics.,1,"Same N-player repeated trust game as in the core model with NI=10, NT=5, r=0.8, R=10 (ω=0.9), T=5. Punishment fine intensity set to δ=0.06 (> (1−r)/NT). For this regime, theoretical analysis predicts a stable boundary equilibrium (0, y*), meaning all investors become cautious (x=0) while a positive fraction y* of trustees are trustworthy. Numerical phase portrait (Fig. 3(a)) shows trajectories converging to (0, y*).",Summarizes model details specific to this punishment level.,0.95
