d numerical study only.,1,"Same repeated N-player trust game with NI=10, NT=5, r=0.8, R=10, T=5. Punishment intensity δ=0.1 lies between δ* and 1−r. Theory predicts and simulations confirm an asymptotically stable interior equilibrium (x**, y**) where all four strategies (C, K, T, U) coexist. As δ increases and trustworthy trustees are more common, the fraction of unthinking investors (K) rises from zero as the perceived market environment improves.",Summarizes distinguishing properties of this punishment regime.,0.95
