ion.,1,"Same repeated N-player trust game with NI=10, NT=5, r=0.8, R=10, T=5. Punishment intensity δ=0.22 (> 1−r = 0.2). For this strong-punishment regime, the boundary equilibrium (0, y*) vanishes and only the interior equilibrium remains stable. Simulations (Fig. 5(a,b)) show coexistence of the four strategies with a high trust level, but with growing share of unthinking investors as punishment becomes very strong, which reduces reporting and hence punishment frequency, allowing some untrustworthy trustees to persist.",Captures qualitative dynamics and parameterization specific to δ=0.22.,0.95
