10.1016_j.chaos.2023.114031.md,"Numerical simulation with NT=1, δ=0.30 (interior center and periodic orbits)","Condition described under Case 2 (NT=1) with NI=10, NT=1, r=0.8, R=10, T=5, δ=0.3 corresponding to Fig. 7.",0.95,"Punishment fine δ set to 0.30 with NT=1 (case δ > 1−r, interior equilibrium is a center with periodic solutions)","Text states that when δ>1−r and NT=1, there is an interior equilibrium (x̂, ŷ) that is a center; numerical example uses δ=0.3.",0.98,False,"Still within the same theoretical-simulation framework, no human participants.",1,False,Not an empirical experiment.,1,False,No lab setting.,1,True,Fig. 7 shows numerical trajectories (closed orbits and time series) for this parameter set.,1,True,"Theorem 4 proves that the interior equilibrium (x̂, ŷ) is a center; simulations illustrate periodic solutions.",1,11,NT=1 and NI=10 imply N=11 players in each group.,0.95,10,R=10 (ω=0.9) again used.,0.98,1,Same basic trust-game payment rules; investors pay 1 to the single trustee when investing.,0.3,N/A,No public-goods endowment allocation for humans.,1,N/R,No MPCR defined for this trust-game setting.,1,N/A,No human communication.,1,0,"Simulated dynamical system, not an interface.",1,N/A,Identity not modeled.,1,N/A,Identity not modeled.,1,0,Rounds not displayed to any human participants.,1,1,Government punishment mechanism is active with δ=0.3 (>1−r).,1,N/R,Punisher cost not parameterized.,0.4,N/R,Fines defined by δ; no tech parameter reported.,0.4,1,Investors reporting untrustworthy trustee are rewarded with δ.,1,N/R,Reward cost not specified.,0.4,N/R,Reward mapping is direct; no separate tech parameter.,0.4,N/R,No explicit endowment per player described.,0.4,N/R,"Dynamics reported in terms of cyclic changes in trust and strategy composition, not contributions.",1,N/R,No numeric contribution amount data.,1,N/R,Efficiency not quantified.,1,N/R,No explicit payoff totals reported over the limit cycle.,0.9,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Study is analytical with supporting numerical simulations.,1,"Single-trustee (NT=1) repeated trust game with NI=10, r=0.8, R=10, T=5, δ=0.3 (>1−r). The system admits an interior equilibrium (x̂, ŷ) with 0 < x̂, ŷ < 1. The Jacobian at this point has zero trace and positive determinant, and via Volterra's principle and a first integral, Theorem 4 shows the point is a center. Numerical simulations (Fig. 7(a,b)) display closed orbits around (x̂, ŷ) and stable periodic fluctuations in trust: as many investors invest persistently, the single trustee tends to choose untrustworthy strategy U to exploit them; punishment via reporting later shifts the trustee back to T, leading to cycles.","Summarizes the qualitative behavior and key parameters of this NT=1, δ>1−r regime.",0.97
