 human,Agent-based computational simulation with social vaccine.,1,"Same meta-norms simulation as in the no-vaccine N/generations condition but with social vaccine agents always defecting and never punishing. Lower panel of Fig. 10 shows that with social vaccine, cooperative regimes are achieved regardless of population size and number of generations considered.",Summarized from Sec. 3.3.,0.9
10.1098_rsif.2024.0019.md,Mean-field well-mixed population with prosocial punishment bots (CP bots),Distinct analytical condition: infinite well-mixed population with bots that always play CP; outcomes vary over dilemma strength r and bot density ρ but core setup is one condition.,0.9,"Bot density ρ (0–0.5) and dilemma strength r (0–1) in an infinite well-mixed population; bots always play CP; imitation strength κ fixed at 0.1, no conformist transmission (α = 0).","The section 2.2 and Methods specify r and ρ as the main varied parameters in the well-mixed mean-field model with fixed CP bots and κ=0.1, α=0.",1,False,Purely theoretical mean-field model with no human data.,1,False,No controlled human or field experiment; only analytical/numerical modeling.,1,False,No lab setting or human participants.,1,False,"This condition uses mean-field ODEs, not Monte Carlo or agent-based simulation.",0.95,True,Mean-field equations (4.2–4.3) are solved numerically but represent an analytical deterministic model.,1,1000000,Infinite well-mixed limit; represented approximately by very large N; use large placeholder to indicate effectively infinite.,0.3,1,One-shot two-stage Prisoner’s Dilemma; strategies interact once per match; evolutionary time is not repeated game rounds.,0.9,1,"Players choose discrete actions (C, D, CP, DP) rather than contribution levels; mapped as free choice among strategies, treated as non all-or-nothing contribution game.",0.3,N/A,No endowment allocation or continuous contribution; only binary cooperate/defect with costs and benefits.,1,N/R,"Prisoner’s Dilemma formulation with benefit b and cost c, not a linear public goods game; MPCR not defined.",1,N/A,No human participants or communication mechanism.,1,0,Model payoffs are implicit; no user interface or feedback summaries to agents.,0.9,N/A,Agents are anonymous; no identities modeled.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism exists in the model.,1,0,No explicit information structure about number of rounds is modeled.,0.9,