icantly increase efficiency beyond Baseline, but no numeric efficiency.",0.4,N/R,No treatment-level mean payoffs.,0.2,United States,NYU-based lab experiment.,1,N/R,Not specified.,0.2,Mixed; proportion female varies by group,Sex composition measured and used as a regressor.,0.7,"University students (NYU, level N/R)",Participants are NYU students.,0.7,On site,Lab experiment described.,1,"Same heterogeneous public goods structure as Private Baseline; after seeing each member’s contribution, participants can spend points to reduce others’ earnings at 3:1 multiple. Types are private and cannot be inferred perfectly from contributions, leading to underuse of punishment on low-contributing High Demanders and concentration of punishment on Low Demanders, which undermines mechanism effectiveness.",From Section 2.2 and 4.1; includes described sanction stage and behavioral outcomes.,1
