n,Theoretical evolutionary game dynamics.,1,"Same dynamics ẋi=xi(1−xi)Li(−1+βy)[q(x)−p−bLi(1−xi)], ẏ=y(1−y)β(q(x)−p)∑Lj(1−xj). For β>1, initial states in (0,1)^n×(1/β,1) near {1}×[1/β,1] converge to an equilibrium (x=1,y=y0) with y0∈(1/β,1]. Each such (1,y0) is an attractive solution of the game (Theorem 2).","Paraphrase of Theorem 2 for β>1 and subsequent argument that (1,y0) is attractive.",1
10.1016_j.tpb.2015.06.005.md,"Model with redistribution of penalty, symmetric case, limited penalty (beta=1)","Section 5.1 studies a model where total penalty is partly redistributed among faithful members; symmetric case with L_i=L and α_i(x)=xi/n, β=1, yielding a strict NE (λ*1,1).",1,Redistribution rule α_i(x)=xi/n; symmetric production Li=L; penalty parameter fixed at β=1; penalty rate y chosen by cooperative (focus on y=1 in NE).,Assumptions for symmetric limited-penalty model stated explicitly in Section 5.1.,1,False,Analytical model of payoffs and NE; no participants.,1,False,Not an empirical experiment.,1,False,No lab or field implementation.,1,False,Stability assessed via Jacobian and eigenvalues; no computational simulation runs described.,1,True,Theorems 3–5 derive NE existence and stability conditions analytically.,1,N/R,n members plus cooperative considered; n not specified numerically.,0.5,1,"Static game with NE analysis, plus continuous-time stability; no repeated discrete rounds.",1,1,"xi∈[0,1], continuous effort choice.",1,N/A,"Theoretical producers, not experimental subjects with endowments.",1,N/R,Payoff not linear public good; no MPCR indicated.,1,N/A,No communication protocol; not an experiment.,1,0,No experimental feedback; purely analytical.,1,N/A,One cooperative entity administers penalty; no individual identities to reveal.,1,N/A,"Rewards are modeled as redistribution α_i(x)P(x,y), but no identity revelation in an experimental sense.",1,0,Static game; no rounds presented.,1,1,"Penalty P(x,y)=βy[q(x)−p]∑Li(1−xi) with β=1.",1,N/R,Cost to cooperative of imposing penalty not separated from redistribution and payoff.,0.5,N/R,"Penalty size is function of q(x), p, Li, and strategy profile; no single scalar factor reported.",0.5,1,"A part of total penalty P(x,y) is redistributed among members with xi>0 via α_i(x)P(x,y), which acts as a reward for faithfulness.",1,N/R,"Reward is funded from collected penalty, not from an external costly resource; no token cost specified.",0.5,N/R,Redistribution proportional to xi and total outside sales; not encapsulated by simple multiplier per reward token.,0.5,N/R,"Each member produces L units; L is a parameter, but no numeric value specified.",0.5,N/R,"Unique symmetric NE (λ*1,1) exists with λ*∈(0,1), but the exact numeric λ* is not given.",0.5,N/R,"Equilibrium contribution to cooperative is λ*L, but λ* and L are parameters without numeric instantiation.",0.5,N/R,"Theorems discuss stability, not explicit welfare ratios.",0,N/R,"Payoff expressions include parameters a,b,L,p,c and λ*, but no numeric solution provided.",0.5,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Game-theoretic analysis.,1,"Penalty P(x,y)=βy[q(x)−p]∑Li(1−xi), with β=1 and symmetric Li=L. Redistribution rule α_i(x)=xi/n for xi>0; each member payoff fi(x,1)=L(p−c)+ (xi/n)[a−bL∑(1−xj)−p]L∑(1−xj). There exists a unique λ*∈(0,1) such that profile (x=λ*1,y=1) is a strict Nash equilibrium (Theorem 4). Stability of this NE under partial adaptive dynamics is characterized by condition H=a−2nbL(1−λ*)−p>0 (Theorem 5).",Directly summarized from Section 5.1 and Theorems 4–5.,1
10.1016_j.tpb.2015.06.005.md,"Model with redistribution of penalty, symmetric case, effective penalty (beta>1)","Section 5.2 extends the symmetric redistribution model to effective penalties β>1, analyzing NE structure (Theorem 6) and dynamic stability (Theorem 7).",1,"Penalty effectiveness parameter β>1; symmetric production Li=L; redistribution rule via average contribution (1−(1/n)∑xi); penalty rate fixed at y=1 in NE; Cournot parameters a,b,p and production L subject to condition (5.13).",Section 5.2 explicitly distinguishes cases β>n/(n−1) vs 1<β<n/(n−1) plus condition b<(a−p)/((n+1)L).,1,False,Analytical derivations for NE existence and stability; no empirical data.,1,False,Not an experiment with subjects.,1,False,No lab implementation.,1,False,ODE stability determined analytically via Jacobian; no numerical simulations shown.,1,True,"Theorems 6 and 7 present conditions on β,a,b,L for strict NE and asymptotic stability.",1,N/R,Model defined for general n; not instantiated.,0.5,1,Game itself is static; dynamics considered in continuous time.,1,1,"Members choose xi∈[0,1]; continuous action space.",1,N/A,No human subjects or endowments.,1,N/R,Not a linear public good model.,1,N/A,No communication among players in experimental sense.,1,0,Analytical model; no interface.,1,N/A,Cooperative is a single punishing agent; no experimental identity mechanism.,1,N/A,"Rewards via redistribution, not through identity-based mechanism.",1,0,Static game plus continuous dynamics; no discrete rounds displayed.,1,1,"Effective penalty parameter β>1 applied to extra profit; cooperative payoff fn+1(x,y) includes βy(q(x)−p)ΣL(1−x).",1,N/R,Punishment is a transfer (or plus redistribution); explicit resource cost not specified.,0.5,N/R,"Penalty magnitude depends on β,y,q(x), and ΣL(1−x); no simple per-unit mapping given.",0.5,1,"Part of the collected penalty is redistributed among faithful members, effectively rewarding higher xi.",1,N/R,Rewards financed from penalty pool; no separate cost per reward unit provided.,0.5,N/R,Redistribution formula involves xi and Σ(1−xj); not a simple linear token technology.,0.5,N/R,Li=L parameter; no numeric value.,0.5,N/R,"For β>n/(n−1), symmetric strict NE is (1,1); for 1<β<n/(n−1) and condition (5.13), strict NE is (λ*1,1) with λ*∈(0,1). λ* is not given numerically.",0.5,N/R,Equilibrium contributions are λ*L or L but parameters remain symbolic.,0.5,N/R,No explicit welfare calculations or ratios reported.,0,N/R,Payoffs given symbolically as functions of parameters; no numeric values.,0.5,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Analytical NE and stability analysis.,1,"For β>1 in symmetric redistribution model, cooperative payoff is fn+1(x,y)=(1−(1/n)∑xi)[βy(q(x)−p)∑Lj(1−xj)]. With y=1 and symmetric xi=λ, member payoff derivative Di fi(λ1,1) determines NE. Case (A) β>n/(n−1): (1,1) is the only symmetric strict NE. Case (B) 1<β<n/(n−1) and b<(a−p)/((n+1)L): there exists unique λ*∈(0,1) with (λ*1,1) a strict NE (Theorem 6). Under condition (5.13), there exists β0∈(1,n/(n−1)) such that for all β0<β<n/(n−1), this NE (λ*1,1) is asymptotically stable for the associated partial adaptive dynamics (Theorem 7).",Summarizes Theorems 6–7 and conditions on β and parameters.,1
