10.1016_j.physa.2017.09.046.md,"Simulation – spatial PD with adaptive disconnection (β > 0, varying b and c)","Main simulation condition where β>0 introduces adaptive interaction; covers results in Figs. 1–5 over ranges of b, c, β.",0.9,"Disconnecting strength β ∈ (0,1], including values around phase transitions; temptation b ∈ (1,2); sucker’s payoff parameter c varied (affecting R=b−c); noise K=0.1; lattice 200×200; initial cooperator fraction P0=0.5.","Section 3.1 and tables/figures describe varying β, b, c with fixed other parameters.",0.9,False,Monte Carlo simulations only.,1,False,Not an empirical controlled experiment.,1,False,No physical lab setting applicable.,1,True,Explicitly described as simulations on periodic lattices.,1,False,Analytical reasoning supports but does not replace simulations.,0.9,40000,Simulations on 200×200 lattice.,1,100,They average over η=100 independent steps; use as effective number of evolutionary updates.,0.7,0,Players choose C or D each interaction; no graded contribution.,1,N/A,Not a contribution game.,1,N/A,No public good or multiplier.,1,N/A,Artificial agents do not communicate via chat.,1,N/A,No interface in simulations.,1,N/A,Identity display not meaningful for simulated agents.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,Agents do not observe horizon.,1,1,Defectors are punished structurally by probabilistic disconnection with probability β>0.,1,N/R,"No explicit cost per disconnection; only opportunity loss of foregone payoffs, not parameterized.",0.2,N/R,Disconnection prevents any payoff that round; not expressed as per-token multiplier.,0.3,0,There is no additional positive incentive mechanism beyond interaction payoffs.,1,N/A,No reward option.,1,N/A,No reward option.,1,N/A,"Game framed in payoff units, not spending a fixed endowment.",1,N/A,"Key outcome is fraction of cooperators and extinction conditions, not contributions.",1,N/A,Binary PD without contribution levels.,1,N/R,They do not report normalized efficiency; only qualitative