ator receives 100 MUs; third party has 50 MUs but focal contributor is allocator with 100.,1,N/R,"This paper reports punishment levels, not distribution of offers m_a.",0,N/R,No numeric summary of allocator offers is provided here.,0,N/R,No aggregate welfare or efficiency measures are reported.,0,N/R,Group payoff statistics are not provided.,0,N/R,Fehr & Fischbacher (2003) are cited; their sample country not stated in this text.,0,N/R,No demographic info provided.,0,N/R,No demographic info provided.,0,N/R,No demographic info provided; likely students but not stated.,0,On site,Standard economic lab experiment circa 2003; no indication of online implementation.,0.7,Allocator endowed with 100 MUs chooses transfer to recipient; third party endowed with 50 MUs can spend up to 50 on punishment at efficiency r_p = 3; one-shot third-party punishment game.,Summarized directly from Sect. 3 description.,1
