aphs and regression effects.,0,0.97,Table 4 reports social efficiency of 97% for punishment in the treatment trial.,1,N/R,"Paper provides relative welfare gains and efficiency, not absolute group payoffs.",0,India,"Same sample: households around Bengaluru, India.",1,Mean ≈ 42.15 years in punishment treatment,Table 1 provides treatment-specific mean ages.,1,58.75% male in punishment treatment,Table 1 lists gender share for punishment.,1,Mean 6.49 years schooling in punishment treatment,Table 1 education by treatment.,1,Field experiment,Framed field experiment in actual communities.,1,"Same dynamic 4-player groundwater CPR game as baseline; in treatment trial, payoff function adds expected penalty term: π_it = α x_it − (γ/2)x_it^2 − φ d_t x_it − |p z (x_it − s)|, with p = 1/5 monitoring probability, z = 100 tokens per excess hour, s = 1 hour allowed; random monitoring via 10-sided die; identity of monitored player determined by pre-assigned numbers.",Summarizes punishment-specific payoff modification and monitoring details.,1
