10.1098_rspb.2021.1611.md,Sole-Punisher scenario – immune sole punisher,Condition where one group member is the only player allowed to punish and is de facto immune to punishment.,1,"Scenario: Sole-Punisher; Immunity: immune sole punisher (1 of 4 players per group, only one who can punish and cannot be punished)",Independent variables are scenario structure (only one punisher) and role of that sole punisher.,1,True,Human laboratory experiment.,1,True,Scenario and roles manipulated by experimenters.,1,True,Run in HEC-LABEX lab.,1,False,No simulation models.,1,False,No purely analytical treatment; data are behavioral.,1,4,All scenarios use groups of four.,1,5,Participants play 5 repeated rounds under perfect-stranger design.,1,1,Contribution choice is 0–20 MU.,1,0,20 MU initial endowment in private account.,1,0.4,Same linear PGG parameters in all scenarios.,1,0,No chat or communication options described.,0.9,1,Contributions and payoffs of each group mate shown before punishment phase.,1,0,"Punishees only see amount deducted, not punisher identity.",1,0,No reward mechanism.,1,1,Participants told the number of rounds (five).,0.9,1,Sole punisher can pay to punish others.,1,1,Punishment cost is 1 MU to reduce 3 MU.,1,3,1 MU spent leads to 3 MU deducted from target.,1,0,No rewarding stage described.,1,N/A,Rewards not available.,1,N/A,Rewards not available.,1,20,Same 20 MU endowment per round.,1,0.26,Immune sole punishers declined from 40% to 12%; approximate mean over 5 rounds ~26%.,0.6,5.2,ContributionRate (0.26) × 20 MU = 5.2 MU.,0.6,N/R,Efficiency for sole-punisher role not reported; only punishment costs vs benefits discussed qualitatively.,0,N/R,No detailed payoff by scenario and role.,0,Switzerland,Same lab and participant pool.,1,"Mostly under 26; 134 <20, 257 age 20–25, 23 age 26–30, 2 age 30–35, 3 >35, 1 not reported",Sample description for all experimental conditions.,1,"202 female, 215 male, 2 other, 1 declined",Overall gender composition for entire experiment.,