an participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Lattice Monte Carlo evolutionary simulations with AP and selfish players.,1,"Score-dependent viability on lattice: each player dies with probability inversely proportional to its score; one of its nearest neighbors colonizes the open site randomly. If AP reduces its neighbor's score, the neighbor’s death probability increases and AP can colonize the site, effectively yielding a spite-like advantage. AP can invade the selfish population starting from low density in both lattices and complete-mixing, but requires a lower fine in the lattice than in complete-mixing.",Summarizes model rules and the key comparative result between lattice and complete-mixing.,0.95
