ture as Social–Punishment condition, but with Non-social group identity created via square puzzle task with relatively little sharing and exchange. This condition is pivotal for the main result: punishment significantly increases Non-social investors’ trust towards out-group trustees relative to No Punishment.","Summarized from Sections 3.1 and 5.1, focusing on Non-social with punishment.",1
