w horizon.",0.8,1,Authority chooses enforcement rule that deducts 24 tokens according to signals.,1,24,Enforcement rule deducts 24 tokens from each punished citizen.,1,24,Each punishment action results in 24 tokens removed from punished citizen per enforcement event; one unit of 'punishment' equals 24 tokens.,0.8,0,No positive rewards; only punishment via deductions.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Each citizen has a 20-token endowment per period.,1,2.93,Average group contribution is 2.93 of 4 citizens contributing under this condition (Table/Fig. 3); this equals fraction of contributors since each has same endowment and all-or-nothing choice.,1,58.6,2.93 contributors × 20 tokens each = 58.6 tokens contributed per group on average.,0.9,N/R,No efficiency ratio (actual/maximum payoff) reported for this specific condition and not derivable without full payoff components including punishments.,0.4,N/R,Average total group payoff under this specific condition not reported and cannot be computed from given summary stats.,0.3,United States,"Sessions at NYU (New York) and Yale (New Haven, CT); participants are university students in the U.S.",0.9,Median 20,Methods: 'the median age was 20.',0.9,46% female,Methods: 'A total of 46% of the subjects were female.',0.9,University students; 8% economics majors; 27% social science majors,Subjects recruited from university pools; proportions by major reported.,0.9,On site,Conducted in physical university laboratories (NYU CESS and Yale Behavioral Research Laboratory).,1,"Linear public goods game with centralized authority (one of five players) selecting investment in accuracy and an enforcement rule. Signals about citizen contributions are noisy with 25% error under medium accuracy. Under PATS rule, authority punishes (deducts 24 tokens from) each citizen with a 'kept' signal. Citizens’ decisions do not affect each other’s material payoffs beyond their contributions; repeated 20 periods with random reassignment of groups and roles.",Summarizes structural details from Methods section specific to this configuration.,1
