10.1016_j.geb.2009.07.007.md,Section 3.4 – Dictator game with envy preferences (theoretical model),Single underlying dictator game structure analysed with different welfare principles; no empirical condition.,1,"Envy parameter α > 0; complier share κ ∈ (0,1); guilt cost g; total pie normalized to 1","Section 3.4 defines underlying utility u_i(π) including α and notes pie is normalized to 1; κ,g affect norms.",1,False,No subjects are run; paper only references external empirical work.,1,False,The dictator games in this section are purely model-based.,1,False,No lab implementation here.,1,False,No computational or simulation results.,1,True,"Predictions about giving x are derived analytically as functions of α, κ, g.",1,2,Dictator game defined with player 1 and player 2.,1,1,One-shot dictator decision.,1,1,"Player 1 chooses x ∈ [0,1]; continuous, not limited to all-or-nothing.",1,N/A,No human endowment mechanism in a real experiment; theoretical allocation of a normalized pie.,1,N/R,"Dictator game is a transfer, not a linear public good; MPCR not defined.",1,N/A,No procedural communication described.,1,0,One-shot interaction; no summaries are modelled.,0.5,N/A,No punishment.,1,N/A,No formal reward mechanism distinct from the dictator’s transfer decision.,1,0,Single decision; no display of rounds.,1,0,No costful punishment stage.,1,N/A,No punishment.,1,N/A,No punishment.,1,0,"Transfers are the main action, but no separate post-play reward technology is defined.",0.8,N/A,No formal reward stage/cost.,1,N/A,No formal reward stage.,1,1,"Total monetary amount normalized to 1, which dictator allocates between self and recipient.",1,N/R,"Model provides thresholds for giving vs. zero but not a fixed numeric rate independent of α, κ, g.",0.3,N/R,"Equilibrium giving x is symbolic (min{1/2, g} etc.) and parameter-dependent.",0.4,N/R,Utility-based welfare is analyzed rather than monetary efficiency ratios.,0.2,N/R,"Focus is on utility with envy, not reported aggregate monetary pay