ted.,0.6,Netherlands,Same lab and recruitment base.,0.9,N/R,No specific age info for extra treatments.,1,N/R,Gender composition not reported.,1,Mainly undergraduate university students from various fields,Same subject pool for all sessions.,1,On site,Conducted in CREED laboratory.,1,"First (vulnerability choice) stage is removed. Each subject is matched to a subject from a previous Gradual session and assigned that subject’s sequence of possible punishment levels exogenously, so that the distribution of (x1,x2) pairs exactly mimics the Gradual treatment. Within each round: Stage 1 (assignment): own possible punishment level is given and revealed; Stage 2: PD with payoffs (C,C)=(55,55), (C,D)=(5,70), (D,C)=(70,5), (D,D)=(25,25); Stage 3: optional punishment with 4-point cost and partner losing their own assigned punishment level. Same random rematching in groups of 8 and same social history screen with punishment levels, actions, and punishment decisions.",Directly from description of ExGradual treatment in Section 4.,1
