orted.,1,Mainly undergraduate university students from various fields,Same recruitment pool applies.,1,On site,Conducted in the CREED laboratory.,1,"Identical to ExGradual except that exogenous possible punishment level sequences are taken from subjects in the Leap treatment rather than Gradual, reproducing the Leap distribution of (x1,x2) pairs. No endogenous stage: subjects receive assigned possible punishment levels each round, then play the PD ((C,C)=(55,55), (C,D)=(5,70), (D,C)=(70,5), (D,D)=(25,25)), then can punish at cost 4 with partner losing their own assigned punishment level. Same rematching and social history screen as other punishment treatments.",From description of ExLeap in Section 4 and comparative explanation in Section 5.3.,1
