ed.,0.6,On site,Lab sessions at a university using z-Tree.,1,"Two-player linear public goods game with individuals as decision units. Each subject endowed with 40 points, chooses integer contribution 0–40 to group account. Payoff for subject k: π_k,t = 0.5·(40 − c_k,t) + 0.4·(c_k,t + c_l,t). Partner matching: subjects matched with same individual for all 15 periods; no communication allowed.",Summarizes rules in Section 2.2 and the definition of I-P.,1
