10.1162_ARTL_a_00251.md,"Structured population simulation – diminishing returns model (baseline E=0.75, M=0.1, beta=300, gamma=0.0075)","Figure 5a describes a version of the model where investment in the public good directly increases carrying capacity with parameters E=0.75, G=20, M=0.1, beta=300, gamma=0.0075.",0.95,"Ecological feedback form: diminishing returns of productive public good on carrying capacity (Kj(t)=G+β[1−exp(−γ h_j n_cj B)] with β=300, γ=0.0075) in structured population (Ng not explicitly given but consistent with Ng=50) with G=20, M=0.1, E=0.75.",This condition contrasts with earlier fixed-total-carrying-capacity hard selection and introduces diminishing returns via β and γ.,0.9,False,Simulation-based model only.,1,False,"Computational scenario, not empirical.",1,False,No human lab.,1,True,Figure 5 describes dynamics produced by simulations for the modified K_j function.,1,False,Dynamical behavior obtained numerically.,0.9,20,"Group size parameter G=20, as stated for Figure 5a.",0.9,1,One interaction per generation.,0.8,0,Binary cooperate/defect decisions.,0.8,N/A,No endowment concept.,1,N/R,Not reported.,0.5,N/A,No communication modeled.,1,0,No explicit summaries shown to agents.,0.9,N/A,No identity-handling modeled.,1,N/A,No identities for rewards.,1,0,No information on total generations for agents.,0.9,1,Punishment term remains present through E(1-hj)(1-rj) n_cj B / n_dj.,1,N/A,Punishment funded through public good fraction.,1,N/R,"Only efficiency parameter E, no separate punishment multiplier.",0.6,1,Reward term E(1-hj) rj B in cooperator growth rate.,1,N/A,Rewards paid from institutional pool.,1,N/R,No explicit reward technology separate from E.,0.6,N/R,Endowment not defined.,0.5,N/R,"Text states that in this model individuals do not overinvest in productive public goods and cooperation remains stable, but does not quantify the stationary cooperation level.",0.5,N/R,No raw contribution values reported.,0.4,N/R,"Improved stability is discussed qualitatively, but no efficiency ratio is reported.",0.4,N/R,No summary group payoff vectors presented.,0.4,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Computational simulations only.,1,Modified carrying capacity: K_j(t)=G+β[1−exp(−γ h_j(t) n_cj(t) B)] with β=300 and γ=0.0075; growth rates become rho_cj= rho0 − C + E(1−h_j) r_j B and rho_dj= rho0 − E(1−h_j)(1−r_j) n_cj B / n_dj; parameters: G=20; M=0.1; E=0.75; B=0.9; C=0.1; rho0=2; mu=0.001; sigma=0.1; Ng implied to remain 50.,All functional forms and parameter values taken from the subsection describing the diminishing returns model and Figure 5a caption.,0.95
