ents at National Taipei University.,1,On site,Laboratory environment with physical attendance.,1,"Same two-stage VCM with heterogenous MPCRs and peer punishment as other treatments. In the hetero-pairwise network, each low-MPCR subject is connected only to one high-MPCR subject and vice versa; these paired subjects observe each other's contribution and MPCR and can impose at most one punishment (cost 1, impact −3) on their partner. No links to same-MPCR players.",Network topology from design description of hetero-pairwise network.,1
10.1007_s10588-017-9244-6.md,Simulation – No punishment mechanism,Paper defines five series of simulations; one is explicitly 'conducted without introducing a punishment mechanism'.,1,"Punishment mechanism: none; Organizational structure parameters (levels: 1–4, span of control categories: 4, 8, 12) varied across organizations.","Main manipulated factor across the five series is the punishment mechanism; within each series, hierarchies (levels and span of control) vary.",0.88,False,"Authors repeatedly state this is an agent-based simulation with artificial agents, no human participants.",1,False,No human or field experiment; purely computational agent-based simulations.,1,False,Not a lab or online human experiment; it is a computer simulation.,1,True,Described as 'agent-based simulation model' and 'computer simulations' throughout.,1,False,No closed-form or proof-based analytical model is presented; focus is on simulation runs.,1,1428,They note organizations had an 'average size of 1428 agents'; precise per-organization sizes vary but average is best available numeric descriptor.,0.4,20,Section 6: 'A simulation run consisted of a repeated public goods game of 20 decision rounds'.,1,1,"Agents contribute a real-valued fraction of endowment via Eq. (4), not just all-or-nothing.",1,N/A,No human subjects; this parameter defined only for human games.,1,N/R,Utility Eq. (5) effectively uses average of group contributions but no explicit marginal per-capita return parameter is given.,0.2,N/A,No human communication; purely simulated agents.,1,1,Agents observe others’ contributions to compute 'perception about cooperation'; effectively they receive summary info each round.,0.8,0,"Identity visibility is not modeled; punishers act based on roles and contributions, not on disclosed identities.",0.6,0,No reward mechanisms implemented or discussed.,1,1,"Agents behave differently in last round based on known final round (Finding 3 and algorithm lines 7–14), implying horizon is known