10.1007_s10588-017-9244-6.md,Simulation – Punishment: supervisor punishes most egoistic subordinate,One of four punishment mechanisms: 'The supervisor punishes the most egoistic direct subordinate with the smallest contribution to the public good.',1,"Punishment mechanism: supervisor punishes single most egoistic direct subordinate in each organizational unit; Organizational structures (1–4 levels; span of control 4, 8, 12) varied.","This series is defined by that specific punishment rule, with hierarchy parameters varied as in Table 3.",0.9,False,Agent-based simulation with artificial agents.,1,False,No empirical experiment; purely computational.,1,False,Not a lab experiment.,1,True,Described as agent-based simulations.,1,False,"Uses simulation, not analytical derivation.",1,1428,Average organization size reported as 1428 agents; used as approximate player count descriptor.,0.4,20,Each simulation run is a 20-round repeated public goods game.,1,1,Contributions are continuous fractions of endowment.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/R,No explicit marginal per-capita return constant specified.,0.2,N/A,No communication among simulated agents beyond modeled perceptions.,1,1,Agents observe others’ contributions in their unit to compute perceptions.,0.8,0,Punishment is rule-based (supervisor to specific subordinate) with no notion of identity revelation beyond structural roles.,0.6,0,No rewards.,1,1,Last round behavior depends on knowledge that round 20 is final.,0.9,1,This mechanism explicitly uses punishment via fines and punisher costs.,1,1,"Cost to supervisor: its endowment divided by number of subordinates, i.e., cost scales linearly with 1 'unit' of its own endowment share per punished event; normalized endowment assumed 1.",0.4,0.4,Fine to punished agent is p percent; p is set to 40% of endowment (Section 7.2).,0.95,0,Only punishment mechanisms are modeled.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,1,"Endowments defined on [0,1], with fines as % of endowment; initial equal endowment normalized to 1.",0.7,N/R,"Only relative comparisons and graphs (e.g., lower aggregate contribution than punishing-all cases); no single numeric value.",0.2,N/R,No absolute amount data reported.,0.1,N/R,Efficiency not computed or reported.,0.1,N/R,No total payoff outcomes reported.,0.1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely computational agent-based model.,1,"Same base game and population as no-punishment condition. Punisher: supervisor of each organizational unit. Each round, for each unit, supervisor identifies subordinate with smallest contribution and imposes fine of 40% of that agent’s endowment; supervisor pays a cost equal to its endowment divided by number of subordinates, which is added to public good. Punishment does not include top-level agents who lack a supervisor.",Details taken from Section 5.4 mechanism 1 and Section 7.2 fine definition.,0.95
