t round) punish the single most egoistic agent (smallest contribution). Each punisher pays cost = its endowment divided by number of neighbors (agents in unit). Punished agent pays fine of 40% of its endowment. Supervisor is not involved. Simulation findings: having multiple small units (small span of control) increases cooperation via stronger group pressure and positive perceptions.",Mechanism from Section 5.4 item 3; effects summarized from Observations 1 and 3.,0.95
