10.1017_s0266267121000195.md,N/A,"The paper is purely theoretical/philosophical and does not report any concrete experiment, simulation, or observational condition with specific parameters.",1,N/A,No experimental or observational conditions with manipulated or grouped independent variables are described; only illustrative anecdotes and literature references.,1,False,"No new data with human participants are collected; all discussions of Singapore littering, traffic lights, footbinding etc. are illustrative or secondary-source based.",1,False,The article does not describe any controlled experiment or field experiment that it runs; it only references other scholars’ work conceptually.,1,False,No lab or lab-like setting with participants is reported.,1,False,"No agent-based models, numerical simulations, or computer experiments are presented.",1,True,"The paper develops formal/analytical constructs (e.g., PRACTICE, NORM, GOVERN, SCOOP, SCOOR) and uses game-theoretic notation and reasoning without data.",1,0,"No concrete game implementation with a fixed number of players is instantiated; only generic notation like ‘players’ in prisoner's dilemma, coordination games, etc.",1,0,Theoretical discussion only; repeated vs single-shot games mentioned abstractly without specifying actual experimental round counts.,1,0,There is no actual contribution decision implemented; config is not applicable. Using 0 by default and clarifying non-applicability.,0.9,N/A,No public-goods style experiment with endowments is run; hence no default allocation exists.,1,N/A,No linear public goods game or marginal per capita return is specified in an implemented experiment.,1,N/A,No participant interaction protocol is implemented; no chat/communication manipulation.,1,N/A,No actual feedback or information screens are implemented for participants.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism is experimentally implemented.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism is experimentally implemented.,1,N/A,No human-subject game with a defined horizon is run.,1,0,"Punishment is only discussed conceptually (sanctions, fines) and via external examples; no mechanism is implemented in a new experiment.",1,N/A,No specific punishment technology with per-unit cost is instantiated.,1,N/A,No mapping from spent tokens to punishment is defined in an implemented game.,1,0,Rewards are not implemented in any new experiment; they appear only in general discussion.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism with explicit per-unit costs is set up.,1,N/A,No reward technology is parameterized in an experiment.,1,N/A,"No experimental endowments are given to subjects; examples like payoffs c and d are symbolic, not experimental currencies.",1,N/A,No actual contributions are measured; there is only conceptual discussion of cooperation vs defection.,1,N/A,No numeric contributions (tokens/points) are reported.,1,N/A,No realized payoffs or efficiency measures from an implemented game are reported.,1,N/A,No experimental payoff data are collected.,1,N/A,"There are no human participants recruited by this study; only populations are mentioned illustratively (e.g., Singaporeans, Swedes, Chinese historically).",1,N/A,No human-subject sample is defined by the author.,1,N/A,No participants are recruited.,1,N/A,No participant pool is described.,1,No human,The work is purely theoretical/analytical without human subjects or field/online implementation.,1,"The paper defines abstract game-theoretic constructs (coordination vs cooperation/mixed-motive games, variables c and d, delta parameters for norm weight, SCOOP and SCOOR indices) but does not instantiate a concrete payoff matrix or design with actual subjects.",Summarizes the nature of games discussed while clarifying their purely theoretical status.,1
