.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/R,Per-round income drawn uniformly from 20–100 ECU; no single fixed endowment per round.,1,N/R,Baseline used only for norms; contribution (declaration) behavior not separately reported by treatment-country for this baseline.,0.5,N/R,No baseline-specific average declaration amount reported.,0.5,N/R,No payoff-efficiency statistics reported.,1,N/R,No group-earnings statistics reported.,1,Moldova,Sessions conducted at ASEM in Chisinau.,1,N/R,Only that they are students is reported; no age stats.,1,N/R,No gender composition provided.,1,University students,‘All participants were students at one of the universities where the experiment was conducted.’,1,On site,"Lab sessions at physical university labs, not online.",1,"Tax evasion game with 4-player groups, 20% audit probability each round, 40% tax on declared income, 1.5× tax penalty on undeclared income if audited; no feedback about others; norm elicitation questionnaire on social acceptability of reporting after the 15 rounds.",Summary of core institutional features for this condition.,1
