 reported as strategy frequencies C, P, D (Figs. 4–5); no explicit contribution rate.",0.3,N/R,No numeric summary of contributions.,0.2,N/R,No explicit efficiency numbers.,0.2,N/R,Group average payoffs used internally for conflict but not reported numerically.,0.2,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Simulated community-structured population.,1,"M = 20 communities of size N = 50. Within each community, PGG/P with c = 0.8, r = 3, beta = 20, gamma = 5, selection w1 (e.g., 0.1). Local Fermi updating as before. With probability m' = m N / (m (N - 1) + 1) (derived to match average copying count), a group conflict step occurs: two communities I and J are sampled; their average payoffs \bar{pi}_I, \bar{pi}_J computed; one community is replaced wholesale by a copy of the other with probability p = 1 / (1 + exp(w2 (\bar{pi}_I - \bar{pi}_J))) and 1 - p, where w2 = 1. This implements group selection based on group mean fitness.",Summarized from Section 4 and the m' expression.,0.95
