t are not reported as outcome measures.,0.2,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,All results from agent-based simulations on a computer.,1,"Meta-population with M = 20 communities of N = 50 individuals. Within each community, PGG/P with parameters c = 0.8, r = 3, beta = 20, gamma = 5. Local updating with probability 1 - m via Fermi process with fitness f = exp(w1 pi), selection strength w1. With probability m = 0.05, a fitness-based migration (cross-community Fermi updating) step occurs: two individuals i, j sampled from entire metapopulation; j is replaced by an offspring of i with probability p(j -> i) = 1 / (1 + exp(w2 (pi_j - pi_i))) with selection strength w2 (e.g., w2 = 1 in baseline, varied in Fig. 7(b)), with mutation probability mu = 0.0025 assigning one of the other pure strategies.",Summarized from Section 5 and Table 1.,0.95
