10.1098_rspb.2019.1943.md,Theoretical two-community cross-scale cooperation model,Paper presents a stylized dynamical model of two interacting communities managing a common-pool resource with cross-scale biophysical and social interactions; no separate empirical treatments are defined.,0.98,"Biophysical coupling strength δ (0–0.5), social coupling strength λ (0–0.5), norm-setting scenario (uncollaborative vs collaborative), and assumed social equilibrium of subsystem 2 (φ^(2)* = 0 or 1); effort factor μ^(1) varied, μ^(2) fixed at 2.95 in many analyses.","These parameters are systematically varied to study different qualitative regimes (phases) of the model (purely biophysical: λ=0, purely social: δ=0, combined: δ,λ>0; norm scenarios and φ^(2)* = 0 or 1 are explicitly contrasted).",0.96,False,"Model is purely theoretical with no human participants; described as stylized model, analytical and numerical approaches, and no data available.",1,False,No controlled experiment with participants; only mathematical/agent-based style dynamical modeling.,1,False,No lab or field setting; entirely theoretical.,1,True,They numerically solve coupled ODEs and compare with perturbation approximations; also reference agent-based simulations in prior work though this paper itself uses differential equations with numerical solutions.,0.9,True,"They derive and analyze ODEs, use perturbation theory, fixed point analysis, and phase plots.",1,50,They assume symmetrical populations n^(i) ≡ n and specify n=50 in the caption of figure 2.,0.95,0,Model is continuous-time replicator dynamics with no discrete rounds; use 0 here to indicate not applicable to round-based games.,0.9,1,"Agents choose between cooperative effort e_c and defective effort e_d; effectively two discrete effort levels, but this does not match the requested coding where 1 means any amount and 0 means all-or-nothing; however, effort choice is binary, so coded as 0 would better match; yet in original TSL it is a 2-strategy game,