ent per round.,0.4,N/R,"Primary DV is distribution of fixation probabilities of mutants, not contribution behavior.",0.4,N/R,No numeric average contributions reported for robustness test.,0.4,N/R,Efficiency is not numerically presented in this figure.,0.4,N/R,Group payoff levels are implicit in payoff calculations but not reported numerically.,0.4,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,All computations are conducted on high-performance computing resources.,1,"Three-person public-goods/donation game with resident CAPRI-3 strategy (memory length m=5). Mutants sampled randomly from the huge space of deterministic strategies with memory m=5: 5×10^6 mutants were tested. Parameters: population size N=10, benefit of cooperation b=2, error probability ε=10^-4, selection strength σ=1. Result: none of the tested mutants achieved fixation probability above 1/N, suggesting strong evolutionary robustness of CAPRI-3 against random mutants with same memory length.",Summarizes the structure and main findings of the n=3 robustness test.,0.97
