icit numeric average contributions per player reported.,0.4,N/R,"While CAPRI-2 is said to achieve near-full cooperation (probability 0.999), efficiency as payoff ratio is not provided numerically.",0.5,N/R,No explicit group payoff numbers for the CAPRI-2 homogeneous profile are reported here.,0.4,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Efficiency validation conducted via matrix calculations and Monte Carlo simulations.,1,"Two-person game using CAPRI-2 for both players. Memory length m=3. Implementation error probability ε=10^-4. Using linear-algebraic or Monte Carlo calculations, the probability that the system is in the full-cooperation state in the stationary distribution is reported as 0.999, confirming the efficiency criterion in the small-error regime.",Captures the structure and numeric outcome for the CAPRI-2 homogeneous-strategy efficiency check.,0.95
