cy, but do not provide a numeric efficiency ratio in this subsection.",0.5,N/R,Group-level payoffs for homogeneous CAPRI-3 are not tabulated here.,0.4,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Efficiency verified through automaton mapping and Monte Carlo simulations.,1,"Three-player public-goods game with CAPRI-3 adopted by all players. Memory length m=5. Implementation error ε=10^-4. Using linear algebra, automaton reduction, or Monte Carlo simulations, probability of full cooperation in the stationary distribution is found to be 0.997 for n=3, providing numerical support that CAPRI-3 satisfies the efficiency criterion in the small-error limit.",Describes the game configuration and main numeric outcome for this homogeneous CAPRI-3 efficiency check.,0.95
