 specified in main text.,0,University students,Participants described as university students in participating cities.,0.9,On site,Lab-style sessions with university students interacting via computers.,0.9,"Same CRSD as German treatments: group of 6 Russians, 10 periods, 60-token endowment per period valued at 2 rubles per token, up to 50 tokens may be contributed; T=2100 total over group and periods for certain safety; otherwise 75% loss to private accounts with probability 1-P, where P = min{C/T,1}.",Methods specify same CRSD structure and local currency conversion for Russia.,1
10.1098_rspb.2021.2174.md,"RUS_NAT_S (Russia, National, Sanctions)","Directly from table 1: RUS_NAT_S, National Russia, sanctions yes, nationality revealed.",1,Sanction availability: Sanctions possible (S); Interaction level: National; Nationality info: Revealed; Country composition: 6 Russians; Game: CRSD with threshold T=2100 plus second-stage sanctioning per period.,Treatment differences from table 1 and methods section.,1,True,Human participants (Russian university students).,1,True,Controlled experimental game with random assignment to sanction treatments.,1,True,Conducted in Russian universities via computer terminals.,0.9,False,No non-human simulations involved.,1,False,"This is empirical, distinct from the theoretical analysis.",1,6,Groups of six participants.,1,10,"Ten periods, identical across treatments.",1,1,Continuous choice of contribution from 0 to 50 tokens.,1,0,All tokens start as private before decisions.,0.95,N/R,No linear MPCR defined; CRSD probability model instead.,0,0,No mention of any communication capability.,0.9,1,"Participants see other members’ contributions histories and, in S, sanctions between members.",1,1,Information on sanctions assigned by each group member to each other member is provided along with persistent numeric identities.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism.,1,1,Fixed 10-period game; likely displayed to subjects as part of instructions/progress.,0.6,1,Sanction stage allows reducing others’ accounts using up to 10 tokens per period.,1,N/R,Cost equals tokens spent; but cost per ‘punishment unit’ not explicitly detailed in excerpt; sanctioning cost schedule in supplement.,0.1,N/R,Only qualitatively ‘more than proportionally’ increasing losses for target; no numeric factor given.,0.1,0,No rewards.,1,N/A,No reward stage.,1,N/A,No reward stage.,1,60,All treatments share 60-token endowment per period.,1,N/R,No explicit normalized contribution mean given for this treatment.,0,N/R,Exact mean contributions not printed.,0,N/R,Efficiency number