10.1017_ehs.2022.32.md,Homogeneous non-Gitano groups,One-shot PGP condition with groups composed only of non-Gitanos.,1,Group ethnic composition: homogeneous non-Gitano (4 non-Gitanos per group),Between-subjects factor is ethnic composition; this condition is all non-Gitano members.,1,True,Human-subjects economic experiment.,1,True,Random assignment to homogeneous vs. mixed sessions; incentivized game.,1,True,Same lab-in-the-field setting as other sessions.,0.9,False,No simulations reported.,1,False,No separate analytical-only condition.,1,4,Four-person groups in all PGP sessions.,1,1,Design is explicitly one-shot.,1,1,Standard PGG with contribution choice from €0–€10; no binary restriction mentioned.,0.95,0,Endowment is given to private account; players decide how much to allocate to group pot.,1,0.5,Same design for all conditions; MPCR given as 0.5.,1,0,No communication option described; anonymity stressed.,0.95,1,Participants observe others’ contributions and earnings before punishing.,1,0,"Only colour-based identities, not personal identities; punishment is anonymous.",0.95,0,No reward mechanism.,1,1,One-shot nature clear from instructions; participants know there is only one round.,0.9,1,Peer punishment stage implemented.,1,1,€1 cost per punishment unit.,1,3,Each €1 spent reduces target’s earnings by €3.,1,0,Game only allows reducing earnings.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,10,Same €10 endowment in all conditions.,1,0.6,Overall contributions “well above 60%”; separate exact rate for non-Gitano homogeneous groups not reported.,0.3,N/R,No numerical mean contributions per condition reported.,0.1,N/R,No realized-vs-maximum payoff ratio by condition.,0.1,N/R,"Only pooled earnings given, not by condition.",0.2,Spain,Participants from southern Spain towns.,1,Mean 42.80 years overall (SD 18.42); non-Gitanos on average 49.97 (SD 18.97) pooling across non-Gitano conditions.,By-ethnicity ages reported; allocation to homogeneous vs mixed not described as age-differentiated.,0.9,59% female overall; no condition-specific gender split provided.,Same as for Gitano condition; random assignment across sessions suggests similar shares.,0.8,Low/varied; literacy requirement minimal (numbers only).,Applies to full sample including non-Gitanos.,0.5,Field experiment,Same lab-in-the-field context in semi-rural towns.,0.95,"Same one-shot PGP: 4 non-Gitano players, €10 each, contributions doubled and evenly shared (MPCR 0.5); peer punishment with cost-to-impact 1:3 after feedback on others’ contributions and earnings. Scarf colours used as anonymous identifiers only; in homogeneous sessions colours not tied to ethnicity differences.",Design identical across homogeneous sessions except for ethnicity composition.,1
10.1017_ehs.2022.32.md,Mixed Gitano/non-Gitano groups,"One-shot PGP condition with ethnically mixed groups (2 Gitanos, 2 non-Gitanos) and ethnicity made salient.",1,"Group ethnic composition: mixed (2 Gitanos, 2 non-Gitanos) with scarf colours mapping to ethnicities","Between-subjects treatment: homogeneous vs. mixed composition; here, mixed groups with colour-ethnicity correlation.",1,True,Human participants; no simulations.,1,True,Controlled lab-in-the-field experiment with exogenous group composition.,1,True,Same organized sessions in field setting.,0.9,False,No agent-based or numerical simulation.,1,False,"Theory in introduction, but this condition is empirical.",1,4,Four-person groups throughout.,1,1,One-shot game in all conditions.,1,1,Contribution decision from €0 to €10; no binary restriction specified.,0.95,0,Endowment initially private; chosen amount allocated to public pot.,1,0.5,Same marginal per capita return applied.,1,0,No communication or chat channel described; anonymity emphasized.,0.95,1,Feedback on each partner’s contribution and earnings is given before punishment.,1,0,"Only colour and corresponding ethnicity known, not individual identity; punishment anonymous.",0.95,0,No rewarding institution.,1,1,Participants know the game is played only once.,0.9,1,Punishment stage described as core of design.,1,1,€1 cost per punishment.,1,3,Each €1 spent reduces target’s earnings by €3.,1,0,No option to increase others’ earnings.,1,N/A,Reward mechanism absent.,1,N/A,Reward mechanism absent.,1,10,Same €10 endowment per participant.,1,0.6,"Authors say average contributions “well above 60%” overall, and no condition effects for ethnicity or condition; thus rate roughly similar here.",0.3,N/R,Only graphical summaries; no numeric means by condition.,0.1,N/R,No explicit efficiency reported and insufficient numeric detail for calculation by condition.,0.1,N/R,"Only overall mean earnings reported, not split by condition.",0.2,Spain,Same recruitment locations in southern Spain.,1,Mean 42.80 years overall (SD 18.42); mixed sessions include both Gitanos (mean 34.56) and non-Gitanos (mean 49.97).,By-ethnicity ages given; mixed condition combines both; no further breakdown.,0.8,59% female overall; no separate gender shares for mixed vs homogeneous.,The same sample-wide statistic applies; assignment across sessions not reported as gender-selective.,0.8,Low/varied; minimal literacy required.,Described for entire sample; applies here as well.,0.5,Field experiment,Same lab-in-the-field framework with community members in town venues.,0.95,"Mixed-ethnicity, one-shot public goods game with peer punishment. Groups of 4 (2 Gitanos, 2 non-Gitanos); €10 endowment; contribution stage (contributions doubled, divided equally: MPCR 0.5) followed by punishment stage (cost-to-impact 1:3). Scarf colours map to ethnicity (two colours for Gitanos, two for non-Gitanos), made salient via group photos so participants can condition punishment on targets’ ethnicity while remaining anonymous at individual level.","Includes features unique to mixed condition: ethnic salience via colours and photos, 2+2 composition.",1
10.1016_j.jebo.2023.10.029.md,"VCM-L (No punishment, LOW instructions)","Condition label constructed from Table 1 treatment name VCM-L, which uses no punishment and short (LOW) instructions.",1,"Punishment availability: No; Instruction format: LOW (short, 503 words, 2 examples)","2×2 design varies punishment (yes/no) and instruction format (LOW vs HIGH); this row is the no-punishment, LOW-instruction cell as described in Section 2 and Table 1.",1,True,Human subjects from University of Essex undergraduate body participated in z-Tree lab sessions.,1,True,Controlled randomized lab experiment with predefined treatments and payoffs.,1,True,"Sessions conducted at EssexLab, a laboratory setting.",1,False,No computer-only or agent-based simulations described.,1,False,No formal analytical model as standalone study; focus is on experimental data.,1,4,“groups of four subjects played a repeated VCM game” in all treatments.,1,20,“subjects interacted in the same group for 20 rounds (partner-matching)” in all treatments.,1,1,Subjects could invest any number of tokens from 0 to 20 in IP or GP; not restricted to all-or-nothing.,1,0,Each round subjects receive an endowment of 20 tokens individually; no pre-allocation to GP implies all starts in private IP account.,0.9,0.5,"Explicitly stated: “A token invested in the GP yielded a return of 0.5 tokens for each of the four group members, i.e., MPCR = 0.5.”",1,0,No mention of communication; standard anonymous VCM protocol with no discussion allowed.,0.9,1,"After contribution stage, subjects saw individual contributions of all players, total contribution, and their earnings from IP and GP.",1,0,"No punishment stage in VCM treatments, so punishment IDs are inapplicable; coded as 0 by design convention.",1,0,No reward mechanism described in any treatment.,1,0,Paper does not state that total or remaining rounds were displayed on screen; cannot infer presence.,0.2,0,Treatment column in Table 1 explicitly indicates ‘Punishment? No’ for VCM-L.,