e c if cooperating, but no explicit endowment per round is given.",0.6,N/R,The paper describes attraction basins for full cooperation (x+z=1) and defection but does not provide numerical contribution rates as dependent variable outputs.,0.5,N/R,Contribution per contributor is c but its numerical value is a parameter (often c = 1 in figures) and not a single experimental outcome.,0.5,N/R,Outcomes like 'full cooperation' imply high efficiency but no numerical efficiency statistics are presented.,0.4,N/R,Group payoffs could be computed but are not tabulated as results.,0.4,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Analytical model with infinite well-mixed population and local interaction structure for payoffs.,1,"Three-strategy public goods game with punishment, as in other conditions, but multiplication factor r_L = r0 + k*(n_C + n_P)/n depends on the fraction of contributors in the local group of size n. Local feedback creates nonlinear public goods returns; conditions 1 < r0 ≤ r_L ≤ r0 + k < n ensure a social dilemma without punishment. Replicator equations incorporate local-feedback contributions to payoffs.",Summarizes Sec. II.A and Appendix C for the local feedback case.,1
