ts contribution rates for subsets and time blocks (e.g., 84% for non-punished in periods 6–10; 27% after punishment phase) but not a single aggregate rate over all 15 periods for this condition.",0.4,N/R,"Only block-specific averages (e.g., 84% and 27% of endowment in certain phases) for this subgroup; no overall E$ amount reported.",0.4,N/R,"Table 1 gives efficiency for all Team group subjects in WP (61.64%), but not separated by punished vs not punished.",0.2,N/R,"No separate group payoff for non-expelled, non-punished subset.",0,USA,Same subject pool description applies.,1,N/R,Not provided.,0,N/R,Not provided.,0,Undergraduate college students (Principles of Economics and general campus recruitment),Same recruitment approach used across treatments.,0.9,On site,"Same lab setting as EO, with z-tree.",1,"Linear public goods game with E$10 endowment per period in Team group, MPCR=0.2 over 16 initial members. Single expulsion vote after period 5 (majority rule; successful expulsion costs each voting member E$0.25 and moves target to Expelled group with E$5 endowment). Additional punishment vote after period 10: Team group members can vote to punish others; if ≥ half of current Team group vote to punish, target loses E$40, and each successful voter pays E$0.25. Punished subjects remain in Team group; only wealth changes.","Summarizes institutional environment faced by non-expelled, non-punished Team group members in WP.",1
