n reported in tables.,0.1,N/R,No explicit welfare ratio or efficiency index reported.,0.1,N/R,"Only differences between stages are reported, not raw baseline payoffs.",0.1,Ecuador,"Sessions at ESPOL in Guayaquil, Ecuador; subjects are local undergraduates.",0.95,Mean 21.6 (range 17–32),"Table 2 reports mean age 21.60, SD 2.28, min 17, max 32.",1,45% women,Table 2: Woman proportion 0.45.,1,"Undergraduate students (35% economics/social science; others in engineering, STEM and related fields)",Described as undergraduate students from various majors; Table 2 details field distribution.,1,On site,Conducted in a physical laboratory at ESPOL.,1,Linear public goods game with 5 players; per-period payoff π_it=20−c_it+0.4*C_t; socially optimal to contribute full endowment; Nash equilibrium c=0.,Directly from general framework description.,1
10.1017_xps.2020.10.md,"Stage 2 – Single selection – Leviathan (exogenous manager, centralized punishment)",Stage 2 treatment cell with single selection and exogenous delegation mechanism as in Table 1 and treatment description.,1,Power delegation: Leviathan (exogenous manager selected by experimenter with 75% probability highest stage-1 contributor). Political accountability: Single (manager selected once and remains in office for all 10 punishment rounds).,Two-by-two design: delegation (Leviathan vs Democracy) × accountability (Single vs Multiple). This row is Leviathan × Single.,1,True,Human participants in lab.,1,True,Random assignment to treatment cells in controlled environment.,1,True,Sessions in ESPOL laboratory.,1,False,No simulations used as treatments.,1,False,No separate analytical-only treatment.,1,5,Groups of n=5 participants continue from stage 1.,1,10,Centralized punishment institution runs for 10 rounds in the single-selection treatments.,1,1,Contribution decision remains linear VCM with 0 ≤ c ≤ w.,1,0,Endowment still starts in private account; taxes are separate.,1,0.4,"Same VCM technology as stage 1: m=2, n=5.",1,0,No communication introduced in stage 2.,0.95,1,Ex-post full information: subjects see others’ contributions and profits anonymously and total punishment points used.,1,0,Subjects observe total punishment points used but not to whom they were targeted.,1,0,No reward mechanism.,1,1,Finite horizon of 10 rounds in stage 2 described; typical experimental interface displays remaining periods.,0.7,1,Centralized punishment institution with manager assigning punishment points.,1,1,Manager assigns p points from 10-point budget; each assigned point transforms via convex function but costs 1 point of the tax-funded management account.,0.8,3,Max ratio from table: 10 assigned -> 30 reduced (3 per assigned). Function is convex with varying ratios (1–3); we record maximum efficacy.,0.5,0,"Design is described as punishment/tax only; unused points are returned equally, not allocated as intentional rewards.",1,N/A,No reward technology.,1,N/A,No reward technology.,1,20,VCM stage within each punishment round keeps w=20 per period.,1,N/R,"Only differences in contribution points between punishment and VCM are reported, not normalized rates.",0.2,2.863,"Panel A, Table 3: Leviathan Single cell reports average Punishment−VCM contribution difference of 2.863 points.",0.7,N/R,No efficiency ratio reported for this treatment.,0.1,0.576,"Panel C, Table 3: Leviathan Single cell shows average Punishment−VCM profits difference of 0.576 points.",0.7,Ecuador,"Laboratory located in Guayaquil, Ecuador.",0.95,Mean 21.6 (range 17–32),Applies to all 435 subjects; no treatment differences reported.,1,45% women,Same subject pool across treatments.,1,"Undergraduate students (35% economics/social science; others in engineering, STEM and related fields)",Same pool across all treatments.,1,On site,Conducted in ESPOL laboratory.,1,"Single manager per group chosen exogenously. Selection rule: 75% probability highest stage-1 contributor, with rest of probability on others; subjects informed about selection probabilities and complete contribution history. Manager controls 10 tax points each round (2 EU from each of 5 group members). Unused points returned equally. Payoff: π_it = (20 − c_it + 0.4*C_t) − [2 − p_i,t* + (1/5)*(10 − p_j,t)] if non-negative; negative-earnings cap based on min of payoff magnitude or punishment points assigned.",Directly from description of centralized tax/punishment institution and Leviathan mechanism.,1
