ments, representative-sharing average). Rate = 5.75/10 = 0.575.",1,5.75,Table 1 reports average contribution 5.75 (SD 2.86) over rounds 6–10 for equal endowments.,1,N/R,No explicit efficiency metric reported for this condition.,0,N/R,Group earnings by condition not provided.,0.2,Nicaragua,Same sample of rural Nicaraguan villagers.,1,N/R,Age not reported.,0,56.25% female; remaining 43.75% male,Gender composition applies to entire sample; no indication it differs by treatment.,0.9,Generally low education; exact distribution N/R,Same participant pool as other condition.,0.6,Field experiment,Same artefactual field experiment in village field lab.,1,"Rounds 6–10: after contributions and public revelation of g_i, the highest contributor becomes representative; if multiple highest contributors, one is randomly selected. Representative first chooses own aid share s_r, then assigns each other player a high, low, or zero share (coded S_i=2,1,0), with high shares twice low shares; resulting s_i = S_i * (1 − s_r) / Σ_{j≠r} S_j.",Based on detailed description and footnote 4 in Section 2.1.,1
