m.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Participants began each round with an endowment of 20 MU.,1,N/R,Paper reports regression effects and qualitative comparisons but no overall mean contribution proportions by condition.,0,N/R,"Only marginal effects (e.g., +0.14 MU per 1 MU of alter) are reported, not mean contributions.",0,N/R,No aggregate payoff relative to maximum is reported.,0,N/R,Group payoff levels are not presented.,0,N/R,"Paper notes a more representative sample and anonymous interactions over the internet, but not the country or countries.",0,N/R,Demographic information not provided.,0,N/R,No gender composition information reported.,0,Mixed/More representative sample (non-student specific),Paper contrasts this sample with prior work using only college students and calls it 'more representative'; exact distribution not given.,0.4,Online,Interactions are described as anonymous over the internet.,1,One-shot style repeated public goods game over 6 rounds with fixed groups of three per round; no repeated partners; contributions chosen between 0 and 20 MU; contributions multiplied by 1.5 and evenly divided; no punishment or reward stage.,Summarized directly from design description and anonymity/rotation procedures.,1
