10.1038_s41598-018-38323-7.md,"Low-cost, high-impact punishment condition","Explicitly named 'low-cost, high-impact' version; focus of paper.",1,"Punishment cost-impact scheme: punishment cost 1 MU and reduced target's income by 3 MU (low-cost, high-impact).",Condition defined by having low cost and high impact of punishment.,1,True,Human participants engaged in this version of the game.,1,True,Controlled manipulation of punishment cost/impact.,1,True,"Part of laboratory experiments, with anonymous online interaction.",0.9,False,No simulation model.,1,False,No closed-form analysis.,1,3,Groups of three players.,1,6,Six rounds per participant.,1,1,Contributions could be any amount from 0 to 20 MU.,1,0,Endowment initially fully private.,0.95,0.5,Same public goods production function as other versions: total ×1.5 divided by 3.,1,0,No communication channels described; anonymity enforced.,0.95,0,No mention of summary statistics or history views.,0.3,0,Strict anonymity implies that individual identities of punishers/targets are not revealed.,0.8,0,No reward option in any version.,1,0,Whether subjects knew total number of rounds is not specified.,0.3,1,One of the four punishment-enabled versions.,1,1,Punishment cost 1 MU and reduced income of target by 3 MU.,1,3,Each MU spent on punishment reduces target payoff by 3 MU.,1,0,"Only punishment, not reward, exists.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,20 MU per round for each participant.,1,N/R,"Known qualitatively that 'rate of cooperation' is significantly higher than other versions, but no numeric rate reported.",0.1,N/R,Marginal regression coefficients are provided but not mean MU contributed.,0,N/R,No efficiency statistic is presented.,0,N/R,Group payoff numbers by condition not included.,0,N/R,Country origin of sample not specified.,0,N/R,Age information missing.,0,N/R,Gender composition not shown.,0,Mixed/More representative sample (non-student specific),"Same more-representative, non-student-specific sample as other conditions.",0.4,Online,Anonymous interactions over the internet.,1,"6-round, 3-player public goods game with no repeated partners; contributions 0–20 MU, multiplied by 1.5 and evenly shared; second-stage punishment where each 1 MU spent reduces a chosen group member’s income by 3 MU (low-cost, high-impact).",Condition-specific punishment rules added to general design.,1
