ith δ=0.3 and random rematching. From round 2 on, within each 4-person group, each member votes on whom to exclude based on each member’s number of contributions in previous rounds. A member is expelled if at least two vote to exclude them. Excluded members receive 100 points per period (400 per round) but do not participate that round and may rejoin new groups in subsequent rounds.",Captures the voting-based peer selection mechanism specific to V.,1
10.1371_journal.pone.0202878.md,Treatment VP (Voting with Punishment),Treatment VP combines both voting system and punishment rule.,1,Institutional rules: voting (majority-based exclusion) enabled; punishment (forfeiture) rule active.,Treatment VP is defined as Treatment P plus voting system.,1,True,Human-subject lab experiment treatment.,1,True,Institutional conditions experimentally manipulated.,1,True,Conducted on-site in lab with z-Tree.,1,False,Not purely simulated; uses student subjects.,1,False,Not a closed-form analytical exercise.,1,4,Again 4-person groups as specified for all treatments.,1,10,Ten-round sessions.,1,0,Same binary GIVE 100 / NOT GIVE 0 choice.,1,0,All 100 points are private by default.,1,N/A,Not a linear public good.,1,0,No mention of communication beyond institutionally required voting and feedback.,0.9,1,Voting is based on information about how many times each member contributed in previous rounds; contributions and payouts are displayed.,1,1,"As in Treatment P, forfeiture is determined from publicly known past contributions; group members observe which scheduled recipient cannot receive payout.",0.8,0,No explicit reward mechanism exists.,1,1,Subjects know the game lasts ten rounds of four periods.,1,1,Punishment (forfeiture) rule is applied in VP plus voting.,1,0,Punishment is enforced automatically without cost to others.,1,100,Punished scheduled recipient loses their 100-point payout that round if they failed to contribute earlier.,0.5,0,No separate reward institution.,1,N/A,No costly reward option.,1,N/A,No costly reward option.,1,100,Same per-period endowment as other treatments.,1,0.56,Table 3: β0 (before payout) in Treatment VP equals 0.56.,1,56,0.56 * 100-point endowment.,0.8,N/R,No efficiency ratio reported.,0,N/R,Only mean individual payoff (4494) shown.,0.3,Japan,Same experimental location and subject pool.,1,N/R,Not specified beyond student status.,0.3,N/R,No gender statistics given.,0,Mainly undergraduate students; some graduate students,Applies to all sessions across treatments.,0.9,On site,Conducted in-person in laboratory with computers.,1,"Same 4×4 ROSCA with δ=0.3, random rematching. From round 2, groups use majority voting to exclude members based on contribution histories; excluded subjects earn 100 points per period (400 per round) while out of the group and can rejoin later rounds. Additionally, punishment rule prevents any scheduled recipient from receiving a payout if they have not contributed in preceding periods.",Combines voting and forfeiture details specific to VP treatment.,1
