10.1371_journal.pone.0263028.md,"High-noise punishment (β ~ U[0,6])","Treatment where punishment enhancement factor β is drawn uniformly from [0,6].",1,"Punishment noise amplitude σ = 3; punishment enhancement factor β ~ Uniform[0,6] with mean 3","High-noise treatment defined by β drawn from uniform distribution on [0,6]; in regression noise amplitude coded σ = 3.",1,True,Human-subject experiment condition.,1,True,Random assignment to punishment-noise treatments.,1,False,"Conducted online, not in physical lab.",1,False,"Human decisions, not agent-based simulation.",1,False,Not a purely analytical treatment.,1,4,Groups of four participants.,1,20,Same main game length of 20 incentivized rounds.,0.9,1,Contribution choice from 0 to 10 MU.,1,0,All endowment initially private.,1,0.5,Same r = 2 and group size 4.,1,0,No chat function described.,0.9,1,Participants see others’ contributions and the effects of punishment each round.,0.8,0,Participants’ identities concealed; only anonymous positions shown.,0.9,0,No rewards.,1,0,Actual number of rounds not communicated.,1,1,Punishment present with noisy multiplier.,1,1,1 MU per punishment coin spent.,1,3,"Average β is 3 (mean of U[0,6]); although actual draw varies, the mean technology is 3.",1,0,No reward option.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,10,10 MU round endowment.,1,N/R,"Contribution distributions are shown, but no single normalized rate is reported numerically for this treatment.",0,N/R,"Text reports declines and proportions (e.g., percent contributing ≥8 MU) but no exact mean contribution level.",0,N/R,Efficiency (relative to maximum) not reported numerically.,0,5.6,Mean payoff per round dropped to 5.6 ± 1.2 MU in high-noise group.,1,"Multiple (41 countries, mainly Prolific online sample)",Same global online sample as other treatments.,0.9,N/R,Age not provided.,0,Sex ratio ≈ 2:1 (overall sample; allocation by condition not specified),Only overall sex ratio in final analyzed sample given.,0.5,N/R,