10.1057_s41599-019-0249-2.md,System V: Public goods game with democratic punishment (shared costs),System V in Table 1 is 'Public goods game with democratic punishment (shared costs)'.,1,Punishment system = Democratic peer punishment; Voting = Yes; Cost sharing = Shared among punishers,Described as democratic punishment with shared punishment costs and voting.,1,True,This condition was played by all human participants.,1,True,It is one of the experimentally varied institutional designs.,1,True,Conducted on-site in lab cubicles via z-Tree.,1,False,No simulations reported.,1,False,No purely analytical study.,1,4,Groups of four players.,1,10,Ten periods in each of the five systems.,1,1,Same contribution freedom (0–20 MU) as other versions.,1,0,Endowment is entirely private at period start.,1,0.4,Multiplier 1.6 and 4 players.,1,0,No chat reported.,0.9,1,"Players were informed about contributions, public good payoff, intended punishments, votes, and executed punishment as in democratic system description.",1,0,No mention of revealing real identities; players refer to anonymous group members.,0.7,0,No reward mechanism implemented.,1,1,Total periods and versions were announced beforehand.,0.9,1,Democratic punishment with shared costs is a punishment system.,1,1,"Players invest their own MUs; in shared-cost democratic system they 'had to cover the cost when a majority voted for the execution of the punishment', with each covering one-third of the total costs; the relevant unit cost is still 1 MU per invested MU.",0.8,3,Underlying punishment factor from peer system (3 MU reduction per MU invested) is retained; only cost sharing is altered.,0.7,0,No rewards described.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,20,Same 20 MU endowment in each period.,1,N/R,Reported data are total contributions over 10 periods.,0.3,140.22,Table 2: 'Contribution (in MUs)' = 140.22 (55.73) for 'Democratic peer punishment with shared costs'.,1,N/R,Efficiency measure not given.,0.1,N/R,Only individual 'Total Income' reported (238.13).,0.4,Germany,Same German sample across all versions.,1,"M = 22.92, further distribution N/R",Single age summary given.,0.9,49 women; remaining 27 not specified by category label,Overall gender breakdown applies to all conditions.,0.9,N/R,No education-level information.,0.1,On site,Same in-lab experimental environment.,1,"Game structure mirrors the democratic punishment with individual costs, but with shared costs in the punishment stage: players propose punishments, vote on execution, and, if a majority votes 'yes', each punisher and potentially other designated cost-bearers cover one-third of the total punishment costs for a target in that period.",Summarized from 'systems with shared costs' and democratic punishment descriptions.,1
