10.1371_journal.pone.0248599.md,"CS; No peer – Collective sanctions, no peer punishment",Table 1 lists 'CS; No peer' as collective sanctions without peer punishment.,1,Sanction regime: Collective sanctions (CS); Peer punishment: absent; Collective sanctions: present,2×2 design; this treatment has collective sanctions and no peer punishment.,1,True,Same lab experiment with human participants; this is one treatment condition.,1,True,Controlled manipulation of sanction regime (CS vs IS) and peer punishment.,1,True,Conducted in CELSS lab.,1,False,No simulation reported.,1,False,Primarily empirical; analytical formula used only to define payoffs.,1,3,Groups of three in all treatments.,1,15,15 periods across all treatments.,1,1,Continuous contributions 0–20 tokens allowed.,1,0,Endowment is private before contribution choice.,0.9,0.5,Rate of return a on sum of contributions equals 0.5.,1,0,No communication described; anonymity and non-revealed identities emphasize lack of interaction.,0.9,0,No mention of aggregate feedback about others’ earnings or sanctions.,0.6,0,No peer punishment stage; external fines are algorithmic and not tied to identifiable individuals for participants.,0.9,0,No rewards in any treatment.,1,1,Number of periods communicated at start.,1,0,"No peer punishment stage in 'No peer' treatments; only external collective sanction operates, not peer-based punishment.",1,N/A,No peer punishment mechanism.,1,N/A,No peer punishment mechanism.,1,0,"Design uses only fines, no positive incentives.",1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,20,Endowment of 20 tokens per participant each period.,1,N/R,Only token contributions reported.,0.2,8.06,Table 3 lists mean contribution for 'CS; No peer' as 8.06 tokens.,1,N/R,Efficiency not quantified per treatment.,0.1,N/R,Average earnings not broken down for this specific treatment.,0.2,United States,Same Columbia University lab subject pool.,0.9,N/R,Only class year specified; no age stats.,0.6,Mixed,"Gender breakdown table includes this treatment, so both men and women participated.",1,2nd- and 3rd-year university students at Columbia University,Same pool across all conditions.,1,On site,Lab sessions in CELSS.,0.9,"Linear public good game, group size 3, endowment 20, MPCR 0.5. External collective sanctions: each period, group is checked with probability 1/3. If checked and at least one group member’s contribution is ≤10 tokens (threshold T=11), all three group members lose 7 tokens from their earnings for that period. No peer punishment stage.",Summarized from description of collective sanctions without peer punishment.,1
10.1371_journal.pone.0248599.md,CS; Peer – Collective sanctions with peer punishment,Table 1 lists 'CS; Peer' as collective sanctions with peer punishment.,1,Sanction regime: Collective sanctions (CS); Peer punishment: present; Collective sanctions: present,2×2 design; this treatment combines collective sanctions and peer punishment.,1,True,Human-subject lab experiment; this is one of four treatments.,1,True,Random assignment to treatment with controlled rules.,1,True,Conducted in Columbia’s CELSS lab.,1,False,No mention of simulations beyond random number draws for checks.,1,False,Not a purely analytical study.,1,3,Groups of three across all treatments.,1,15,Design specifies 15 periods.,1,1,Continuous choice 0–20 tokens is allowed.,1,0,Endowment privately held; contribution chosen each round.,0.9,0.5,Payoff function uses a=0.5.,1,0,No communication channel mentioned; anonymity emphasized.,0.9,0,No description of showing others’ payoffs or punishment statistics.,0.6,0,Identities of group members are not revealed; punishment assignments thus anonymous.,0.9,0,No rewards implemented.,1,1,Participants informed of total periods.,1,1,Peer punishment Stage 3 available in this treatment.,1,1,Each deduction point costs the punisher 1 token.,1,2,Each deduction point reduces target’s earnings by 2 tokens.,1,0,Only deduction (punishment) allowed.,1,N/A,No rewards exist in design.,1,N/A,No rewards exist in design.,1,20,Endowment is 20 tokens per period per player.,1,N/R,Only token-level averages reported.,0.2,10.03,Table 3 lists mean contribution for 'CS; Peer' as 10.03 tokens.,1,N/R,No direct measure or derivable per-treatment efficiency reported.,0.1,N/R,Group payoffs by treatment not given.,0.2,United States,Same Columbia University lab subject pool.,0.9,N/R,Participants described by class year only.,0.6,Mixed,Gender-specific results highlight differences in CS; Peer treatment.,1,2nd- and 3rd-year university students at Columbia University,Same subject pool as other treatments.,1,On site,Laboratory experiment in CELSS.,0.9,"Linear public good game, group size 3, endowment 20, MPCR 0.5. External collective sanctions: with probability 1/3 each period, the group is checked; if any member contributes ≤10 tokens, all members incur a 7-token fine that period. Peer punishment Stage 3: each participant can assign up to 10 deduction points to each of the other two group members; each point costs 1 token to the punisher and reduces the target’s payoff by 2 tokens.",Combined description of CS regime and peer punishment stage.,1
