10.1561_102.00000099.md,Equal – No Punishment,One cell of the 2×2 design: Equal endowments and no punishment.,1,Endowment distribution: Equal (all 50 ED); Punishment institution: No Punishment,Treatment varies endowment equality and presence of punishment. This cell has equal endowments and no punishment stage.,1,True,Laboratory experiment with 120 student subjects.,1,True,Controlled randomized lab experiment with imposed treatments.,1,True,Conducted at the Cleve E. Willis Experimental Economics Laboratory.,1,False,No agent-based or numerical-only simulations reported.,1,False,"Paper includes theory but the reported results are from lab data, not pure analytical model.",1,4,Groups of four subjects in all treatments.,1,15,Subjects played fifteen periods of the CPR game.,1,1,"Subjects chose ""how much"" of their endowment to allocate; implies continuous/any amount, not binary all-or-nothing.",0.9,0,Endowment starts in private control; they decide how much to put into group vs. private account. Default is fully in private account.,0.9,N/R,Nonlinear CPR with V(G)=aG−bG²; marginal per capita return is not a single constant MPCR.,1,0,No mention of communication; only extraction (and punishment in other treatments).,0.9,1,"After choices, subjects saw group aggregate extraction and their earnings; this is summary information about others’ actions and payoffs.",0.95,0,No punishment stage in this treatment; identities in punishment not applicable. Set to 0 for absence.,1,0,No reward mechanism in any treatment.,1,1,Standard in these experiments and they refer to early (1–7) and late (8–15) periods; instructions typically state total periods. Not explicitly stated.,0.6,0,"""No Punishment"" treatment explicitly has no punishment stage.",1,N/A,No punishment mechanism in this treatment.,1,N/A,No punishment mechanism in this treatment.,1,0,Only deduction (punishment) points are mentioned; no positive rewards.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism implemented.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism implemented.,1,50,"In Equal, each subject was given an endowment of 50 ED each period.",1,N/R,"They report extractions (use of common pool), not normalized contribution/ extraction rates relative to endowment.",1,33.12,Table 3 reports average extractions in Equal No Punishment (all periods) = 33.12 ED per subject.,1,N/R,They present earnings and theoretical benchmarks but do not report realized efficiency as ratio to maximum.,0.6,103.75,"Table 2 shows average period earnings in Equal No Punishment (all periods) = 103.75 ED (group average per person); group total would be 4×, but they consistently report per-subject averages, so we record that.",0.9,USA,Subjects recruited from University of Massachusetts Amherst in the USA.,1,N/R,Only described as undergraduates; no age statistics provided.,0.7,N/R,No information on gender composition.,1,Undergraduate students,Subjects recruited from the undergraduate population.,1,On site,Conducted in a physical experimental economics laboratory.,1,"Common-pool resource game with V(G)=6G−0.025G², private account return w=1, group size 4, 15 periods, equal endowment 50 ED per period, decisions on how much to allocate to group vs private account; no punishment stage.",Summarizes structural parameters and flow for this treatment.,1
