10.3389_fphy.2018.00156.md,"Authoritative third-party punishment – dimorphic population, ALL variant (various β, T = 2, F = 1)","Section 2.2 and Figure 3A,C analyze dimorphic equilibrium under authoritative punishment with ALL variant for β in {−1, 0, 1}, T = 2, F = 1.",0.9,"Punishment variant = ALL (all defectors punished); risk attitude β ∈ {−1, 0, 1}; observation probability z; weak prisoner’s dilemma parameters T = 2, F = 1.","Figure 3 captions specify ALL variant, T = 2, F = 1 and compare β values.",0.9,False,"Theoretical and numerical analysis, no human data.",1,False,Not an empirical experiment.,1,False,No lab setting.,1,True,Stable frequencies x* and expected punishments per observation are obtained by numerically solving replicator dynamics.,0.9,True,Replicator equation and utilities are derived analytically; fixed points then studied numerically.,0.9,2,Two players per game in ALL variant description.,1,1,Single game per encounter in infinite-population dynamics.,0.9,1,C/D binary choice.,0.7,N/A,Not a contribution game.,1,N/R,Prisoner’s dilemma payoff matrix only.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,Not modeled.,0.8,0,Punisher is an abstract authority; no identity revelation modeled.,0.8,0,No rewards.,1,0,No notion of round count display.,1,1,Authority punishes all defectors when observing (Figure 2A).,1,N/R,"Punisher’s cost is described qualitatively (e.g., pays cost 2C in mutual defection) but numeric C not specified for this section.",0.5,N/R,Only fines F to defectors and qualitative cost C to punisher are described; no per-token tech parameter.,0.5,0,No rewarding institution in ALL variant model.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,"Matrix payoffs only, no explicit endowment parameter.",0.8,N/R,Primary outcomes: stable frequency of cooperators x* and expected number of punishments per observation; no normalized contribution measure.,1,N/R,No explicit contribution quantity variable.,1,N/R,"Paper discusses cost-effectiveness via number of punishments, not formal efficiency ratio.",0.7,N/R,Group payoff levels are implicit; not reported as a summarized DV.,0.6,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Replicator dynamics with no empirical data.,1,"Two-strategy evolutionary dynamics (cooperators vs defectors). ALL variant: any observed defector is punished; in mutual defection both defectors are punished and authority pays cost 2C, each defector fined F; in one-sided defection, defector fined F and punisher pays C. Stable frequency x* and expected number of punishments per observation = 2(1−x*). Parameters used in Figure 3: T = 2, F = 1, β ∈ {−1,0,1}.",Summarizes textual description and Figure 2A & Figure 3.,1
10.3389_fphy.2018.00156.md,"Authoritative third-party punishment – dimorphic population, ONE variant (various β, T = 2, F = 1)","Section 2.2 and Figure 3B,D,E analyze ONE variant with same parameters as ALL variant.",0.9,"Punishment variant = ONE (one defector punished in mutual defection); risk attitude β ∈ {−1, 0, 1}; observation probability z; T = 2, F = 1.","Figure 3B,D,E labelled ONE variant, parameters specified.",0.9,False,Model-based analysis.,1,False,Not an empirical experiment.,1,False,No lab study.,1,True,Stable x* and expected punishments per observation calculated numerically from replicator dynamics.,0.9,True,Replicator equation and utilities are explicitly specified.,0.9,2,Two-player games as in variants description.,1,1,Single encounter per game.,0.9,1,Binary C/D choice.,0.7,N/A,No contribution endowment.,1,N/R,Not a public goods game.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,Not modeled.,0.8,0,No identity structure.,0.8,0,No reward.,1,0,No displayed round count.,1,1,Authority punishes in mutual defection by punishing only one randomly chosen defector (Figure 2B).,1,N/R,Punisher’s cost C is qualitative; no numeric value specified here.,0.5,N/R,Only fines F and costs C specified symbolically.,0.5,0,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,Not specified.,0.8,N/R,Outcome measured as cooperator frequency x*; no normalized contribution values reported.,1,N/R,Binary C vs D.,1,N/R,"Cost-effectiveness discussed via expected number of punishments, not as efficiency ratio.",0.7,N/R,No explicit group payoff statistic reported.,0.6,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Model-based analysis.,1,"ONE variant: in one-sided defection, the sole defector is punished (defector pays fine F, punisher cost C). In mutual defection, only one of the two defectors is randomly selected and punished (punisher cost C, punished defector fine F). Stable cooperator frequency x* < that of ALL variant; expected punishments per observation = 1 − x*^2. Parameters: T = 2, F = 1, β ∈ {−1,0,1}.",Based on description of Figure 2B and Section 2.2 text.,1
10.3389_fphy.2018.00156.md,"Authoritative third-party punishment – dimorphic population, ONE-SIDED variant",Section 2.2 defines ONE-SIDED variant and states it does not achieve cooperative dimorphism when ESS condition is violated.,0.9,Punishment variant = ONE-SIDED (only one-sided defectors punished); risk attitude β varied; observation probability z; parameters T and F as in main model.,"Section 2.2 and Figure 2C define variant and analyze its dynamics; no fixed numeric T,F beyond earlier defaults.",0.7,False,Theoretical replicator dynamics.,1,False,No experiment.,1,False,No lab setup.,1,True,Stable points found numerically for each variant.,0.9,True,"Utilities and replicator equation given analytically (Equations A1, A2c).",0.9,2,Two-player games in variants description.,1,1,Single-shot encounters.,0.9,1,Binary cooperation vs defection.,0.7,N/A,No endowment contributions.,1,N/R,Not a public goods game.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,Not included in model.,0.8,0,No identity modeled.,0.8,0,No rewards.,1,0,Rounds not displayed.,1,1,Defectors that exploit cooperators are punished; mutual defectors are not punished.,1,N/R,Punisher’s cost C is symbolic without assigned numeric value in this section.,0.5,N/R,Only symbolic costs and fines provided.,0.5,0,No rewarding.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,Not reported.,0.8,N/R,Outcome: whether cooperative dimorphism is achievable; no quantitative contribution DV.,1,N/R,No continuous contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency not quantified; variant judged qualitatively less effective.,0.7,N/R,No explicit group payoff DV reported.,0.6,N/A,No human study.,1,N/A,No human study.,1,N/A,No human study.,1,N/A,No human study.,1,No human,Evolutionary dynamics model only.,1,"ONE-SIDED variant: in one-sided defection (D vs C), the defector is punished (punisher cost C, defector fine F). In mutual defection (D vs D), no one is punished. Authors find this variant does not support stable cooperative dimorphism when monomorphic ESS condition is violated, because u_C > u_D reduces to same ESS threshold as monomorphic case.",From Section 2.2 and Figure 2C description.,1
10.3389_fphy.2018.00156.md,"Endogenous third-party punishment – three-strategy model, ALL variant (β = −10, T = 2, C = 1, F = 3, w = 0.1, μ = 0.01)","Section 3 describes three-strategy model; Figures 4A–C show β = −10 case with parameters T = 2, C = 1, F = 3, w = 0.1, μ = 0.01 for ALL, ONE, ONE-SIDED variants.",0.9,Punishment variant = ALL; risk attitude β = −10 (strongly risk-averse); weak prisoner’s dilemma with T = 2; punishment cost C = 1; fine F = 3; intensity of selection w = 0.1; mutation rate μ = 0.01.,Parameter set explicitly given in Section 3 for reference figures.,1,False,"Mathematical and numerical analysis, no empirical data.",1,False,Not an experiment with subjects.,1,False,No lab environment.,1,True,Replicator-mutator dynamics (three ODEs) are numerically simulated to illustrate trajectories and stable states in Figure 4A.,1,True,"Model equations and utilities defined analytically (Equations 8–10, A3, A4).",1,3,"Three individuals sampled; two play game, one is observer/punisher (Section 3).",1,1,Single game per sampling event in continuous evolutionary process.,0.9,1,Each game participant chooses C or D; punisher’s action is whether to punish; no continuous contribution choice.,0.7,N/A,No endowment-based public goods contribution.,1,N/R,Not a linear PGG.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,0,Model only specifies payoffs from current interaction; no summaries displayed.,0.8,0,Observer is randomly selected third party; no identity display modeled.,0.8,0,No reward mechanism.,1,0,"Continuous-time dynamics, no displayed round count.",1,1,Third-party punishers (strategy P) punish each defector at cost C; defectors pay fine F.,1,1,Parameter C = 1 is the per-defector cost to punisher in this model (Section 3: 'can punish each defector at cost C (>0)'; reference parameters: C = 1).,1,3,Fine F = 3 is per punished defector; interpreted as punishment technology multiplier from punisher’s one unit cost to fine level.,0.7,0,No rewarding strategy or institution.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/R,"Payoffs defined by matrix, not from explicit endowment allocation.",0.8,N/R,"DV is long-run frequencies of C, D, P strategies; contributions are binary and not normalized.",1,N/R,No explicit contribution quantity.,1,N/R,Paper reports qualitative result 'almost full cooperation' rather than efficiency metric.,0.8,N/R,Group payoff not summarized numerically.,0.6,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Model-based replicator-mutator dynamics.,1,"Three strategies: C (cooperator, plays C, does not punish when observer), D (defector, plays D, does not punish), P (punisher, plays C and punishes each defector as observer, paying cost C per defector, each defector fined F). Two of three sampled players play weak prisoner’s dilemma (T = 2, base payoffs as in Equation 1), third is observer. Fitness f_s = 1 − w + w u_s, with risk-sensitive utility u_s defined via exponential utility with β = −10. Dynamics follow replicator-mutator with mutation rate μ = 0.01. For β = −10, population converges to almost full cooperation with a small fraction of punishers.","From Section 3, Equations (8)–(10), and narrative around Figures 4A–C.",1
