10.1140_epjb_e2018-90042-8.md,"Model 1 – Regular lattice PGG with heterogeneous defectors, r=1.1",Original model on 100x100 regular lattice varying MPCR r; this row for r=1.1 as shown in Fig. 1.,0.9,"Network: 100x100 regular lattice (Von Neumann, degree 4), MPCR r=1.1, no punishment, initial cooperators 50%, defectors 50%, ξ ~ Normal[0,1]","Summarizes condition-specific parameters: topology, r, and absence of punishment; initial fractions from Sec. 3.1.",0.9,False,"Paper describes numerical simulations with agents on networks, no human participants.",1,False,Not a controlled human or field experiment; it is a computational model.,1,False,No lab or field setting; purely simulated agents.,1,True,Authors repeatedly state they perform simulations and Monte Carlo steps on networks.,1,False,"They provide model equations but results are from simulations, not closed-form analysis.",0.9,10000,"100×100 grid used to represent topology, so 100*100=10000 agents.",1,10000,They carry out evolutionary processes by 10000 steps.,1,1,"Model allows continuous contributions via λ(ξ) between 0 and 1, not just all-or-nothing.",1,0,Standard PGG: each has endowment c=1 in private account and chooses how much to donate.,0.8,N/R,"They define r as enhancement factor and say r is defined as MPCR, but do not report r/N numerically for each r; schema asks for MPCR, and only r is given.",0.4,N/A,No human participants; communication concept not applicable.,1,0,Agents only use local payoffs; no mention of displaying summaries or global info.,0.9,N/A,No punishment mechanism in Model 1.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism in any model.,1,0,Simulated agents do not observe round counts; not mentioned.,0.8,0,Model 1 explicitly described as original model without punishment; punishment added only in Model 2.,1,N/A,No punishment in this model.,1,N/A,No punishment in this model.,1,0,Only punishment is modeled; no rewards described.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,1,They set c=1 as the contribution cost; standard interpretation is each agent’s endowment per game is 1.,0.8,0,"Fig. 1: when r=1.1, the sum of final donations is zero, so normalized contribution is 0.",0.9,0,Total donations go to zero at equilibrium for r=1.1.,0.9,0,"With zero contributions, total payoff from PGG is zero; efficiency relative to full cooperation is 0.",0.9,N/R,They do not report aggregate payoff in numerical form.,0.1,N/A,No human participants; simulated agents only.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,"Numerical simulations on networks, no empirical environment.",1,"Public goods game on 100x100 lattice; group size N=5 (self + 4 neighbors); strategies: cooperator C (ξ=0, contribute 1), heterogeneous defector HD (0<ξ<1, contribute λ(ξ)=(1−ξ)^2), complete defector D0 (ξ=1, contribute 0). Strategy update by pairwise comparison using Fermi rule with k=1. Initial 50% cooperators and 50% defectors; ξ drawn from normal distribution on [0,1].",Summarizes model 1 description in Sec. 2.1 and 3.1.,1
