eward mechanism is absent.,1,N/A,Reward mechanism is absent.,1,N/R,"No explicit per-period endowment is stated, only that cooperators/punishers pay cost c = 1.",0.4,N/R,"Reported outcomes are frequencies of strategy types, not normalized contribution rates.",0.3,N/R,Average contributions per agent are not reported.,0.3,N/R,No efficiency metrics (payoff relative to maximum) presented.,0.2,N/R,"Simulation results emphasize frequencies, not aggregate payoffs.",0.2,N/A,There are no human participants.,1,N/A,There are no human participants.,1,N/A,There are no human participants.,1,N/A,There are no human participants.,1,No human,All dynamics are simulated for artificial agents.,1,"Finite population M = 100; sample N = 5 each period from well-mixed population; three strategies (cooperators, defectors, punishers) with initial counts X = 30, Y = 40, Z = 30; contribution cost c = 1; multiplier r = 3; punishment cost γ = 0.3 and strength δ = 1; costly signaling efficacy α = 0.3; λ = 1 meaning altruistic punishment and nonpunishing contributions are treated as the same costly signal; selection strength ω = 0.5; mutation rate μ = 0.001; Moran process with mutation.",Direct from parameter statements for Fig. 1(b) and model description.,0.98
