Max-Planck-Institute of Economics.,1,"Three-player simultaneous prisoners’ dilemma with punishment using the strategy method. Stage 1: all choose cooperate or defect; payoffs follow a 3-player PD matrix adapted from Falk, Fehr, Fischbacher (2005). After choices, one randomly chosen player’s PD decision is replaced by a random move (cooperate or defect with equal probability). Stage 2: one randomly chosen player (never the random-decision player) can assign up to 15 deduction points to each of the other two players; each point costs the punisher 1 and reduces the punished player’s payoff by 2.5. Strategy method: all subjects specify punishment points for all combinations of partners’ actions and intentionality before roles and random replacement are realized. One-shot game; roles and payoffs determined after all decisions.",Summarizes detailed procedural information given in the experimental setting section.,1
