 of a repeated principal–agent model.,1,"Infinite-horizon principal–two-agent model with stochastic collaboration opportunities (probability θ). Under Type 3, only team contract is high-powered: individual work yields zero wages, while collaboration with effort is incentivized. Peer-sanction via loss of future collaboration supports effort, but the contract can be socially inefficient because agents exert no effort when collaboration opportunities do not arrive.",Summarized from Section 4.1–4.3 and Lemma 3 plus welfare discussion in 4.3.,1
