 costs 20 points to third party per 50-point deduction from a player.,1,50,Each punishment deducts 50 points from punished player.,1,0,No rewarding option described; only costly punishment.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/R,"Game described via outcome payoffs (e.g., 200 tokens for mutual cooperation, 125 for mutual defection); no explicit per-period endowment before actions.",0.4,0.3016,"Overall cooperation rate of juniors is 30.16%; in J/J all participants (players) are juniors, and cooperation does not differ by third-party generation for juniors, so using 30.16% as treatment-level normalized cooperation.",0.7,N/R,"Only cooperation rates (percent) reported, not raw tokens contributed per period.",0,N/R,"Welfare discussed in terms of earnings, but no normalization to theoretical maximum efficiency is provided.",0,3227,Average number of tokens earned per person in J/J reported as 3227.,1,Austria,"Experiment at University of Innsbruck, with comparisons to Austrian population and education statistics.",1,"Juniors: mostly in their 20s, mean age 22; sample restricted to students in their 20s.",Described as students in their 20ies with average age 22 years.,1,Approximately 50% female in both generations,Gender composition is close to 50% in both generations (Appendix tables).,0.8,All juniors enrolled at university; above-average education compared to Austrian population.,All junior participants are students enrolled at a university.,1,On site,"Conducted in Innsbruck Laboratory / lab-in-the-field, with participants present in sessions.",1,"Two-person repeated Prisoner’s Dilemma with binary cooperate/defect actions; payoffs: mutual cooperation yields 200 tokens each (400 total), mutual defection yields 125 tokens each (250 total); third party receives 200 points per period, can punish each player separately (binary) at cost 20 to deduct 50 from the player; matching groups of 6 (4 players, 2 third parties), random rematching within group each perio