2 row (1).",1,16.013,"Average taxes reported (points) in rounds 1–20, Table 2 row (5).",1,N/R,Efficiency relative to maximum not explicitly reported.,0,N/R,Only individual average earnings (91.900 points) given; group-level payoff not stated.,0.3,Taiwan,Same subject pool and location.,1,N/R,Only undergraduate status mentioned.,0.4,N/R,Gender breakdown not included.,0,Undergraduate students,All subjects are undergraduate students.,1,On site,Conducted in computer laboratory.,1,"Structure matches endogenous-audit tax compliance game except audit probability is fixed at p̄=0.5 (2 of 4 group members audited each round) and 8 monitoring points are subtracted from X account exogenously each round. Income w_i ∈ {40,60,80,100}, report R_i, tax t=0.3, public good X with MPCR m=0.5, fine rate θ=3 on detected evasion.",Summarized from random-audit treatment description and payoff equation π_i^RN.,1
10.1016_j.jet.2017.02.011.md,Theoretical repeated game model with public deterministic monitoring,Paper presents only a general game-theoretic model and proofs; no distinct empirical conditions or parameterized simulation runs are defined.,0.9,N/A,No experimental manipulation or simulation parameter sweep; the work is purely theoretical across arbitrary games.,1,False,"No human participants, data collection, or empirical measurements are reported; all results are analytical.",1,False,"There is no controlled experiment described, only definitions, lemmas, theorems, and proofs.",1,False,No lab or in-person/online experimental setting; purely theoretical.,1,False,"Although Blackwell’s algorithm and approachability are discussed, no numerical or agent-based simulations are run.",1,True,All results are derived via formal mathematical analysis of repeated games and monitoring structures.,1,0,"The model allows a general finite set of players N={1,…,n}; no fixed numeric player count is chosen for an implemented game instance.",0.7,0,"The analysis considers an infinitely repeated discounted game (t=1,2,…), not a finite number of rounds.",1,1,"Action sets X_i are general compact sets, allowing arbitrary pure actions; not restricted to all-or-nothing contributions.",0.7,N/A,No contribution game or endowment structure with default allocations is specified; general repeated game framework only.,1,N/R,"No public goods or linear contribution structure is modeled, so no MPCR is defined.",1,N/A,No human subjects or communication stage; strategies are abstract mappings from public histories to actions.,1,0,The only publicly observed object is the public signal f(x_t); no mention of explicit payoff/summary displays.,0.7,N/A,"Punishments and rewards are implemented via strategy profiles, not via an explicit punishment action with displayed identities to participants.",1,N/A,"Rewards are part of equilibrium continuation payoffs, not a mechanism with displayed rewarder identities.",1,0,"