med about how many DP specific third parties (anonymously yet identifiable by arbitrary number and academic background) assign to them; thus identities (numbers and background) of punishers are effectively revealed.,0.9,0,No reward option.,1,0,One-shot game with strategy-method elicitation; text does not mention on-screen round counters.,0.4,1,Third parties can assign decrement points to targets.,1,1,Each decrement point cost the punisher 1 MU from the additional MU for punishment.,1,3,Each decrement point reduced target's earnings by 3 MU.,1,0,"Only decrement points, no positive rewards.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism exists.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism exists.,1,100,Each PGG group member receives an endowment of 100 MU.,1,N/R,"Paper reports general patterns (free-riding punished more, etc.) but no average contribution rates or amounts in Experiment 2.",0.2,N/R,No numeric mean contributions reported for Experiment 2.,0.2,N/R,No efficiency statistics reported.,0.1,N/R,No group payoff numbers reported for Experiment 2.,0.1,Netherlands,Students at Leiden University.,0.95,N/R,Age not given.,0.1,N/R,Gender not discussed.,0.1,First-year university students in Psychology or Pedagogical Science,Same recruitment pool is described for all experiments.,1,On site,Participants attended a one-hour lab session in cubicles at Leiden University.,1,"Procedure: (1) Participants in pluriform groups of six play a linear one-shot PGG with 100 MU endowment, contributions in steps of 10, MPCR 0.25. (2) Each six-person group then serves as third-party punishers overseeing another pluriform group of six (3 similar, 3 dissimilar to the participant). Using the strategy method, participants state for each possible contribution level how many decrement points they would assign to similar vs dissimilar targets; their punishment strategies are common knowledge to targets, and punishment costs 1 MU per DP and reduces target payoff by 3 MU.",Summarizes combined PGG and third-party punishment structure where this condition manipulates target similarity.,1
