erlands,Leiden University.,0.95,N/R,Not provided.,0.1,N/R,Not provided.,0.1,First-year university students in Psychology or Pedagogical Science,Same participant pool described.,1,On site,Lab experiment in cubicles.,1,"In this uniform-similar context, the overseen group consists solely of members who share the participant's academic background (e.g., psychology). Participants first make a PGG contribution in similar uniform groups of three and then, via the strategy method, specify for each possible contribution level how many decrement points they would assign to each similar member.",Summarizes how this context differs structurally from pluriform contexts.,1
