cles at Leiden University.,1,"In this context, the overseen uniform group contains only members whose academic background differs from the participant’s (e.g., pedagogy when the participant is psychology). Participants use the strategy method to indicate DP assignments for all possible contribution levels by these dissimilar others. Reported results: dissimilar others in uniform groups are punished as frequently as similar others (39.46% vs 39.26%) but at slightly higher cost (1.842 vs 1.738 MU).",Summarizes distinctive features and key discriminatory-punishment result for this condition.,1
