10.1038_s41598-021-86668-3.md,"Simulation condition (g,p,a) = (0.5,0,0.5)","Condition described in Figure 2 panel (g) as (g,p,a) = (0.5,0,0.5).",1,"Locality parameters: game locality g = 0.5 (partially global game), punishment locality p = 0 (local punishment), adaptation locality a = 0.5 (mixed local/global adaptation); other fixed parameters N=100, n=4, b=2, c=1, f=6, s=3, mutation rate μ=0.01.","(g,p,a) values given for panel (g); base model parameters shared.",1,False,"Agent-based simulation, no human participants.",1,False,Not an empirical experiment.,1,False,No lab or field environment.,1,True,Described repeatedly as simulations on a regular graph.,1,False,Behavior explored numerically rather than fully analytically.,1,100,N=100.,1,100,100 generations in transition diagrams.,0.9,1,Same unconditional cooperator/defector framework.,0.8,N/A,No explicit endowment allocation.,1,0.4,Same b and group size.,1,N/A,No communication.,1,N/A,Simulation with no participant interface.,1,N/A,No human identifiers.,1,N/A,Reward absent.,1,N/A,Not shown to any user.,1,1,Local punishment present with p=0.,1,3,Cost s=3 per punishment.,1,6,Fine f=6.,1,0,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,1,Contribution cost c=1.,0.8,N/R,"They state that with g>0 and mixed adaptation, cooperative regimes can collapse or be maintained due to randomness, but give no numeric cooperation rate.",0,N/R,No quantitative contribution data.,0,N/R,No efficiency values reported.,0,N/R,No group payoff data given.,0,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Simulation study only.,1,"Demonstrates that with partially global games (g=0.5) and mixed adaptation (a=0.5), DN colonies tend to grow and global adaptation can either preserve or destroy cooperative regimes, depending on which strategies are imitated.",Summarized from Results discussion of panel (g).,1
