treatments.,0.9,On site,Lab at Maastricht University.,1,"Same Tullock team contest. In Stage 3, each player gets F=50 response tokens and may choose for each teammate either to reward or to punish (cannot both reward and punish the same teammate in the same round). They can reward some and punish others in the same period. Reward: cost 1 to giver, +1 to recipient; Punish: cost 1 to giver, −1 to recipient, with payoffs truncated at zero. Unused response tokens are kept for that round’s payoff but cannot be carried over.",Description of R&P treatment: ability to both reward and punish with exclusion on same person in same round.,1
