.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/R,Endowment not reported.,0.2,N/R,"Only relative statements (e.g., contributions per punishing point about three times higher in PUN&IR than in PUN).",0.2,N/R,No raw average contribution amounts provided.,0.2,N/R,"Fig. 11.4 compares overall efficiency across treatments, but numeric values for PUN alone are not given.",0.3,N/R,No explicit payoff levels reported.,0.2,N/R,Country not specified.,0.2,N/R,Age not mentioned.,0.2,N/R,Gender not discussed.,0.2,N/R,"Likely students, but not stated here.",0.3,On site,Described in context of lab public goods experiments.,0.9,Public goods game with peer punishment but without an attached indirect reciprocity game; used as a control to compare with the PUN&IR treatment that combines punishment and reputation.,"Taken from description of PUN as control “which allowed for punishment, but did not entail an IR game.”",1
