me; no numeric rates.,0.3,N/R,No numeric average contributions are given.,0.2,N/R,"Discussion focuses on wealth levels and ability to cooperate, but no explicit efficiency ratios.",0.3,N/R,No explicit payoffs for no-punishment groups.,0.2,N/R,Country not mentioned.,0.2,N/R,Not described.,0.2,N/R,Not described.,0.2,N/R,Not reported.,0.2,On site,Described as experimental study within typical lab public-good frameworks.,0.9,"Dynamic linear public-good game where each subject receives an initial wealth endowment and plays repeatedly using whatever is on their wealth account. Contribution capabilities depend on own and others’ past contributions; payoffs equal final wealth, not sum of period payoffs. In this treatment, there is no peer punishment mechanism; cooperation fractions decline over time and wealth paths differ from the punishment treatment.",Summarizes dynamic design as described and notes absence of punishment.,1
