ed for mean-field equilibria.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,No human,Theoretical mean-field model without human data.,1,"Mean-field approximation assumes local neighborhood composition equals global averages. Transition probabilities W_{X→Y} computed over all neighbor patterns M (m=35 for n=4) using multinomial probabilities and Fermi rule with noise K. ODE system for x_SC, x_WC, x_D, x_L defined via these W_{X→Y}. Equilibria approximated by minimizing f1^2+f2^2+f3^2+f4^2. For σ=-0.3, small A gives near-all-D, larger A yields coexistence of cooperators and loners with defectors disappearing.","Directly from equations and narrative in Section 2.4, Fig. 5(d–f).",1
