ound contribution amount specified.,0.1,N/R,No reported efficiency measure relative to a benchmark.,0.1,N/R,Figures and text discuss only fractions and exit probabilities.,0.1,N/A,"Simulation only, no human participants.",1,N/A,"Simulation only, no human participants.",1,N/A,"Simulation only, no human participants.",1,N/A,"Simulation only, no human participants.",1,No human,These are Monte Carlo simulations with varied punishment efficiency.,1,"Same spatial PDG with C, D, P on a square lattice and adaptive exit mechanism as in the main model. Aspiration level is fixed at A=0.6; sensitivity γ=0.05; punishment cost α=0.1; punishment fine β is varied to realize different sanction-to-cost ratios β/α. Dilemma strength b is varied, and steady-state fractions of each strategy are recorded to assess how adaptive exit interacts with punishment efficiency to promote cooperation and eliminate second-order free-riding.","Summarizes the subset of simulations where β/α is varied, based on Fig. 4 description.",0.95
