ayoff function making simple inference unclear.,0,N/R,Average payoffs not reported.,0,Germany,Same Hamburg student subject pool.,1,Mean 25.11 years (SD 0.2833) [likely mis-printed SD but reported as such],Group Monitoring Punishment row in Table 2.,0.8,28.33% male,“Male 0.2833 (0.4508)” in Table 2.,1,University students (mean semester 4.983),Semester row for Pun-GM in Table 2.,1,On site,Same lab environment.,1,"Stage 1: C recommends contribution. Stage 2: A, B, C contribute simultaneously. Stage 3: C can punish A and/or B by spending points; each point spent reduces own account by 1 and reduces targeted follower’s account by 3 points. In Group Monitoring, C observes only aggregate contributions via payoff.","Punishment treatment and Group Monitoring descriptions, plus footnote on 3:1 punishment.",1
