nt each round.,1,N/R,"Only token contributions presented; while endowment is known, condition-level normalized rates by SR vs WR are not fully tabulated beyond the means we already use; to avoid mixing, leave as N/R.",0,7.49,"Table 3: compliant SR, Punishment available, excluding cohort 1, mean contributions 7.49 tokens.",0.8,N/R,Net efficiency (considering punishment costs) not reported by sleep condition.,0,N/R,No per-condition payoff statistics.,0,United States,Same subject pool and location.,1,Mean age 19.88 years for compliant SR; range 18–28.,Table 1 Panel A SR compliant stats apply to SR subjects in both treatments.,1,66% female,Same SR compliant gender share (0.66 female).,1,University students.,Same as other conditions.,0.9,On site,Run in the same lab at Appalachian State University.,1,Partners (fixed) groups; 10 rounds. Two-stage per round: contribution then punishment. Each subject can assign up to 10 punishment points total to the two others per round. Each sent point costs $0.10; recipients lose 10% of that round’s earnings per point (losses capped at 100% of earnings; senders’ costs reduced proportionately). Subjects received an initial $5 prior to Round 1 to offset potential negative earnings. Order of Punishment vs No Punishment block was counterbalanced across cohorts.,All these parameters described in punishment design section.,1
