10.1063_5.0215702.md,"Baseline RL PD without punishment (p=0, c=0, ρ=0)","Condition explicitly described as benchmark scenario with no punishment: (p,c)=(0,0) and ρ=0.",1,"Punishment parameters: p=0, c=0, ρ=0; temptation b=0.1; Q-learning RL PD on L×L lattice","Independent variables are punishment intensity p, cost c, punishment probability ρ, with b fixed at 0.1 and lattice size L=100 in baseline description.",0.95,False,"Study is an agent-based evolutionary game model with Q-learning agents, not human participants.",1,False,No controlled human or field experiment; purely computational model.,1,False,No lab environment; simulations only.,1,True,Authors explicitly state they develop an agent-based evolutionary game model and use Q-learning simulations.,1,False,No closed-form analytical model; all results from numerical simulations plus qualitative analysis of Q-tables.,1,10000,"They fix L=100 if not stated otherwise, so N=L×L=100×100=10000 for main results including benchmark.",0.95,10000000,"They state: 'For each round, a transient of at least 10^7 steps is used, and then, we average over another 500 steps'; use 10^7 as effective number of learning rounds before measurement.",0.8,1,"Binary action set A={C,D}; not a continuous contribution game. Coding 1 because players choose full cooperation or full defection, consistent with all-or-nothing interpretation in PD context.",0.9,N/A,"This is a Prisoner’s Dilemma with fixed payoffs, not a public goods contribution with an endowment.",1,N/A,Not a linear public goods game; PD payoffs do not use an MPCR concept.,1,N/A,No human subjects; communication between learning agents is not modeled as chat.,1,N/A,No user interface; agents obtain payoffs locally via game interactions and learning rule.,1,N/A,No identities or UI; lattice neighbors are fixed and anonymous in human sense.,1,N/A,No explicit reward mechanism separate from PD payoffs.,1,N/A,Agents are not given meta-information such as total number of simulation steps.,1,0,"Benchmark case is explicitly 'absence of punishment' with (p,c)=(0,0) and ρ=0.",1,N/A,No punishment in this condition.,1,N/A,No punishment in this condition.,1,0,"No separate prosocial reward mechanism is modeled, only PD payoffs and punishment.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,"PD is modeled via payoff matrix parameters, not via endowments and contributions.",1,0.47,"They report cooperation level f_C≈47% in absence of punishment; interpret cooperation as contributing vs defecting, so normalized rate is 0.47.",0.9,N/R,"Only binary C/D choices, no token amount per se is reported.",0.5,N/R,They do not report average payoffs or efficiency normalized to maximum.,0.5,N/R,No explicit aggregate payoff numbers reported for this condition.,0.5,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Agent-based numerical simulations only.,1,"Prisoner’s Dilemma on 2D L×L lattice with periodic boundary; payoff matrix [[1, -b],[1+b,0]] with b=0.1; each agent interacts with four nearest neighbors plus self-state count; Q-learning with α=0.1, γ=0.9, ε=0.01; synchronous updating; state s_j is number of cooperators in self+neighbors.","Summarized from model description in Section II, including payoff matrix, lattice, neighborhood, and learning parameters used 'if not stated otherwise'.",1
