,1,N/A,Payoffs directly from PD matrix and punishment; no endowment.,1,N/R,"They show f_C as function of p in Fig. 2(a) but provide only curves, not explicit numeric values per p; values cannot be read precisely from text.",0.4,N/R,Binary PD action; no token amount reported.,0.5,N/R,No explicit payoff efficiency values reported across p.,0.5,N/R,Aggregate payoffs are not numerically provided.,0.5,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,All results from agent-based simulations.,1,"Same PD and Q-learning setup as baseline: lattice L=100 with periodic boundaries, four nearest neighbors, states s_j based on number of cooperators in neighborhood including self, α=0.1, γ=0.9, ε=0.01, b=0.1. Punishment: each cooperator who chose C may, with probability ρ=0.2, punish all neighboring defectors, inflicting penalty p on each punished defector and incurring cost c=0.2 per punished defector. Multiple punishers and multiple punished neighbors possible.",Summarized from model description; punishment specifics taken from Section II and Fig. 1 with parameters for this condition.,1
