10.1093_pnasnexus_pgad054.md,Bounded and discretized behavioral space robustness simulations,Robustness simulations examining effects of discrete step size and bounded trait range on norm dynamics.,1,"Behavioral step size (e.g., 1.5) and range (e.g., −12 to 15); strength of similarity-based effects; presence of migration and/or direct effects.","Section states that with parameters from Fig. 1, behavioral space can be discretized with step 1.5 and bounded; also considers larger discrete steps and narrower ranges.",0.8,False,"Numerical simulations, no human subjects.",1,False,Not empirical.,1,False,No lab.,1,True,Described as numerical simulations studying finite and discrete behavioral spaces.,1,False,"Qualitative results from simulations, not closed-form.",1,2,Based on base migration-type model with pairwise interactions.,0.7,N/R,Simulation horizon unspecified.,0.2,1,"Even with discretized steps, many trait levels are possible; not all-or-nothing decisions.",1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,No MPCR.,1,N/A,Simulations only.,1,0,No summaries in design.,1,N/A,No explicit punishment stage.,1,N/A,No explicit reward stage.,1,0,Not shown.,1,0,No punishment actions.,1,N/A,No punishment actions.,1,N/A,No punishment actions.,1,0,No reward actions.,1,N/A,No reward actions.,1,N/A,No reward actions.,1,N/A,No tokens.,1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/A,No contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency not reported.,1,N/R,Group payoff not given.,1,N/A,Simulation.,1,N/A,Simulation.,1,N/A,Simulation.,1,N/A,Simulation.,1,No human,Simulated agents only.,1,"Using parameters as in Fig. 1, a mildly discrete space with step size 1.5 over range [−12,15] yields same equilibrium as continuous infinite space; larger discrete steps can allow similarity-based norm effects to maintain multiple stable equilibria by effectively discretizing payoffs, while narrow trait ranges limit possible evolution and can force equilibrium to differ from external-force optimum, without similarity-based effects determining which equilibrium is reached.",Summarizes discrete-step and bounded-range findings from robustness section.,1
