10.3390_e24091289.md,"Simulation – U=35, full punishment parameter grid",Same simulation system with highest environmental risk parameter U=35; figures give separate panels for this case.,0.94,"Risk threshold U=35; central punishment intensity t1 ∈ [2, 9.5]; peer punishment intensity t2 ∈ [1, 6.5]; other parameters fixed (N=100, n=10, m=10, u=5, w1=2, w=4, w2=1, β=0.1, α=0.05).",U is explicitly set to 35 as one of three risk levels; same t1 and t2 ranges are explored for this higher risk scenario.,0.96,False,Evolutionary simulations involve artificial agents only.,1.0,False,No empirical experimental protocol with human or field data.,1.0,False,Not conducted in a laboratory setting with people.,1.0,True,Authors repeatedly call them 'simulation results' and specify parameter sweeps.,1.0,False,"Results are numerical, not analytical derivations.",0.96,100,Total number of individuals N=100 is constant.,1.0,N/R,Number of rounds/generations is not provided.,0.2,1,Strategy space allows only full collaborator contribution u=5 or zero (defector).,0.9,N/A,No human-controlled endowment allocation; contributions depend on agent strategy.,1.0,N/R,"Payoffs depend on threshold-crossing of contributed sum, not a fixed marginal per capita return.",0.9,N/A,No human communication modeled.,1.0,N/A,Agents do not receive explicit summary displays; they only observe payoffs via the imitation rule.,1.0,N/A,Identities or explicit observability are not part of the model.,1.0,N/A,No rewards are implemented.,1.0,N/A,No interface for agents; number of rounds is not displayed.,1.0,1,Both central and peer punishment remain active mechanisms.,1.0,N/R,Model distinguishes w1=2 and w2=1; schema does not allow encoding both in one numeric.,0.3,N/R,Two distinct punishment intensities t1 and t2; no single punishment magnitude.,0.3,0,No rewarding behavior is defined.,1.0,N/A,No reward channel exists.,1.0,N/A,No rewards implemented.,1.0,10,"Each round, each individual receives m=10 resources.",1.0,N/R,"Out