10.3389_fpsyg.2022.794953.md,Study 2 – SPPG – Intuition punishment decision,Second-party punishment game (recipient punishes proposer) with time-pressured punishment decision.,1,Game type: Second-party punishment game (recipient is direct victim); Decision time: intuition (5 s time pressure).,"Study 2 manipulated partyness between subjects (SPPG vs TPPG) and decision time within subjects; this row is SPPG, intuition condition.",1,True,Human undergraduates made incentivized punishment decisions.,1,True,Random assignment to SPPG vs TPPG; controlled payoff rules and time pressure.,1,True,Classroom setting with detailed instructions and decision sheets.,1,False,No computerized agents.,1,False,Not a purely theoretical treatment.,1,2,SPPG uses a modified dictator game with proposer and recipient; third party absent.,1,1,Described as one-time dictator game with punishment option; no repetition described.,1,1,"Proposer can allocate any amount 0–1,200 to recipient; punishment choice among multiple discrete levels including 0–400; not restricted to pure all-or-nothing for contributions.",0.8,0,"Dictator game: all JPY 1,200 starts with proposer (selfish agent), and JPY 400 starts with recipient; no endowment automatically in a public fund.",0.7,N/R,Not a public goods game; no group multiplier structure reported.,1,0,Participants only interact through instructions and feedback; no communication between proposer and recipient.,0.9,1,"Feedback sheet informed recipient that proposer kept JPY 1,200; provides summary of other’s payoff.",1,0,No indication that identities of punishers are revealed; roles are anonymous in classroom context.,0.7,0,No reward mechanism included.,1,0,Game is one-time; no statement about multiple rounds.,0.9,1,Recipients can pay to deduct from proposer’s payoff.,1,1,Options: pay JPY 100 to deduct JPY 300; cost per 1 token spent is 1.,0.8,3,Deducted amount is three times the amount paid.,1,0,Only punitive deductions are allowed.,1,N/A,No rewards available.,1,N/A,No rewards available.,1,400,Recipients (second parties) are given JPY 400 by the experimenter.,1,N/A,No contribution to a public good; only dictator allocation and punishment.,1,N/A,No voluntary contribution decision by SPPG participants; they are recipients.,1,N/R,No efficiency measure reported for SPPG outcomes.,0,N/R,No aggregate payoff figures reported.,0,Japan,Participants described as Japanese female undergraduates in Study 2.,1,"Mean 19.83, SD 0.71; undergraduates",Explicitly reported for Study 2 participants.,1,All female,Study 2 participants: 46 Japanese female undergraduates.,1,Undergraduate students,Participants were undergraduates recruited from a lecture.,1,On site,Study 2 conducted in a classroom setting.,1,"Modified dictator game with punishment: proposer given JPY 1,200 decides allocation 0–1,200 to recipient; feedback (fake) states proposer kept JPY 1,200. Recipient (second party) is given JPY 400 and can pay 0–400 in steps of 100 JPY to deduct 0–1,200 (3× cost) from proposer. Intuition punishment decision under 5 s time pressure. Mean amount deducted from proposer’s payoff for SPPG participants in intuition condition was JPY 782.61.",Summarized directly from Study 2 SPPG procedure and results.,1
