ation only.,1,N/A,Simulation only.,1,N/A,Simulation only.,1,No human,Theoretical stability analysis via simulation.,1,"Under Heckathorn base parameters (N=10, Sc=75, Si=150, K1=100, K2=K3=3, E2=E3=0.2, accelerating production), evaluates for each intermediate M (0.30–0.65) how many simultaneous cooperators at level 1 or level 2 are needed to move from full-defection to high-compliance equilibrium, and how many simultaneous defectors are needed to move from high-compliance back to full defection. Table 2 shows that as M increases, full defection equilibrium becomes more stable and high-compliance equilibrium less stable.",Summarizes specific focus on stability and needed deviations reported in Table 2.,0.98
