ically detailed in this section.,0.6,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,N/A,No human agents.,1,No human,Theoretical cost-minimization analysis based on simulation outputs and analytical cost function.,1,"Uses same group control simulation with N=10, costs K1=100, K2=K3=3, E2=E3=0.2, and derived cost function C=[N−M(N−G)]Si+N(1−M)^{N−G}Sc, where G is expected number of compliers. Compares expected cost for achieving full compliance using only individual sanctions at M=0.5 (C=2000) vs M=0.1 (C=10000), and for achieving moderate compliance using only collective sanctions at M=0.1 (Sc≈85, C≈655.64, G≈7.5) vs M=0.5 (Sc=65, C≈256.38, G≈8.7) assuming sufficient initial cooperation to reach high-compliance equilibrium at M=0.5.",Summarizes analytical focus on agent’s cost trade-offs across monitoring efficacies and sanction types.,0.98
