' in Table 2 panel A.,1,N/R,Final group payoffs including effects of punishment are not normalized or reported.,0,N/R,Panel B shows group contributions (26.06173) but not net monetary payoffs after punishment.,0.3,Ethiopia,Same AAWSA employee sample.,1,Mean 37 years; detailed distribution not provided.,From Table 1.,0.9,"Approximately 81.6% male, 18.4% female.",From Table 1 panel A.,1,"Mixed; 16.1% primary, 20.4% secondary, 38.5% technical diploma, 24.1% first degree and above.",Same participants across conditions.,1,On site,Conducted in AAWSA training facility.,1,"Standard linear public good with five players and 10-token endowment, plus a randomly and anonymously selected monitor. Monitor is informed of role only after all contribution decisions and the post-experimental questionnaire, sees anonymous contribution amounts of group members, and can choose to punish one or more players, paying 1 token per punished player which reduces that player’s payoff by 3 tokens. Monitors receive a fixed 10-token payment for the role.",Described in 'Public good game with monitor' section and monitor behavior section.,1
