vestment without punishment: 6.693 credits.,1,N/R,No ratio of actual to maximum group payoff reported.,0.1,N/R,No aggregate payoff values reported.,0.1,Germany,"Participants recruited at Julius-Maximilians-University of Würzburg, Germany.",0.9,"Mean 27.57 years (SD = 9.33), all at least 18 years old.",Reported in Participants section.,1,79.44% female (85 of 107); remaining approximately 20.56% other genders (not further specified).,Reported number and percentage of female participants.,0.9,Primarily university students; recruited through local advertisements and could receive course credit.,Mention of course credits and university lab suggests mainly university students; exact breakdown not reported.,0.6,On site,Participants invited to the lab and tested on desktop monitors.,1,"Repeated one-shot linear public goods game with 4 players (1 real, 3 fictitious). Contribution range 0–20, integer credits. Pool multiplied by 0.4 and equally redistributed; fictitious others’ contributions follow 10 fairness profiles (Table 4). No punishment or reward is possible in this block. 50 trials, preceded by 5 practice trials.",Summarizes procedural and structural details specific to this block from Paradigm and Calculation of the credits sections.,1
