udents; no precise ages provided.,0.6,N/R,Gender composition not tabulated.,0,University students at Kansai University,Explicitly described as students at Kansai University.,1,On site,Face-to-face lab experiment.,1,"Same finitely repeated linear PGG as other main treatments: group size 5, MPCR 0.4, partner matching, 4 initial periods without sanctions; in Part 2, subjects perform depletion version of crossing-out-letters task before Phase 2 and a flashing, incongruent-color Stroop task in each period to maintain depleted self-regulatory resources; no sanction schemes available.",Summarizes key structural and depletion features unique to this condition.,1
10.1016_j.jebo.2024.04.016.md,Voting-N – FS scheme with deterrent sanction rates,"Subset of Voting, No Depletion treatment when groups choose FS and enact deterrent sanction rates (0.8 or 1.2).",0.9,Self-regulatory resources: Not depleted; Institutional choice: Voting allowed; Selected scheme: FS; Sanction rate: Deterrent (0.8 or 1.2),Condition-level unit defined by majority vote for FS and subsequent median vote implementing deterrent rates.,0.95,True,Human subjects in lab choosing institutions and sanction rates.,1,True,Randomized assignment to depletion/voting; institutional choices determined endogenously.,1,True,Run in on-site lab with zTree.,1,False,No artificial agents.,1,False,"This observation set is behavioral, not theoretical.",1,5,PGG group size fixed at 5.,1,28,4 periods Part 1 plus 24 in Part 2; FS may be active in some subset of the 24 but horizon is 28.,1,1,Contributions can be any integer 0–20.,1,0,Endowment fully in private account at start of each period.,1,0.4,r=0.4 in payoff equation.,1,0,No communication channel mentioned.,0.9,1,"Subjects see each member’s contribution in IS; under FS they need to know fines and payoffs, implying group-level feedback.",0.7,0,"Under FS punishments are centralized fines implied by the rule, not peer-target choice; individual identities of who caused fines are not relevant; no evidence of identity revelation.",0.7,0,No rewards used.,1,1,"Design describes multi-phase finite horizon, typically known to subjects.",0.7,1,FS is a formal sanctioning institution that penalizes allocations to private account.,1,1,"For each point lost by a fined member, every group member incurs cost 1/11; total variable cost to punishers is 4*(1/11)=4/11 when target loses 1 point, so cost per 1-point fine to all four punishers = 4/11; but the primitive per-capita admin cost per punished point is 1/11. Using 1 as the cost parameter to punished vs punishers ratio is ambiguous; better to use marginal cost to punishers per 1 point fine = 4/11