10.1098_rsos.230830.md,Baseline model (no sanctions),Paper defines a baseline system without sanctions in section 2 and compares it to two sanction systems.,1,"Sanction system type = none (baseline); network structure, costs x_k, losses g_k, benefits b_k treated as parameters.",Independent manipulation is presence/type of sanction system; baseline corresponds to no sanctions.,1,False,Model is purely theoretical using replicator equations and tree graphs; no human subjects.,1,False,No controlled empirical experiment; only mathematical analysis and numerical simulations.,1,False,No laboratory setting; analytical model.,1,True,Uses numerical simulations of replicator dynamics on networks plus analytical derivations.,1,True,Core of study is derivation and stability analysis of replicator equations for asymmetric games.,1,1,Each node has a continuum/infinite group but replicator is at group level; treat as one strategic entity per group.,0.3,1,"Evolutionary replicator dynamics over continuous time, not discrete rounds; approximate as single repeated interaction structure.",0.2,1,Players choose between two pure strategies: cooperate or defect; no partial contribution.,1,N/A,No endowment or contribution stage as in public goods games; purely cooperate/defect on task.,1,N/R,Not a public goods game; no marginal per capita return defined.,1,N/A,No human participants or communication module.,1,0,Model does not include information feedback about others’ payoffs or actions beyond payoff structure.,1,0,No punishment mechanism in baseline.,1,0,No reward mechanism modeled.,1,0,No explicit rounds known to agents; continuous-time evolutionary dynamics.,1,0,Baseline system explicitly defined as without sanctions/punishment.,1,N/A,No punishment option.,1,N/A,No punishment option.,1,0,"No positive reward system modeled; only costs, benefits, and losses.",1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No reward mechanism.,1,N/R,"Model uses benefits b_k, costs x_k, losses g_k but no endowment is defined.",1,N/R,"They track frequencies of cooperators per group, not normalized contribution from an endowment.",0.3,N/R,No token contributions; only binary strategy and resulting payoffs.,1,N/R,"They discuss stability of equilibria and coexistence, not aggregate efficiency ratios.",1,N/R,Payoff formulas given symbolically but no single reported aggregate payoff outcome.,0.5,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Purely mathematical and computational modeling.,1,"Division-of-labour game on directed tree graph with infinite populations per node; players chosen randomly in each group either cooperate (pay cost x_k, pass task, generate benefits b_k) or defect (receive benefit from upstream, pay no cost, stop task) causing system-wide losses g_k distributed along branches. Dynamics given by replicator equations for asymmetric games.",Summary of formal model assumptions described in sections 2.1–2.2.,1
