10.1371_journal.pone.0307832.md,"CNN – Communication with penalties in Phase 1, no communication/penalties in Phases 2–3","Condition label and sequence taken from Table 1: CNN (Comm (Pen), then N/A, N/A) described as 'Communication followed by no communication'.",1,Initial regulatory environment: lax enforcement (communication with peer sanctioning) in Phase 1 without facilitation; no communication or penalties in Phases 2–3.,"CNN differs from other treatments by timing/availability of communication, peer sanctioning, and lack of facilitation across three phases.",1,True,Uses undergraduate human participants in a lab resource dilemma.,1,True,Random assignment of groups to six treatments with controlled manipulations.,1,True,Conducted in a networked computer lab with private cubicles.,1,False,"Although they use a computerised task, primary data come from human decisions, not agent-only simulations.",1,False,No formal closed-form or purely mathematical model is analyzed as a standalone study.,1,4,Participants were randomly assigned to four-person groups; Player Numbers 1–4.,1,9,Experiment consisted of 9 rounds divided into 3 phases of 3 rounds each.,1,1,Real-time foraging: participants can move and harvest any number of tokens; no evidence of binary all-or-nothing choice.,0.9,0,"Common-pool extraction game; no initial endowment placed in a public account. Players harvest from shared field, not contribute to it.",0.9,N/R,No linear public-goods style multiplier or marginal per capita return is defined; payoffs are per token.,1,1,CNN Phase 1: 'Comm (Pen)'; communication via chat before and during rounds.,1,1,Sanctions and each player’s in-round total harvest were visible to all ('visible to all participants'; harvest totals shown top right).,0.9,1,Sanctioning via player number keys (1–4) with penalties visible to all implies targeted identity is known by Player Number.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism is described.,1,1,"Standard in this foraging paradigm; although not explicitl