ishment in CP_0,60 as 60.20 ECUs.",1,Spain,Sessions run at University of Valencia lab in Spain.,0.95,Undergraduate students; exact age distribution N/R,Subjects described as undergraduate students.,0.8,Mixed; exact gender proportions N/R,Gender collected but only used as control; no breakdown given.,0.8,Undergraduate university students,Stated that subjects were undergraduate students with no similar-experiment experience.,1,On site,Laboratory sessions at LINEEX using z-Tree.,1,"Same team investment game structure: two investors, one allocator; binary investment with cost 5 ECUs; 30 ECU surplus if both invest; allocator chooses x∈[0,30] to split equally; partners matching over 15 periods; strategy method for allocator choices. Punishment effective only if both investors punish; allocator payoff multiplied by 0.4 when λ2=0.60.",Summarizes game plus specific coordinated punishment rule for this treatment.,1
10.1007_s11238-024-09977-9.md,"CP_0,80 (Coordinated punishment, 80%)","One of the four between-subjects treatments; coordinated punishment with λ1=0, λ2=0.80 (increasing returns to scale).",1,"Punishment institution: coordinated punishment with λ0=0, λ1=0, λ2=0.80 (CP_0,80).",Treatment varies punishment technology; this is the high-intensity coordinated punishment condition.,1,True,Human-subject laboratory experiment.,1,True,Controlled between-subjects experimental design.,1,True,Conducted at LINEEX lab.,1,False,No simulation-only study.,1,False,Row corresponds to experimental treatment with human subjects.,1,3,Two investors and one allocator in each trio.,1,15,Same 15-period partners-matching design used for all treatments.,1,0,"Investment choice is binary, but allocator’s return is continuous on [0,30].",0.7,0,20 ECU endowment per player; investment paid only upon investing.,1,N/R,Investment game structure without defined marginal per capita return.,0,0,No chat or communication described; only informational feedback screens.,0.9,1,"End-of-period feedback shows each investor’s decisions, amount returned, and punishment choices.",1,1,Punishment decisions per investor in each group are displayed.,0.9,0,No reward option exists.,1,1,Finite 15-period game; standard to inform participants about number of periods.,0.6,1,Stage 3 punishment is present when both investors invested.,1,5,Punishment decision has individual cost of 5 ECUs across punishment treatments.,1,0.8,Allocator payoffs reduced by 80% if both investors punish (λ2=0.80); λ1=0.,0.9,0,No reward mechanism is available.,1,N/A,Rewards not implemented.,1,N/A,Rewards not implemented.,1,20,Players in all treatments start with 20 ECUs.,1,N/R,Reported as likelihood of joint investment (42%) rather than normalized contribution fraction.,0.3,N/R,No average ECUs invested reported beyond binary choice frequencies.,0.2,N/R,They provide average total payoffs but not a normalized efficiency measure.,0.3,60.05,"Result 5: fina