okens for each profile; starting per-round endowment not specified.,0.2,0.46,Average first-round cooperation rate with a fine is 46% (“average cooperation rate jumps … to 46% with a fine”).,1,N/R,Only binary C/D decisions recorded; no contribution level in tokens defined.,1,N/R,No efficiency or surplus ratio is reported.,0,N/R,Aggregate or average group payoffs by condition are not given.,0,France,Same subject pool and location as no-fine condition.,0.9,N/R,Age was collected but not summarized in the article.,0,N/R,Gender distribution not reported.,0,Mainly university students; some university employees,"Identical pool: 85% students, 15% employees.",1,On site,Same lab sessions at Ecole Polytechnique.,1,"Indefinitely repeated 2-player prisoner’s dilemma with random continuation δ=0.75; quasi-stranger rematching. Fine F=10 subtracted from all outcomes where the player defects: (C,D)=12,60−F; (D,C)=60−F,12; (D,D)=35−F,35−F. Stage game is designed to be isomorphic to Dal Bó and Fréchette (2011) treatment {δ=3/4; R=40}. First-round decisions are used as outcome variable.","From Sect. 2.1, Table 1b, and surrounding description.",1
