y reward mechanism beyond normal payoffs.,1,N/A,No reward technology.,1,N/A,No reward technology.,1,N/R,"Payoff matrices give profits for each action profile, but no per-round token endowment is specified.",0.5,N/R,"Outcomes reported as cooperation rates (choosing B or Z), not normalized contributions.",1,N/R,No contribution amounts; only discrete action choices and earnings.,1,N/R,"Paper reports cooperation frequencies and payoffs, not normalized efficiency relative to maximum.",0.6,N/R,"Only average individual payoff by treatment is reported (e.g., 67.9 for N0); group payoff per round is not directly stated.",0.7,USA,"Experiment conducted at Missouri State University, Springfield, Missouri, USA.",1,Undergraduate students; exact age distribution N/R,Subjects described as undergraduate students; no ages given.,0.9,N/R,No information on gender composition.,1,Undergraduate students at Missouri State University,Explicitly stated that subjects were undergraduate students.,1,On site,Conducted in a university lab using ORSEE recruitment and oTree; no indication of remote participation.,0.95,Three-player two-period Bertrand game with actions A/B in Period 1 and Y/Z in Period 2; repeated for 16 rounds with random rematching and pay-one-round payment (8 points = $1; plus $5 show-up). No communication stage in N0.,Summarizes structural details specific to N0 condition and general game not captured by other fields.,1
