10.1103_PhysRevE.110.034301.md,"Analytical-simulation condition: moderate growth, monostable interior equilibrium (r = 0.7, w = 0.999, δ = 0.05)",Fig. 2(b) parameter set showing a stable interior equilibrium with coexistence of cooperators and defectors under moderate growth.,1,Resource growth rate r = 0.7; w = 0.999; δ = 0.05; N = 1000; R_m = 1000; b_m = 0.5; α = 0.5,Explicit parameters given for Fig. 2(b).,1,False,No human data.,1,False,Not an experiment with participants.,1,False,Theoretical work.,1,True,Phase plane trajectories numerically simulated for these parameters.,1,True,Interior equilibria existence and stability analyzed generally.,1,1000,N = 1000.,1,0,Continuous time.,0.9,1,Binary C/D choice.,0.9,N/A,No public goods contribution.,1,N/R,No MPCR.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No UI.,1,N/A,Identity not modeled.,1,N/A,Identity not modeled.,1,0,Not round-based.,1,1,Tax-punishment part is active as 1−w > 0.,1,1,Punishment intensity 1.,0.9,1,Intensity 1.,0.9,1,w ~ 0.999 meaning almost all budget to reward.,1,1,Redistribution with unit effect.,0.8,1,Each unit tax increases payoff by one.,0.8,N/R,Not specified.,1,N/R,"Outcome variable is equilibrium x*, not contribution rate.",1,N/R,No contribution decisions.,1,N/R,No efficiency index reported.,1,N/R,No aggregate payoff numbers.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Model only.,1,"Shows a monostable interior equilibrium where both C and D coexist and resources are maintained, under high reward allocation (w≈1) and moderate resource growth.",Captures qualitative finding associated with this condition.,1
10.1103_PhysRevE.110.034301.md,"Analytical-simulation condition: moderate growth, bistability with boundary+interior equilibria (r = 0.6, w = 0.1, δ = 0.004)",Fig. 2(c) parameter set for moderate resource growth with two stable equilibria (boundary and interior).,1,Resource growth rate r = 0.6; w = 0.1; δ = 0.004; N = 1000; R_m = 1000; b_m = 0.5; α = 0.5,Explicit in caption of Fig. 2(c).,1,False,No human data.,1,False,Not an empirical experiment.,1,False,Theoretical study.,1,True,Phase diagrams numerically computed.,1,True,Falls within analytically characterized moderate-r regime.,1,1000,N = 1000.,1,0,Continuous-time ODE.,0.9,1,C/D strategy choice.,0.9,N/A,No contribution-endowment framing.,1,N/R,Not a linear public good.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No interface specification.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,Continuous model.,1,1,w=0.1 leaves 0.9 share for punishment.,1,1,Punishment intensity 1.,0.9,1,Intensity 1.,0.9,1,w>0.,1,1,Redistribution cost per unit equals reward.,0.8,1,Unit tax gives unit payoff.,0.8,N/R,No endowment parameter.,1,N/R,x is cooperation frequency; contributions not defined.,1,N/R,No contributions.,1,N/R,Outcome described qualitatively via coexistence and sustainability.,1,N/R,No numeric payoffs.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Theoretical ODE study.,1,"Shows bistability: depending on initial conditions, trajectories converge either to full cooperation with sustainable resources (right boundary) or to an interior equilibrium with partial cooperation and resource maintenance, under low reward weight (w=0.1) and small δ.",Summarizes dynamic nature of this parameter condition.,1
