10.1103_PhysRevE.110.034301.md,"Analytical-simulation sweep: varying w with moderate growth (r = 0.7, δ = 0.04)","Fig. 3(a)-(d) use r=0.7, δ=0.04 and vary w (0, 0.95, 1) to analyze effect of reward-punishment allocation under moderate growth.",0.95,"Resource growth rate r = 0.7; per capita incentive δ = 0.04; allocation weight w ∈ {0, 0.95, 1}; N = 1000; R_m = 1000; b_m = 0.5; α = 0.5","Parameters for Fig. 3(a)-(d) given as N=1000, R_m=1000, b_m=0.5, δ=0.04, α=0.5, r=0.7; separate panels change w (0, 0.95, 1). They share qualitative analysis; grouped here as a sweep condition.",0.95,False,Simulation and analytical study.,1,False,No participants.,1,False,Not a lab environment.,1,True,Phase diagrams and attraction basins numerically computed for different w.,1,True,Analytical conditions for stability of equilibria used alongside simulations.,1,1000,N fixed at 1000.,1,0,Continuous-time evolution.,0.9,1,C/D strategy space.,0.9,N/A,No endowment structure.,1,N/R,Not defined.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No interface.,1,N/A,Identities not present.,1,N/A,Identities not present.,1,0,ODE dynamics.,1,1,"For w<1, punishment present; at w=1, punishment vanishes but sweep includes both; overall condition includes punishment in some cases.",0.9,1,Intensity defined as 1.,0.9,1,Unit cost equals unit fine.,0.9,1,"Reward exists for all w>0, including pure reward (w=1).",1,1,Tax redistribution.,0.8,1,Unit tax to unit reward.,0.8,N/R,No endowment given.,1,N/R,"Outcomes measured as attraction basin of full cooperation equilibrium, not contributions.",1,N/R,No contributions.,1,N/R,Efficiency not explicitly calculated.,1,N/R,No aggregate payoff numbers.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,No human,Model-based sweep.,1,"Compares pure punishment (w=0), mixed reward-punishment (e.g., w=0.5, 0.95), and pure reward (w=1) regarding stability and attraction basin of full-cooperation equilibrium under moderate resource growth; shows that excessive reward (w close to 1) reduces the basin of attraction for full cooperation.",Reflects main qualitative conclusion from varying w at moderate r.,1
10.1103_PhysRevE.110.034301.md,"Analytical-simulation sweep: varying δ with moderate growth (r = 0.7, w = 0.5)",Fig. 3(e)-(h) study effect of varying δ at fixed r=0.7 and w=0.5 on dynamics and attraction basin.,0.95,"Resource growth rate r = 0.7; allocation weight w = 0.5; per capita incentive δ varied (small, medium, large) as in Fig. 3(e)-(g); N = 1000; R_m = 1000; b_m = 0.5; α = 0.5","Caption states N=1000, R_m=1000, b_m=0.5, w=0.5, α=0.5, r=0.7 and varying δ for panels (e)-(h); individual δ values not all numerically specified but relative comparisons are.",0.8,False,Numerical and analytical.,1,False,No participants.,1,False,Model only.,1,True,Phase diagrams and attraction basins simulated for different δ.,1,True,General conditions involve δ; sweep interprets them.,1,1000,Fixed N.,1,0,Continuous-time evolution.,0.9,1,C/D strategies.,0.9,N/A,No contribution amounts.,1,N/R,Not applicable.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,Not described.,1,N/A,No agents with identity.,1,N/A,No identities.,1,0,No discrete rounds.,1,1,w=0.5 implies both reward and punishment present.,1,1,Punishment intensity 1.,0.9,1,Unit effectiveness.,0.9,1,w>0.,1,1,Tax redistributed.,0.8,1,Each unit yields one payoff unit.,0.8,N/R,Not defined.,1,N/R,"Outcomes tracked via x and attraction basin, not contributions.",1,N/R,No contributions.,1,N/R,Not reported.,1,N/R,No numerical group payoff.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Simulation sweep.,1,"Shows how increasing δ (per capita incentive) enlarges the attraction basin of full-cooperation equilibrium in the moderate-growth regime with balanced reward and punishment; small δ yields interior equilibrium near low cooperation and resource, higher δ induces bistability then monostability at full cooperation.",Summarizes qualitative results across δ values.,1
