10.3390_g12020050.md,Generalized exchange – Baseline (no punishment),Condition labeled 'GENERALIZED EXCHANGE | BASELINE' in Table 1 and described as generalized exchange system without a punishment stage.,1,"Network structure: Generalized exchange (circular chain); Punishment regime: None (baseline, no second-stage decision)",Baseline cell of the 2×3 design for generalized exchange structure.,1,True,Human participants in lab setting.,1,True,Part of the randomized laboratory experiment.,1,True,Implemented at VCEE labs.,1,False,No simulations described.,1,False,Not a purely analytical study.,1,4,Circular network of four players in generalized exchange.,1,16,Game repeated 16 periods in all treatments.,1,0,Binary decision: send social benefits (cooperate) or keep private benefits (defect).,1,0,Each participant chooses whether to send benefits (10 MU) or keep 3 MU privately; default is keeping private benefit.,0.8,10,"As in public good, 3 MU private payoff sacrificed yields 10 MU benefit to a single recipient (total social benefit); using total social return per unit sacrificed.",0.4,0,No communication or chat is mentioned.,1,1,Participants are informed about the decision of their sender each period and the resulting income; this is summary information about relevant others.,0.7,0,No punishment option in baseline generalized exchange.,1,0,No reward in any treatment.,1,0,Participants are not told the exact number of periods.,0.9,0,Baseline treatment without second-stage punishment.,1,N/A,No punishment regime.,1,N/A,No punishment regime.,1,0,No separate reward mechanism is described.,1,N/A,No positive rewards.,1,N/A,No positive rewards.,1,3,"In each round, a player can keep 3 MU or sacrifice it to send 10 MU to the recipient, identical to other treatments.",0.8,0.59,Table 1: COOPERATION for GENERALIZED EXCHANGE BASELINE is 0.59.,1,N/R,Only fraction of cooperation is provided; no raw MU sent is tabulated.,0,N/R,Efficiency not reported and exact reconstruction requires full action distributions.,0,28.64,Average earnings per period are 7.16 MU per player (Table 1). Group payoff ≈ 4 × 7.16 = 28.64 MU.,0.8,Austria,"Lab located in Vienna, Austria.",0.8,Mostly 20–27 years,Same sample across treatments.,0.9,57% female,Overall participant gender share applies.,0.9,Undergraduate students in various disciplines,Described for the whole sample.,1,On site,Sessions at the VCEE lab.,1,"Repeated 4-player indirect helping game on a circular network: each player sends benefits to one recipient and receives benefits from one sender. Positions and identifiers are randomly reshuffled each period so that the specific sender/recipient changes. Player’s period income is 10 MU if sender cooperated plus 3 MU if they defected (0 if they cooperated), with possible range 0–13 MU.",Summarizes generalized exchange structure without punishment from Section 3.2.,1
10.3390_g12020050.md,Generalized exchange – Costly punishment (2;1),Condition labeled 'PUNISHMENT (COSTLY)' under 'GENERALIZED EXCHANGE' in Table 1 and described under punishment manipulations.,1,"Network structure: Generalized exchange (circular chain); Punishment regime: Costly peer punishment (penalty 2 MU, cost 1 MU) limited to immediate neighbors",Punishment regime (2;1) is applied within the generalized exchange structure; punishment constrained to sender/recipient dyad.,1,True,Human subjects in lab.,1,True,Part of the controlled 2×3 experimental design.,1,True,Conducted at VCEE.,1,False,No non-human simulations.,1,False,Not an analytical model.,1,4,Groups of four in a circular exchange network.,1,16,Same number of periods as other treatments.,1,0,Binary cooperation versus defection choice.,1,0,Same basic exchange payoffs as generalized exchange baseline.,0.8,10,Same 10 MU social benefit per cooperative act to single recipient; 3 MU private sacrificed.,0.4,0,No communication tools described.,1,1,Participants learn about the decision of their sender and resulting payoffs and any punishment affecting them.,0.7,1,Punishment is restricted to sender-recipient; the punished player can infer which neighbor punished them; IDs for interaction partners are shown each period.,0.7,0,No reward option implemented.,1,0,Number of repetitions not disclosed.,0.9,1,Second-stage costly punishment decision with regime (2;1).,1,1,Costly punishment regime (2;1) has cost c = 1 MU per punishment.,1,2,Punishment regime (2;1): each unit of punishment reduces target’s payoff by 2 MU.,1,0,No reward scheme is used.,1,N/A,No positive rewards.,1,N/A,No positive rewards.,1,3,"Each round, a player can keep 3 MU or forgo it to provide 10 MU to their recipient, identical to other generalized exchange treatments.",0.8,0.66,Table 1: COOPERATION for GENERALIZED EXCHANGE PUNISHMENT (COSTLY) is 0.66.,1,N/R,Raw contribution amounts not provided.,0,N/R,Efficiency not reported; cannot be reconstructed e