ctly, not experimenter-provided summaries.",0.95,0,No explicit punishment stage or identity revelation mechanism is part of the design.,0.95,0,No explicit rewarding mechanism administered by experimenters.,0.95,0,Animals are not informed about number of trials/rounds.,0.98,0,"Design focuses on cooperative cleaning vs cheating (mucus eating), not on an explicit punishment action by a player.",0.9,N/A,No punishment option implemented.,1,N/A,No punishment option implemented.,1,0,"No separate costly rewarding action; the 'reward' is simply mutualistic benefits, not a selectable experimental mechanism.",0.9,N/A,No explicit reward mechanism implemented.,1,N/A,No explicit reward mechanism implemented.,1,N/R,No notion of experimental token/point endowment is reported.,0,N/R,"They measured percentage of ingested ectoparasites vs mucus, but exact numeric values or normalized rates are not reported in this text.",0.3,N/R,Exact counts/amounts of ectoparasites eaten are not given.,0.0,N/R,No explicit measure of efficiency relative to a theoretical maximum payoff is reported.,0.0,N/R,No aggregate payoff measure is reported in this summary.,0.0,N/R,Field site or lab location for Bshary & Grutter (2006) is not specified in the provided text.,0.0,N/R,Age of fish not discussed.,0.0,N/R,Sex of fish not reported.,0.0,N/R,Not applicable to non-human animals; schema requires string so marked as not reported.,0.0,On site,Described as an experiment on cleaner fish mutualism; likely conducted in controlled aquatic facilities associated with a research station rather than as a broad uncontrolled field observation.,0.55,Biological mutualism experiment with cleaner wrasse (Labroides dimidiatus) measuring cooperative cleaning (ectoparasite consumption) versus cheating (mucus feeding) as a function of being observed by a potential client; interpreted as a test of indirect reciprocity via image scoring.,"Summarizes the cooperative structure, behaviors, and theoretical framing in terms of indirect