ive vs defector receiver strategies, not normalized contribution rates.",1,N/R,"No explicit numerical donation amounts beyond cost d and benefit a,b.",1,N/R,No direct reporting of efficiency metrics.,1,N/R,Global payoffs not summarized numerically; only evolutionary outcomes displayed.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,N/A,No human subjects.,1,No human,Purely computational evolutionary model.,1,"Same repeated Sir Philip Sidney game and replicator dynamics as baseline. Additional mechanism: if a healthy sender falsely signals need and the receiver detects the lie with probability e=0.9, a receiver of type P can pay cost c=0.1 to impose loss l=0.2 on the liar and will not donate in that interaction. Sender strategies: Honest (H) vs Liar (L). Receiver strategies: Reciprocator (R, TFT donation, no punishment), Punisher (P, TFT plus punishment for detected lies), Defector (D, ignores signals and never donates). Simulations: discrete-time replicator dynamics, 3000 periods, 500 independent runs per (T,a) parameter pair; outcome measures are average end proportions of H, P, D across runs.",Synthesized from main text around Fig. 3d–f.,0.97
