me EconLab setting.,1,"All subjects have Type A production function. Participants are randomly allocated into two color groups (yellow or red) that have no payoff consequences. Color serves only to create minimal in-group vs out-group identities. Otherwise, the game matches MAIN: in each period players allocate 10 tokens between production and theft, observe an information table and then vote on excluding others for one period via majority rule.","Section 3.2 describes MIA as minimal groups with Type A production, random color assignment and same exclusion institution as MAIN.",1
