10.3390_math10152823.md,"Simulation – Negative feedback punishment approach with exponential form g(x,k)=k×e^{-x}","Appendix A.3 uses g(x,k)=k×e^{-x} as an alternative negative feedback form and reports group performance in Figure A1a.",1,"Punishment method = negative feedback with exponential form g(x,k)=k×e^{-x}; punishment intention k varied in [0,1]; punishment intensity t^(p) updated each round based on x=f_c^(p).","Appendix A.3: 'We apply two representative functions, the exponential function and the linear function, as different negative correlation expressions... g(x,k)=k×e^{-x}'.",1,False,"Appendix describes simulations, not experiments with humans.",1,False,Simulation study.,1,False,No lab environment.,1,True,Explicitly part of numerical comparison in Appendix A.3.,1,False,"Although accompanied by theory, this row refers to simulation results of that function.",1,100,Appendix A.3 states it uses same simulation environment as earlier figures; base environment has n=100.,0.9,300,Assumed same 300 rounds per k as base simulation; not re-specified but implied.,0.7,1,Same binary C/D contributions.,0.4,0,Same initial endowment and investment rules.,0.8,0.03,Same μ and n.,1,N/A,No humans.,1,0,No explicit summaries reported.,0.6,N/A,No identities in simulation.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,0,Agents not informed of total rounds.,0.6,1,"Pool punishment with intensity g(x,k) is applied.",1,N/R,Institution costs not modeled.,1,N/R,Specific mapping from t^(p) to loss is as in base model but not re-stated.,0.5,0,No reward mechanism.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,N/A,No rewards.,1,5,Same R=5 as base simulation.,1,N/R,Appendix A.3 reports only punishment intensity and cooperation proportion qualitatively.,0.2,N/R,No numeric contribution amounts reported.,0.2,N/R,No efficiency metric described.,0.2,N/R,Group payoff not provided.,0.2,N/A,Simulation only.,1,N/A,Simulation only.,1,N/A,Simulation only.,1,N/A,Simulation only.,1,No human,Agent-based simulation.,1,"Same PGG with pool punishment base. The negative feedback function is g(x,k)=k×e^{-x}, with x the current cooperation proportion. Appendix A.3 notes that this yields stable, continuously changing cooperation similar to baseline g(x,k)=k×5^{-x}.",From Appendix A.3 and Figure A1a.,0.9
