,"Average contribution in this phase for Monetary Punishment groups is 21.48 tokens (Table 2) out of 40 possible group average? Table 2 reports per group average; but individual endowment is 20. Interpreting 21.48 as group average of 4 players (sum) is impossible because max would be 80. More consistent: 21.48 is average of 4 individual contributions (0–20). So normalized rate = 21.48/20 ≈ 1.074, which is impossible. Therefore 21.48 must be sum per group; max sum=80, so rate=21.48/80≈0.2685. However, abstract earlier: 'On average, subjects contribute a total of 40% of their endowment.' For Pre-policy Monetary Punishment, group average 21.48 out of max 80 = 0.2685 ~ 27%. To avoid over-interpretation, set N/R.",0,21.48,Table 2: 'Monetary Punishment – Pre-policy' mean group average contribution is 21.48 tokens.,0.7,N/R,No explicit report of group payoff relative to maximum in this phase; cannot reconstruct from aggregates.,0,N/R,Only contributions are reported; no aggregate payoffs per group/phase.,0,France,Experiment conducted at University of Strasbourg (France); subjects are drawn from that pool.,0.9,"Mean 21 (SD 3.31), typical university students",Reported average age of 21 with standard deviation 3.31.,1,53% female,Reported share of female subjects.,1,University students; 32% studying economics or business management,Subjects recruited from university subject pool; 32% in economics or business management.,1,On site,Conducted in a physical laboratory (LEES) with subjects at computers.,1,Linear public goods game with fixed groups of 4; no incentives; feedback on anonymous ordered contributions; 30 total periods but first 5 belong to this phase.,Summary of structure described under main task and phases.,1
