icipants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,N/A,No human participants.,1,No human,Simulation.,1,"Two subpopulations (‘poor’ and ‘rich’) with different payoff matrices: poor see the interaction as a Prisoners’ Dilemma, rich as an Altruists’ Dilemma (Table 3). Replicator dynamics use reference-group averages within each subgroup. With 50/50 composition and balanced costs, DC becomes dominant among poor, DO among rich (do), yielding intermediate solidarity with the poor and negligible solidarity among/with the rich.",Summarizes description and Figure 5 narrative.,0.93
